<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0285e9ffa3c04bd3020ff5ecb9df9fd643df30fc4f9ea278b98e2c3053548d6b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Tondo: A nude, ithyphallic, balding, bearded satyr, leans
      profile to the right, toward a woman who runs to the right, but turns her head profile to the
      left, to look at the satyr. She wears a short himation over a medium-sleeved chiton, while a
      sakkos covers her hair, and carries a kantharos in her right hand, and a thyrsos in her left
      hand.</P><P>Side A: A youth, standing in a frontal pose, leaning on a staff under
      his left arm, and wearing a himation, turns his head profile to the right, and thrusts the
      palm of his hand, shown in a rare frontal pose, out towards the viewer; to his right stands
      another youth, dressed in Thracian boots (embades), a chitoniskos belted over a long overfold,
      a chlamys, and a (Thracian) fox-skin hat, reaches to the right, to stroke the nose of his
      horse. The horse stands profile to the left, in front of a schematic Ionic capital, supporting
      a narrow entablature. The horse is somewhat agitated, as indicated by his advancing left foot
      and the open lips. A youth, standing in a 3/4-view to the left, but leaning on a staff below
      his left arm, turns his head profile to the right, to look at another youth, who stands in
      near profile to the left, holds a staff in his left hand, and gestures with his opened right
      palm; both wear himatia.</P><P>View of side B: two youths, both wearing himatia,
      stand together and talk. The first is shown frontally, with his head turned profile to the
      right; he rests his right hand on his hip and holds a staff in his lowered left hand. The
      second youth stands profile to the left, facing him, and points his finger aggressively at the
      first youth. A bearded man, wearing a himation around his legs and lower torso, sits profile
      to the right on a stool (diphros), rests his left hand on a staff, and holds his right hand
      over his head. To the right of him stand two more youths, both wrapped in himation. The first,
      show profile to the left, tilts his head down slightly, and holds a staff beneath his right
      arm. The second, standing in a frontal pose, with his head turned profile to the right,
      reaches to touch the first youth on the shoulder.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/029bb0921730a03c72e7f2cffa8ea98b8b15cd4f4b9ef954dc478de971533bec> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Torso of an athletic youth"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/029e61fdc74172948bd9d4ff9e0c64fa1e2c9f6e8b2401ea20ad09849bff9018> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The caryatid figure that supports the incense burner on her
      head is Nike, the winged goddess of Victory. Nike holds up her right hand in salutation. With
      her left hand, she lifts the folds of her himation. A dove perches with raised wings on the
      knob of the lid.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

