<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/06813bd7b014d7e55aa0888b6f9d3589b13504666d3c386e06ac9d6b346862a5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Side A: Athena<lb>Side B: Chariot"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0685a9af68b20895d4a730e6a760bf86632831333a129aa6212048f9705af6a6> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Neck</hi> Three large stylized
      plants, each consisting of a palmette with tall, lyre-shaped tendrils, the latter connected by
      horizontal stripes framing lozenges (sides) or dots (front). Smaller voluting tendrils emerge
      on either side of each palmette are linked to their neighbor by triple stripes. On the back
      are five horizontal stripes framed by paired vertical stripes. The mouth is black, and there
      are horizontal stripes on the handle. <hi rend="ital">Body</hi>: On the shoulder
      are seven water birds geese or swans walk to the right, each preceded by a swastika at throat
      level and, at head level, three wavy lines possibly indicating water. The wings are incised.
      Below, around the middle of the body, is a broad black band framed above and below by five
      narrow stripes rendered with diluted, brown glaze. The black band is divided in segments by
      seven pairs of vertical white stripes. On the lower body is a zone of large black
      rays.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/068fafdf424b04c7c21d8c22b5127bf6c587324b772ff63989a3f726d4a265ea> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Confronting cocks with snake in between, youth on horseback and bird"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/06988bb819ee78e3fae507f18028fdc4a65d4bc1b97fab0b6a7c7775e913f49a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """A female figure, surrounded by ivy leaves, perhaps Eirene or Ge,
      standing 3/4-view to the right, with weight on her left leg, wearing a belted peplos, and long
      hair cascading over her shoulders, holds an infant, on a nebris, towards Hermes; the infant,
      perhaps Ploutos or Dionysos, wearing a himation, reclines 3/4-view to the left, on the nebris,
      but turns near profile to the right and reaches both arms up to Hermes; Hermes, advancing
      3/4-view to the left, with both legs bent, and his head bowed down, holds the child's right
      hand in his left hand, and his right hand on the child's head. He wears calf-length boots, a
      chlamys bucked in front, and a petasos. A kerykeion lies on the ground behind his right
      foot.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/069dd3aff1b6bd0c7f5b9c53b0a5f06a7838e57b41d0d7b8f51b844dae17751d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
