<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/06bc9131154a150759891af98d9c07857b9616f65029cd9966bb78e4744c5374> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Bowl with stamped relief appliqus on interior: two dolphins, a third
      dolphin with a boy clinging to it (Arion or Palaimon?), and a large
      fish.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/06cfd8b614362dc080df7d4fcbcb43c99bc5869a06d525364cd8c01a042c92c7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>One piece of rim broken off and repaired; otherwise unbroken. Some scratches
      and abrasion, particularly on the added white of the eyes.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/06d89c13347320306c66bb75655c113f668a306991edd4ab0b5630e6a379786d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Side A: The ambush of Dolon<BR>Side B: Two woman presenting wreaths to two
      youths."""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/06d9d2f6753ea48bf3facb7bcb6591f359c3aec9b32ffed1ec805e3de64daab4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The neck and body are white ground. The echinus mouth is
      reserved on the topside. The inside of the mouth is glazed to the neck-shoulder join. The
      triple handles are glazed on the outside and reserved on the inside. On the neck, on each side
      are three open palmettes, the outer two upright, the middle one hanging, all linked by
      tendrils and bordered above and below by a glaze line. There is a ridge at the join of the
      neck and shoulder. On the shoulder are enclosed tongues. Below each handle is a configuration
      of four palmettes and one large hanging lotus bud, with two small horizontal buds where the
      tendrils meet and a bar crossing the tendril that springs from the lower handle attachment.
      Below the figures is a pair of glazed lines above and below a right-facing key pattern, a band
      of upright open lotus buds and a pair of glazed lines. Above the foot are thirty-nine rays. At
      the body-foot join is a red fillet. The torus foot is in two degrees, with the division
      reserved. The lower part of the foot edge and the underside of the foot are
      reserved.</P><P>On side A, the scene depicts a duel. A warrior advancing to the
      right is attacking another, who falls to his knees to the right and looks back at his
      opponent. Both warriors are wearing cuirass, short chiton, greaves, and crossed baldrics from
      which scabbards are suspended. Only their helmets and shields are different. The victor wears
      a low-crested Corinthian helmet, and his shield is Boeotian. The falling warrior wears a
      high-crested Corinthian helmet and carries a round shield.</P><P>On side B, a
      similar duel is shown, but the combat direction is opposite to that on side A. Also, on side B
      the hoplites' scabbards hang from a single baldric instead of two. The victor's shield has an
      incised rosette for a device.</P><P>Red is used for the base fillet, on side A for
      the lefthand warrior's helmet crest, baldrics, the edge of his shield's rim's notched
      portions, his short chiton and right greave, the righthand warrior's helmet, shield edge,
      baldrics, the stripes on his short chiton, and his left greave, on side B the lefthand
      warrior's helmet crest edge, shield rim, the stripes of his short chiton, his left greave, and
      the righthand warrior's helmet fillet, baldric, the edge of his shield rim's notched portions,
      the stripes on his short chiton, and his right greave.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/06df5d3671d7ca7ed5522012db76a9b35a19261cae42ad939d6e0130b92238ac> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Procession of figures in Oriental costume: Dionysos (?) on a camel, attendants with
      torch, fan, and lyre, and maenads with tympana"""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/06e37fa2e08b308e5863f57b94bb5316f5cfdcf6152a18de4f65ce2ce79391da> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Eleusinian Procession"@en ;
