<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/077993a2325180bf08530b1aafcc6b0c1a6a166d73f974409e20e02ff3383a14> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Lid: Dionysos, seated maenad, five dancing maenads practicing
      sparagmos, standing maenad attending Dionysos.</P><P>Pyxis: Aphrodite (labelled),
      standing profile to the right, with her weight on her left leg, wearing a belted, sleeveless
      chiton with a kolpos, a stephane, beaded necklace, and two bands on each wrist, holds a
      scepter in her right hand, and holds the white reins of her chariot with both hands; Pothos
      (labelled) and Hedylogos (labelled), both nude, white, winged, wearing chest straps holding
      the reins, rayed crowns, and sandals, pulling Aphrodite's chariot; a small tree; Hygieia
      (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the right, with her head profile to the left, wearing a
      belted, sleeved chiton, a stephane, a beaded necklace, and two bands on each wrist; Eunomia
      (labelled), seated in a chair 3/4-view to the right, wearing a sleeved chiton, a himation
      around her legs, a sphendone, bead earrings, a beaded necklace, and two bands on each wrist,
      holds a beaded necklace with both hands; Paidia (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the left,
      wearing a belted peplos, a beaded necklace, a sphendone, bead earrings, and two bands on each
      wrist, holds a box in her left hand, and a beaded necklace in her extended right hand;
      Eudaimonia (labelled), standing near profile to the right, with her weight on her right leg,
      wearing a belted peplos (?), a high pony tail, a beaded necklace, bead earrings, and two bands
      on her right wrist, ties a sandal on her left foot with both hands; a nude, winged Himeros
      (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the left, with his weight on his right leg, wearing a rayed
      crown and sandals, holds a beaded necklace in his right hand, and an apple (?) in his left
      hand; Harmonia (labelled), seated 3/4-view to the left, with her head 3/4-view to the right,
      wearing a sleeved chiton, a himation around her legs, a spiked crown, bead earrings, a beaded
      necklace, and two bands on each wrist, rests her left arm on the back of her chair, stretches
      her right arm to the left, and holds branches in each hand; Kale (labelled), standing 3/4-view
      to the right, with her head profile to the left, wearing a sleeveless chiton draped over her
      left shoulder, a sphendone, a beaded necklace, bead earrings, and two bands on each wrist,
      raises a beaded necklace between both hands.</P><P>This image of Aphrodite riding
      a chariot led by Erotes compares to an unlabelled scene on a squat lekythos in a private
      collection in Mhlenstein (<bibl>ARV2</bibl>, 1317.3).""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

