    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0ce1d132958ec5b8c9b17be0416f201718a45763e9b473edd3d6d38d08488001> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Mertens 1987, 32 no. 17 (ill.)</bibl>; <bibl>Richter 1954, 5-6 no. 7, pl. 10a-c</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0cf1aa68cf75234e4cd3e66c4a32636b904967f26c9cc5a8d1adf0ab29fb8014> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Around the body is a frieze divided into two scenes: <hi
      rend="ital">Side A</hi>: A symposium is depicted. In the center of the composition is
      a couch with a mattress on the top, placed on raised ground, on which recline three youths to
      the left. The youth on the right is looking back. They all have drapery over their lower
      limbs, and their left arms rest on embroidered cushions. The one on the left wears a fillet in
      his hair, the one on the right, a wreath. The middle one wears two fillets twisted, one is
      white and decorated with flowers. The youth on the left holds a branch, the one on the right a
      phiale, and the middle one holds a kylix with one finger, as if playing kottabos (a drinking
      game). In front of the couch are two tables, on one is a kylix, on the other a kantharos, a
      pomegranate, and other fruit. Between the tables is a situla with a fillet around it, and to
      the left of the tables is a flat basket ornamented with a meander, in which is fruit. On the
      left is a female figure to the right, with her hair in a knot behind and falling in curls to
      her shoulders. She wears earrings, a necklace, an embroidered chiton, an undergarment with
      yellow sleeves, and white shoes. She is playing a double flute. Behind her a female figure
      approaches, with similar hairstyle and jewelry, but also bracelets. In her right hand is an
      Apulian sistrum, and in the left she holds a dish of fruit. On the right of the banqueters is
      a female figure to the left, with the same clothing and jewelry as the flute-player. In her
      left hand she holds a phiale, from which she sprinkles incense on an incense burner in front
      of her. Behind her a youthful satyr approaches, with a fillet ornamented with trefoils, a
      white kantharos in his left hand, and a situla in the right, on which is painted a seated
      female figure in yellow. Between these two figures, and between the two on the left, are vines
      spreading over the scene; in the field is a rosette. The ground lines are indicated by white
      dots.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: In the center of the
      composition Dionysos is seated to the left, looking to the right. He wears two fillets twisted
      together, sandals, and his drapery lies under him. He holds a wreath in his right hand, a
      thyrsos in his left. Before him to the left stands a female figure with her left foot on
      raised ground, holding out a wreath with both hands. Her hair is bound up; she wears a
      radiated cap, earrings, bracelets, a sleeveless chiton and sandals. Below Dionysos are two
      phialae, a large basket, and a myrtle twig; behind, on a lower level, is a youthful satyr. He
      wears a fillet, and carries a thyrsos in his left hand. With his right he offers Dionysos a
      white kantharos with black bands. On the left is a youthful satyr to the right, wearing a
      fillet and sandals, and carrying a torch in his left hand. Before him is a tall plant. Behind
      him is a female figure to the right, similar to the woman offering the wreath. She holds out a
      tympanon with her left hand, and a white bell (?) is her right. Above are two rosettes, and
      the ground line is indicated by white dots.</P><P>On the cover, between two bands
      of egg-and-dart pattern, is a frieze of figures. First is a seated female, holding up the open
      lid of a box. Her hair is gathered up under a cap, and she wears earrings, a necklace,
      bracelets, a chiton and himation, and shoes. At her side is a fan, on which is painted a white
      palmette. Before her are a rosette and a flower. Next is a female figure running to the right,
      dressed as the seated woman. She holds out a wreath in her left hand, and before her, in the
      field, is a tendril. Eros runs to the right, looking back. His hair is tied back in a bunch,
      and he wears a necklace, bracelets, sandals, and holds a fillet in both hands. Before him is a
      plant. Next is a female figure seated to the left. Her hair is pulled back, and she wears
      earrings, a necklace, bracelets, a chiton and himation, and shoes. She holds up a mirror in
      her right hand. Lastly, a female figure runs to the left, wearing earrings, a necklace,
      bracelets, a long chiton and himation, and holding out an embroidered fillet in her right
      hand.</P><P>Around the lip of the vessel is an egg-and-dart pattern, around the
      neck, ivy. On the shoulder is a radiated tongue pattern and egg-and-dart, while below the
      figural designs are meander and checker patterns. The stand is fluted; around the top of it is
      an egg-and-dart pattern, and around the foot is an ivy wreath. On the top of the cover is a
      plastically modelled flower, the edges of the petals are very
      broken.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0cf22a24421e8d15678a3abdfa26dcceb0e895eb53be75fb4d26e73284d1c302> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><bibl>CVA, Great Britain 15, Castle Ashby, 1979</bibl>;
      <bibl>G. Richter "A Kyathos by Psiax in the Museo Poldi-Peoli" <hi
      rend="ital">AJA</hi> 45 (1941) 587-592</bibl>; <bibl>Mertens 1979,
      22</bibl></P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0cf4f8a56ac9d6b91f096d40383d9ede2fb5b73624e2081b1bfb27fcdb1a8978> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Combat of Greeks with a mounted Persian. On the far right a
      bearded Persian cavalryman wears kidaris (peaked head-dress), anaxyrides (trousers <bibl
      n="Hdt. 5.49">Hdt. 5.49</bibl>, <bibl n="Hdt. 7.61">Hdt. 7.61</bibl>),
      and a jerkin decorated in alternating rows of dots and double lines, as well as a short girt
      chiton with a border and central stripe. He charges to the left, reining in his rearing horse
      with his left hand. The spear which he brandishes in his right hand is aimed at the head of
      his adversary. The horse's tail and hind leg overlap the pattern band beneath the scene. At
      center, the nearest Greek, a nude youth with frontal torso faces his opponent on the right,
      steps back to the left and counters with an upward thrust of his spear. The spear passes
      behind or through the horse and reappears behind it. He wears a high, conical pilos
      (close-fitting felt cap) and has a mantle draped from his left shoulder and a shield on his
      right arm. From the left another Greek appears on foot, facing right. The youth with short,
      wavy hair wears a short girt chiton which exposes his left shoulder and a quiver at his waist.
      He steps forward, both arms extended, as he aims his bow at the Persian. Neither bowstring nor
      arrow are shown.</P><P>Added white and yellow are used for markings on the horse
      and pilos. Dilute glaze is used for anatomical details. Spirals of hair are rendered in swirls
      of thinned black on a brown wash.</P><P>Around the rim is an egg pattern. This is
      echoed in another around the belly which acts as a ground line for the figures. On the back
      there is a pattern of palmettes. On the upper surface of the rim and the outer curve of the
      foot are reserved bands.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0cf9f8ec6b25fc878afeefaede369e14d5b546d0b52d34cbef325487ec364544> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
