<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0d064302a5e676bb479f9a74df276e663ac99ce3919266cc04ceee044b5d8214> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: A woman offers a
      warrior a drink at his departure. The woman stands in profile to the right, her left foot
      forward and her weight resting on the right leg. She wears a chiton with sleeves to the elbow,
      and a mantle is draped over head head. She holds a skyphos in her right hand, and an oinochoe
      in her left. In front of her face is a circular floral pattern, while above that, hanging from
      the border decoration at the shoulder of the vessel, is a half circle painted white. The
      warrior stands frontally, with his head turned to the left, looking at the woman. He holds a
      spear in his right hand, and balances a shield on the ground with his left. He wears
      breastplate of three circles and a plumed helmet (typical of native Oscan warriorsee
      <bibl>F. Weege, Oskische Grabmalerei, <hi rend="ital">JdI</hi> XXIV (1909),
      150, figs. 21, 22</bibl> for examples) which are both painted white. His short chiton is
      decorated with dots, perhaps representing an animal skin.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Side B</hi>: A youth and a woman are represented.</P><P>The
      lip of the vessel is decorated with a radial band pattern, the neck with a large palmette, and
      the shoulder with another radial band pattern. The lower border is a wave pattern, and there
      are palmettes under the handles.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

