<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0e8c0241f3a141258c8912e912ed0e54347920fdbcaf4c05b82a9dca6aad77c7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The exterior is undecorated.</P><P>On the interior,
      a boar hunt is depicted, with two hunters holding their spears high and running to the right
      after a running boar. Only the hindquarters and tail of the boar are visible, as it presumably
      moves to attack further hunters in front of it. The curled tail testifies to the kind of
      quarry being pictured, but the animal's hoofs resemble those of a cow or horse much more than
      those of a pig. The boar is wounded, and blood flows from its side. The two hunters wear short
      chitons and have beards and long curly locks. The rear hunter wears an animal skin over his
      chiton. Three birds are flying between the legs of the hunters, and beneath the ground line
      are three large fish.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/0e8ee259d1d6a5aaa9f5f5d379e25f530e3aca9c5d14e2f9089ddc3f931842e9> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
