<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/11dc2e816372a00723c2940503c8ad850462289dde949bb0ebb5e32ae483632e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Theater of Greek type with orchestra, parodoi, and stage building, located in the north of the city, below the acropolis and above the upper gymnasium."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/11e187ddf1a2758a196e5bacd0a70231280117fde25af4f70ff55db01dca1862> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>On the left a woman stands, holding the edge of her garment
      with her left hand and the soldier's helmet in her right. She is modestly dressed in a sakkos
      and a long, sleeved chiton with a deep overfold. Opposite her stands a nude bearded man in a
      frontal pose. He turns his head to look at her, holding his right hand out to receive his
      helmet and holding his spear in his left. Between them a goose with ruffled neck feathers
      pecks at the ground. Behind the woman, partly hidden is a diphros (stool). Above it a small
      jug hangs in the field. Here is a domestic scene within the woman's quarters or perhaps in the
      courtyard.</P><P>The body is covered with a fine white slip, on which the design
      is drawn in brown outline. Above the design is a band of reversing meanders broken by squares
      with dotted oblique crosses. On the shoulder is a pattern of three palmettes, brown on white.
      Above this there is an egg pattern.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

