<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/185bec3aea09baca095a2fb3392c8491b7ce12748abb340a80fef18560ac6da0> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A, upper frieze:</hi> boar
      hunt. In the center a boar is being attacked from both sides by hunters with spears. The boar
      is running to the right, as blood drips from his body. On each side three naked hunters
      wearing fillets stride toward him with their spears raised. A seventh hunter lies beneath the
      boar; he is dressed in a chitoniskos with incised details. Each of the hunters on the left
      carries a mantle over his left arm; all hunters on both sides except the one closest to the
      boar on the right are bearded. The hunter closest to the boar on the left grabs its tail. On
      the left two dogs, one female, accompany the men. On the right is a single dog. Three rosettes
      appear in the background between the figures to the right of the
      boars.</P><P>Added red is used for the left-hand hunters' mantles, the dogs' necks
      and bellies, the boar's jaw outline and belly, its blood, the spear points, and marks on the
      chests and thighs of the three right-hand hunters.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Side B, upper frieze:</hi> wedding procession. In the center the bridal
      couple moves right in a four-horse chariot. The bride is wearing chiton and himation, while
      the groom wears a cloak over his chiton. Behind them, one bearded male, two single females,
      and two pairs of females proceed to the right. The male is dressed like the groom, while all
      the females wear chitons and himatia. All figures wear incised fillets. On the left (far) side
      of the horses stand two more women facing right; their bodies are obscured by the horses'
      rumps. In front of the horses, to the right, stand a man and two pairs of women all facing
      left. These figures are dressed like those on the left. Between pairs of people, snakes or
      flying birds appear intermittently. Two incised rosettes begin and end the scene at far left
      and far right, and a third is barely visible above the horses' backs. The groundline is a band
      of dilute glaze with a narrower band in added red; it runs around the entire
      vase.</P><P>Added red occurs in alternate himatia along the line of left-hand
      female pairs, all the men's cloaks, the inside of the bride's himation, alternate locks of
      hair in the pole horse's mane, and the himatia of the far right-hand pair of women. Dilute
      ochre glaze appears for all figures' chitons except for the second single woman on the left
      and the left-hand male.</P><P>A continuous frieze of animals fills the lower
      panel, panthers alternating with deer and goats. Added red appears in the necks and bellies of
      all the animals, as well as stripes on their haunches. Below this panel is a wide black band
      with narrower added red bands running around the whole base.</P><P>At the base are
      thirteen rays. The foot's exterior is black with narrower added-red bands. The undersurface is
      reserved.</P><P>A siren stretches its wings on each handle plate. Broad added-red
      bands cover each wing and tail, and thinner bands of added red alternate with black on the
      wing edges and tail feathers. The junctures of the handle plates with the top of the rim
      contain double lines on one side and single lines on the other. The top and sides of the rim
      and the sides of the handle plates are filled with zigzag lines. Beneath each glazed handle a
      griffin alights, each with two incised rosettes in the background. Added red appears in much
      the same positions on the griffins as on the sirens. The vessel's neck is mostly black, with
      reserved space at the handles. The rim's underside is also reserved. The intersection of the
      body and neck contains alternating red and black tongues. On side A the spears in the main
      panel overlap with the tongues. Incised lines border most areas of added red. The interior of
      the neck and shoulder are glazed black. Bands of added red decorate the
      neck.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/185d848c003399a33634e3a074c6660e647dda1e6c6f41468a4a1a9b488cb6c8> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Both sides: frieze of centaurs, griffins, deer, horse, panther."@en ;
