<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/19c044c208f200aac94c7d796a11f3b17b8acb288d37de73a34d74d12e8e0457> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """A female figure, perhaps Hera [Clairmont] or Tyndareus [at the abduction
      of Helen, according to Shapiro], holding scepter to right; Peitho (labelled), standing profile
      to the right, wearing a himation veiled over her head, which she holds above her shoulder in
      her upraised left hand, and a narrow red taenia; Aphrodite (labelled), standing profile to the
      right, wearing a himation draped around her lower body and over her breast/left shoulder, over
      a medium-, button-sleeved chiton, and a sakkos decorated with small brown dots, holds her
      lowered, bent left arm at her side, and a flower bud in her right hand, at waist level; nude,
      red Eros, flying near profile to the right (his legs, back of torso and head, and most of
      wings preserved), wearing a narrow red taenia, bends his right arm.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/19c93222502998570aaa0df12f6f20b4811ba4bafbc5704927961404f0ff8684> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>On side A, four runners move to the right. On side B, Athena is
      pictured, facing right, with a column on either side of
      her.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

