<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/1e7a1b60376c795bd8263954fe6b5f33b9d9f545e7c3ffe18ff0de5661638b03> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Eirene and Ploutos, presumably atop a column (or perhaps Tyche and
      Ploutos): Female figure (preserved except for her right hand, both shoulders, and left arm)
      standing 3/4-view to the left, with her weight on her right leg, and her head turned 3/4-view
      to the right, tilted slightly down, wearing an unbelted peplos, a wreath (painted white dots),
      some strands of hair falling around neck, holds a scepter in her upraised right hand, and
      cradles in her left arm a keras (black outlined with a white double-line), from which emerges
      Ploutos (head and top of shoulders revealed), also wearing a white wreath
      (dotted).""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/1e7b329611d08f2324c5689afe43bea149f3c341008d44d8b5c85b0b830a9438> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
