<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/1fb27be638cd91a45774a5ac9cd083a2d9df5456e6e5288bab1e72b900f37234> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Relief from an honorary (?) decree with a representation of Demos"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/1fb520dce4b5f1ec4a6571e215f5787191a4e570c277e099950c62aca4862acd> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Side A: man sits to the right on a klismos, flanked by two
      youths. All wear himations, and the two youths also wear red fillets. The man's head is
      restored from the lips up. The man holds a staff in his left hand and a fruit (fig?) in his
      right. Facing him at right, one youth leans on a staff. Behind him at left, a second youth
      sits on a stool. In front of this youth, hanging on the wall, is a pair of
      sandals.</P><P>Side B: man seated on a block between two standing youths. All wear
      himations. The man and youth at left wear red fillets. The man holds a staff in his left hand
      and twists around to gesture at the youth behind him, who leans on his staff to the right. A
      second youth stands before the man to right; his face is badly damaged. Between them a pouch
      or purse tied with red string hangs in field. Between the man and the other youth hangs a
      cross-shaped object, probably the top of a torch.</P><P>Under the handles are
      palmettes and coiling tendrils. There is a black circle under the
      foot.</P><P>Tondo: a youth sits on a klismos to right. His body between knees and
      shoulder is missing. There is a reserved exergue. In the field at right hangs a tortoise shell
      lyre with a hanging red cord. A meander frame also appears.</P><P>School scenes
      may be intended.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/1fb650cb3e6e70c7392b39cd76de7323b43bace13e572f3d896bc2e2c66fb467> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Sides A and B: Athletic figure and trainer. Tondo: centaur."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/1fc47991d2855c40616e8cf7d5df27cc8a8e79dad746b68bab44ace5ad1fc76d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Side A: athlete with pick to left loosens soil of field at
      palaestra. He wears a red fillet. At right is a stone pillar. At left hanging from a peg is a
      strigil and a flat-bottomed aryballos with red cords.</P><P>Side B: athlete in red
      fillet sits to right, with hands around his knee. A fillet hangs at right. To right are a
      strigil and flat-bottomed aryballos with red cords.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/1fc9ad859e3a38cb234442f510b6b2818d5a59a9e8b73746d6f05c6366179906> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Smith 1997</bibl>, cat. R 4; <bibl>LIMC, 7 (1994) 142 s.v. Paidia no. 13, pl. 96 (A. Kossatz-Deissmann)</bibl>; <bibl>Kossatz-Deissmann 1991</bibl>, 188; <bibl>Simon 1981</bibl>, 19-20, pl. 3; <bibl>Neumann 1979</bibl>, 49, pl. 26b; <bibl>Froning 1971, 8-11</bibl>; <bibl>Pickard-Cambridge 1968</bibl>, 179, fig. 26; <bibl>Bieber 1961a</bibl>, 32, fig. 113a-b (and E. Simon, rev. in Gnomon 41 [1969] 792); <bibl>Hibbs 1962, 62-63, fig. 68</bibl>; <bibl>Lippold 1950</bibl>, 197 n. 12; <bibl>Svoronos 1903-12</bibl>, 512-28, pl. 82; FR, 3.138, fig. 61; <bibl>Harrison 1903, 360</bibl>; M. Bieber, <hi rend=\"ital\">Denkmler zum Theaterwesen</hi> 104 f., no. 41, pl. 53." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/1fd504a6fbeb2f8d5bfcc52906288d778fbc3eb7c7dc38950b6f3fee1c1b671c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
