<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/251c99d77c35c85474b39f3f8cc44f7ea56af94b4c5cda49eaf9bb10d1e7594a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">On the shoulder</hi>: Dionysiac
      group; Dionysos, Ariadne, satyr and maenad. In the center of the composition Ariadne and
      Dionysos sit facing each other. Dionysos, on the left, sits on a footstool and holds a
      drinking horn. Ariadne is seated on a chest or box. To the left of the main scene, Hermes
      stands and holds his caduceus, and a satyr chases a maenad. To the right of the main scene,
      the satyr and maenad composition is repeated. Vine branches are in the
      background.</P><P><hi rend="ital">On the body</hi>: Two heroes
      quarreling. There are seven nude or partially clothed men in the scene. In the center, a
      bearded man wearing only a chlamys strides to the right, between the two fighting men. He
      looks back to the left with his arms raised and mouth open; he appears to be shouting
      excitedly and trying to stop them. The fighting man to the left is bearded. He is brandishing
      his sword above his head, and in his left hand he holds the scabbard in front of him. He
      strides toward his opponent, who is also stepping forward. The opponent is clean shaven, with
      three curling strands of hair falling down on the side of his face. His right arm is hidden
      behind the central figure, and in his left hand he holds a sword. A nude man has grabbed each
      of these fighters around the waist, in a further attempt to stop them. At the furthest edges
      of the composition, another figure stands on each side. The one to the left is draped in a
      cloak and is clean shaven. He steps forward and raises his left arm to grasp the wrist of the
      bearded fighter and stop him from using his sword. The figure on the far right is bearded; he
      wears a loincloth (?) tied around his waist. He has grasped the beardless fighter's arm in the
      crook of his own.</P><P>The vertical borders are ivy and the lower horizontal one
      is palmettes.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/252004742fb12a49b3f99dbf1271199ae4f529b7ee46e53ef4aa8e3204cde8a5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
