<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/28d2c3caea4e241ae980d9ac7d901b04ce355409290bdf150dd26321a02cf61c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Side A: komos. Side B: Three youths in mantles."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/28d3c15185437f2f6c79ba969399eae5812a71377b786aa1bbf360751564b50f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """A: A winged Nike, leaning 3/4-view to the right, with weight on her
      right leg, wearing a belted, bordered peplos, and a red ampyx with black maeander over her
      short hair, pours water from a hydria, held in both hands, into a three-footed loutrophoros; a
      bull standing profile to the left in front of a large tripod, with stemmata around its horns,
      bends his head down to drink; a female figure, perhaps Phyle, advancing 3/4-view to the left,
      wearing a belted peplos, a red sphendone, and a white crown indicated by three spikes, bends
      both arms and holds a white fillet (?) in her upraised right and lowered left
      hands.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/28dab55d8321b23f29ac1e47802ee2c908989bdee252aab85a0785b096b6692d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><bibl>CVA, USA 2, RISD 1, p.31, Pl.23:
      2</bibl></P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/28e9b245e000e02aaa8d18e59b9a7321ac07ac39ca1b3d97092c3ba0dfa3cd3d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Boardman 1995, fig. 28.2</bibl>; <bibl>Karouzou 1968, 167-168</bibl>; <bibl>Svoronos 1903-12, 179, pl. 30.1</bibl>." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/28eac7203fe6699a3dc817608cf31ad479762c134cb886f39554a8ed67362984> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><bibl>CVA, Munich 6, 42-43</bibl>; <bibl>Simon 1975b,
      80-81</bibl></P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/28ec05e160742d0f4c5dcbd152ee2fdfeb01c8523b792d375aa833f9c6c61af1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Interior:</hi> An ithyphallic satyr
      moves to the right in a knielauf position. He carries a wineskin in his left hand and a
      drinking horn in his right. He has a tail, pointy ears, and a snub nose. His beard is long and
      shaggy, and he wears a wreath in his hair.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side
      A:</hi> Dionysos with satyr and maenad. At the left of the composition, a naked
      ithyphallic satyr moves to the right. Like the satyr in the interior of the cup, he carries a
      wineskin in his left hand and a drinking horn in his right. Dionysos at the center, looks to
      the left but stands with lower body facing right. In his left hand he carries a drinking horn
      and in his right a spreading branch with leaves and clusters of grapes. He wears a chiton and
      mantle, and a wreath in his hair. At the right of the composition, a maenad dances to the
      left. She wears an embroidered chiton and diagonal himation. In her left hand she carries a
      thyrsos and in her right krotala. Added red is used to render wreathes in the hair of the
      satyr and Dionysos, and for a bracelet and a fillet in the maenad's hair, as well as for the
      grape leaves. The grape clusters are rendered with relief dots.</P><P><hi
      rend="head">Side B:</hi> Satyr and maenads. At the left of the composition, a naked
      ithyphallic satyr shown in profile moves to the right. He leans forward and grasps the hem of
      a maenad's skirt with his right hand, while gesturing with his left. This maenad, moving to
      the right, looks back at the satyr. She holds a thyrsos in her left hand and in her right a
      snake, which coils up her arm. She wears a chiton, diagonal himation and a sakkos. At the
      right of the composition, a second maenad moves left, gesturing with her right hand toward
      this group. She carries a tree branch in her left hand. She too wears a chiton and a sakkos,
      but adds a spotted leopard skin tied around her shoulders. Added red is used for the satyr's
      wreath and for the maenads' bracelets. <bibl>Carpenter 1986</bibl> points out that
      maenads carrying snakes are rare in Attic vase-painting before this
      period.</P><P>A palmette complex is placed underneath and on either side of the
      handles.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

