<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/2b3022b43e19426e501994bb1baea876cbe0c5dd30e92bdcfaa18d9e5402c136> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Ajax threatens
      Kassandra with his sword. His armor consists of a helmet and harness over a short chiton
      decorated with red dots and incised stars. Kassandra is kneeling in front of him turned to the
      right, her head facing Ajax. To her right stands Athena wearing a peplos with white floral
      decoration, ependytes, and a crested helmet. She is holding a spear in her raised left hand
      and a large shield decorated with a tripod in her right. A nude bearded man runs off to her
      right. The scene is observed on the far left by a woman dressed in a
      peplos.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: A quadriga is depicted
      frontally. The charioteer wears a white himation and holds a kentron. The two central horses
      are facing each other, the other two outwards. Their manes and chest harnesses are painted in
      red.</P><P>Both panels are framed on the top by a frieze of alternating palmettes
      and lotus buds.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

