<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/2d4121a2cd14072944cfc426c27e299d3ebf0682794e1b6c3f692d078bd6bb47> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Front</hi>: winged demon or boread
      flying right. The boread rushes to the right in the bent-kneed, bent-armed running pose
      typical of gorgons. His body is shown frontally and his legs and head are in profile. He is
      bearded and has shoulder length hair, and is dressed in a chitoniskos with zig-zag bands along
      the lower edge, over the shoulders and down the center of the chest.</P><P><hi
      rend="head">Under handle</hi>: standing bird. The large bird stands facing right, its
      head turned toward the left.</P><P>There is much incised detail in the figural
      decoration, and thick filling ornament covers the field, consisting mainly of incised
      rosettes.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

