<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/2ef6f425dc6395d8ff8c3bca60d0836ba5966f317ae17baf10ad9a93be4e3b3a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The tondo depicts a bearded man standing profile to the right,
      wearing drapery around his waist and hips, holding something (meat?) in his left hand, and
      reaching his right hand into a large cauldron on a tripod.</P><P>The exterior
      scenes seem to show butchers. Side A depicts a youth (?), advancing profile to the right,
      behind a long table, who holds a meat clever in his lowered right hand, and an animal leg in
      his outstretched left hand. Another man, standing profile to the left, reaches for the animal
      leg, with his right hand, and holds a skewer in his lowered left hand. On side B is depicted
      another youth (?), advancing profile to the right, who holds skewers in both
      hands.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/2efbce3b8f892eecc5a5831102c30798720b352ea88d4d164e0528e5d26c1bcf> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
