<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/320d8cfc1b4639a284559f816a7009fec5794b53928d12cd270936ba69f60067> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A</hi>Birth of Athena. Athena,
      not yet full size, stands on Zeus' lap while five other deities gather around. Zeus, seated on
      a throne in the center of the scene, reaches toward Athena with one hand while holding a
      stylized thunderbolt in his other hand. He is shown in profile to the right, his feet resting
      on a low stool. Zeus is bearded and is dressed in a striped chiton, a plain red himation with
      a decorative border, and a short, black mantle decorated with rosettes and draped over both
      shoulders. He wears a headband over his long hair. The throne has a ram's head on the visible
      end of the backrest. There is a small, winged Nike beneath the throne; she raises her left arm
      palm upward. Athena is standing on Zeus' lap facing right. Although small in stature, she is
      fully dressed and is armed with helmet, shield and spear. A bird flies away from her to the
      right. Eileithyia stands in front of Athena, facing her and touching her right hand to her
      chin, her other hand held out toward Athena, palm upward. She is dressed in chiton and
      himation, and also wears a band around her head. Ares stands at the far right, facing the
      central figures. He is mostly hidden by the large shield which he holds. It is decorated with
      a star motif at its center and scales around the outside. Ares wears helmet and greaves. His
      dog hides behind his legs. Apollo stands behind Zeus' throne on the left, holding his kithara
      and dressed in a white chiton, over which he wears a striped himation. His kithara is held in
      his left arm while he plays with his right. His hair is long and is worn in a headband, with
      long, thin braids in front of his ears. Another male figure stands beside Apollo and is mostly
      hidden by him. He is dressed in chiton and himation, and holds his right hand, palm open, at
      his waist. A bird flies to the left above him. There are nonsense inscriptions between the
      figures.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B</hi>Assembly of gods, perhaps
      the introduction of Herakles to Olympos. Poseidon and Amphitrite stand together at the left.
      Amphitrite, on the far left, stands facing center, wearing a white(?) chiton with red dots
      under a black and red striped himation, the black stripes decorated with small white rosettes.
      She has white skin and long hair bound with a red band. Poseidon also faces to the right,
      holding his trident upright in his left hand. His right arm is bent at his side. He wears a
      red chiton and a black mantle decorated with rosettes. Zeus and Hera are seated side by side
      on stools in the center of the scene, facing toward the right; there is a small sphinx under
      Zeus' stool. Zeus holds a stylized thunderbolt in his right hand; his extended left arm has
      been damaged. He has a long beard and long hair, and wears a red chiton over which a black
      mantle has been draped to cover both shoulders. Hera is partially hidden behind Zeus and part
      of her head has been lost through damage to the vase. Her white face and one raised hand are
      preserved. She wears a black himation. Above and right, a bird flies left toward her. Four
      figures stand to the right of Zeus and Hera, all facing left. Immediately to the right stands
      a warrior, perhaps Herakles. His torso is hidden behind his shield with its lion head
      decoration. He wears greaves and has a red beard. To the right of him stands a female, dressed
      in a red chiton and a black himation decorated with rosettes; there are inscriptions above and
      between these two figures. On the far right are two overlapping figures, the one in front a
      naked male figure, beardless and with long red hair. Partially hidden behind him is a female
      wearing a simple red chiton or peplos with a black border.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/320fd3f47c117441be8466ae9931f7d3c1b7d69d6d77dec3507e6c36c2ac22bc> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
