<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/35ecfc6d44f5caa4a889976dad0ba53137fa7058d51f0ac7e46ccc96d7d1116d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Herakles, clad in lion's skin and short chiton and armed with
      sword, bow and quiver, rushes from left to center. He pursues Nereus, the old man of the sea,
      catching hold of his right wrist with his own right hand and reaching for his shoulder with
      his left. The old man of the sea, identified by his flowing white hair and beard, holds a fish
      as an attribute in his left hand. Though he walks to the right, he turns round to face his
      pursuer as Herakles grasps his wrist. Nereus wears a wreath in added red, a long, sleeved
      chiton and a himation draped across his left shoulder. His bowed head and quiet resistance
      yield to the force of Herakles' youthful action.</P><P>The design only occurs on
      the body, without borders, except for a frieze band under the figures where two meanders
      alternate with a dotted checker square. Around the neck there is a tongue pattern. Around the
      outer curve of the foot is a reserved band.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/360428654ba9a51ff8876159ddfede3d47c6a7ae949ed54756331294f402664e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
