<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3cf71c9652477873f84d530734ba6a9cb70974d580514e3763f601def8885861> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Woman looking back"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3d04b7e64f43d6231826f5d31245ca0045a4b56805e64eb55a52676056f8107e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A: An inscription, <Foreign
      lang=Greek>[*T*O*N*A*Q]*E*N*E*Q*E*N*A*Q*L[*O]*N</Foreign>, along a black Aeolic (?)
      column on a one-stepped base, topped with a black plinth; on the plinth Eirene, standing
      3/4-view to the right, with her weight on her left leg, and her head in profile to the right,
      raises her right hand, and cradles in her left arm a small, white boy, Ploutos, with black
      hair, wearing a black himation (?), who reaches his right hand up towards the head of Eirene,
      and holds the keras in his left hand; in the center, an archaistic Athena Promachos, standing
      profile to the right; an identical column (?), with an inscription, <Foreign
      lang=Greek>[A*R]*X*W*N*K*A*L*L*I*M*H*D*H*S*</Foreign>.</P><P>B: A bearded
      male figure, probably the referee, standing 3/4-view to the right, with his left leg advanced,
      holds his right hand at his side, and his left hand in front of his body; two nude wrestlers,
      both near frontal, with their heads turned profile, wrestling, but standing on the ground
      (except for left leg of left-most wrestler); female figure (label, according to Themelis, to
      the right of her head, <Foreign lang=Greek>*O*L*U[*M*P*I]*A*S</Foreign>, standing
      near frontal, with weight on her left leg, and her head profile to the left, wearing a black
      himation wrapped entirely around her body, over her bent left arm, holds the back of her left
      hand on her hip.</P><P>For Olympias cf. <rs type="vase">Athens, NM
      20045</rs> and <rs type="vase">Cambridge
      1925.30.124</rs>.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3d1c4093f24f882a82033692dc8bf9f5ee42574e563d57758b58e0193a91a5c6> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Mollard-Besques 1954, 21, cat. B 121 (with previous bibliography), pl. 16</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3d24450371916f97ff7e1d731de7bd6d05fac9c093882c6601e8c796a65f4a6d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Exterior by Euergides Painter, interior by a lesser
      artist.</P><P>Side A: Herakles kneels to right over the top of the crouching lion,
      which raises its left hind leg. Herakles wears a red wreath. The lion's mouth is open and
      snarling. In the background is a tree with red leaves from which hang a cloak and a sword. At
      right, another cloak hangs. At left, two nude youths run up, both with red fillets, gesturing
      emphatically. At right, a third nude youth runs up with a cloak over his extended left arm,
      and a club in his lowered right hand. Behind him is a palm tree. He wears a red wreath, and is
      possibly identified as Iolaos.</P><P>Side B: Herakles and the Cretan bull.
      Herakles stands with his back to the viewer and ties up the bull with a rope. Behind is a tree
      with red leaves from which hangs a cloak. Two youths run up on either side, and two youths run
      away at either edge. Herakles and all youths wear fillets. The youth at far right has a cloak.
      Second youth from left wears a wreath. There is a large ivy leaf below each
      handle.</P><P>Tondo: nude archer to right firing an arrow to right, drawing back
      his bow. Added red is used for the string, arrow, and
      wreath.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3d349aac6cad6821f09633a749f810de8522f39a489635a7d0d52528a5ae5ab9> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Body:</hi> Woman facing stele
      brings funerary offerings. A woman stands, facing right, in front of a stele which has a
      fillet tied around its center. She is dressed in an Ionic chiton, which is broken up into many
      rippling folds. With both hands outstretched she supports a huge basket of offerings,
      including a black lekythos and numerous hanging fillets. In the field hangs another long
      fillet, caught up in two places.</P><P>Neck and handle are red. There are traces
      of black on the lip; and the foot and lower body are black. On the shoulder there are four
      black-figured palmettes connected by tendrils and at the junction of the neck, short rays. On
      the white slip, above the design, there is a simple running
      meander.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3d43858ad862f06329d967978a9a47113e13517a0ab01f40063f2acf05a8d824> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
