<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3ea7161b15a71a4391d24296cefb7c976ec785ac66bb2d5053dda984d82e915e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A:</hi> Dionysos and
      attendants. Dionysos stands at center, facing right, holds a pair of ivy branches in his left
      and holds out a kantharos in his right hand to be filled. Facing him stands a naked youth, who
      pours wine from an oinochoe. Wine shown with dilute glaze. Between the two, an amphora on the
      ground. Behind Dionysos, a naked youth carries a fox and a hare on a pole in his right hand,
      and an ivy branch in his left. Behind this youth, another carries a wineskin. Behind the youth
      pouring wine, another youth, wearing a chlamys over his shoulders, carries a fox and a hare on
      a pole.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B:</hi> four horsemen gallop to
      left. Each holds a spear in his hands, together with the reins. Front youth is unbearded; the
      two rear youths have beards (one red, one incised). All wear short-sleeved chitons and pointed
      caps. Before the horses, a hound races to left.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3eaa9b317ef6710da2cc4fe618d45c7af8720b2a75f5ce97de76699042f5188f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
