<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/3fe3d08aa3c372bbd88e17e2bab1260f8dd46b73f04b87b620f5a83c928b160c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Four-horse chariot, frontal position. The two pole horses have
      turned their heads toward each other. The charioteer in his chariot appears behind and between
      them; the charioteer's face lacks all features. The two trace horses stand to either side with
      their heads turned away from each other.</P><P>Added red is used for the manes and
      tails of all the horses, as well as part of the chariot and the breastbands of the trace
      horses. Added white appears on the charioteer's robe, dots along the reins and along the edge
      of the breastbands.</P><P>The mouth's interior is glazed to a depth of 0.03 m. A
      band of added red circles the lip. The handle cross section is elliptical. The main panel is
      bounded above by a chain of upright palmettes and tongues, with added red for the center petal
      and core of the palmettes. A narrow reserved band runs beneath the groundline. Two bands in
      added red complete the vessel, one beneath the figure scene, the other on the upper edge of
      the foot.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

