<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/45b55ea0ef25342a6e0e3d7a238bcf6549d21df502ab2777bec7736c37593406> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<P><bibl>AuKGP 1986, 176f. (Krystalli-Botsi)</bibl>; <bibl>Pedley 1976, 33</bibl>); <bibl>Richter 1970b, no. 74</bibl>; <bibl>Charbonneaux 1963, 4</bibl>; <bibl>Buschor 1950, 40f.</bibl></P>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/45bf9b049464f1ac9801bcf283e93c7d8d1c952fd5f926768bf7a3f735333b5a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "F. Imhoof-Blumer, <hi rend=\"ital\">Kleinasiatische Mnzen</hi> I (Vienna 1901) 213 no.  24 for obv." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/45d0f346d955943500dbc5bdb01d52af7413177852aba2386be7af05958ef47d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: a young warrior on
      horseback is riding to the right. The horse is depicted at a slow trot, its mane tied up into
      two hair knots and its tail is pointing straight backwards. The muscles along the chest and
      back are delineated in red, the teeth and bridle are indicated with white dots. The horseman,
      who is holding the reins in one hand and a spear in the other, wears a headband with white
      decoration. His red chiton has short sleeves and white dotted decoration along the
      seams.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: The horseman on this side
      is, with a few exceptions, similar to the one on the opposite side. His profile is lost; the
      headband does not show white decoration. The chest of the horse is entirely painted in
      red.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Shoulder B</hi>: The image decorating the
      neck on Side B shows a better state of preservation and is therefore discussed first. Hermes
      is depicted standing in front of Zeus, flanked on either side by a bearded man. Zeus is seated
      on a stool, his left hand raised in greeting, his right holding a scepter. He is wearing a red
      chiton with decorated seams and a black mantle with red dots and rosettes dotted in white.
      Hermes, with a red beard, is leaving to the right, his head turned back to Zeus. He raises his
      right hand in greeting while holding the kerykeion in his left. On his head he wears a
      petasos. His legs are almost entirely lost; only a faint trace of a winged boot is visible. A
      fawn skin is tied over his chiton and he has a black mantle draped around his shoulders, which
      is similarly decorated to that worn by Zeus. The two flanking figures each hold a scepter in
      one hand and have the other raised in greeting. Both men are wearing a long red chiton with
      decorated seams, and a mantle similar to those worn by the two gods.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Shoulder A</hi>: The image is largely destroyed. A bearded man is seated
      between two men in long mantles facing right. A nude youth is facing the one furthest to the
      right; both men are raising their right in greeting. The youth holds his left hand slightly
      raised, the palm pointing forward. He has red hair, a ribbon across his chest, and he wears a
      white beaded necklace.</P><P>Linear scrolls with spiral tendrils are decorating
      the areas below the handles. The frieze on the belly is framed by a band of dentils above a
      garland of buds and arches.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/45d2abe3dc3e3214f6a710c5574620e8ab2a3cf694408ec6393dd5b4b426b004> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><bibl>Boardman 1974, 18</bibl>; <bibl>Fairbanks 1928,
      196, n. 561, pl. 64</bibl>; <bibl>Payne 1931, 196, 199-200, pl. 52,
      2-3</bibl></P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

