<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/467c75bb348eb558932bea4ef4c9e90755ca6502d6be2e69d4b2c232f6a2e18e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Female figure, perhaps Hecuba, resting on her knees"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/4683c8fd9e2beb34df854fdee0bd86e17c2b2903c8b5b0c1feb0afca50ac8dc7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The shoulder zone and inward sloping rim are decorated with
      bands of tongues.</P><P>In the main panel panthers with frontally turned faces
      stand on either side of a large griffin with raised wings. The pointed ears of the griffin
      reach into the shoulder zone. The griffin's throat and breast are marked with purple flecks
      and spots. Large rosettes and smaller blossoms and dots fill the free space between the three
      figures.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/469b9a7e4a52e6cccb0b2a8a24bd834f7dcea4e069afab1dc95fcd757a7c561d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> I, 21, no. 104; <bibl>Cohen 1880-1892, 1.180,1</bibl>; <bibl>Babelon 1885-1886, 2.82.254</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/46ae8fbb94cfa58ebf556b7605d641fc2c27a77cb3b2c51e339a2df827e85fdc> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Three women wearing fillets, chitons and himations are gathered
      in an interior setting, probably the women's quarters of a home. All three have the queues of
      their hair tied up in small cloth bundles secured with crossed cords. The two women standing
      at left are facing the woman at right, who is seated on a klismos; she may be the mistress of
      the house and the other two either relations or slaves. A wool-basket (<hi
      rend="ital">kalathos</hi>) hangs upside down on the wall above. On the ground,
      interspersed between the women, are two herons, probably pets. The heron at left looks up at
      the first woman, whose himation covers both arms and is pulled taut in front by the right arm,
      the hand of which emerges just below the face. The second heron faces the woman in the center,
      who holds a skyphos in her left hand and stretches her right hand forward with the thumb and
      index finger nearly touching; she appears to be dropping a piece of food to the heron, having
      just removed it from the skyphos. The bird raises its head in anticipation, lifting one foot
      off the floor. Behind it, the seated woman also extends a hand over the bird; it is not clear
      whether she is teasing it or trying to calm it.</P><P>The groundline consists of a
      band of paired maeanders to right alternating with cross-squares; the same pattern is used for
      a shorter band above the figures, at the base of the neck. A band of tongue pattern circles
      the lip.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/46af8b36182beaee047a1be376e632c5b1b2a9d550cc2878e33d191637e18feb> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> Satyrs and Maenads. At
      the left a Maenad dances to the left. She wears a long Doric chiton, with a border of
      palmettes at the bottom. Around her neck is a necklace of white beads, and her hair is bound
      with a garland of white berries. She holds a thyrsos in her left hand and a large white
      tympanon or tambourine in her right. Behind her is a nude silen in an ecstatic pose with his
      right arm bent behind his head and his left stretched downwards, perhaps to the drinking horn
      at his feet. In the center, behind the silen, a Maenad dances, her white flesh showing through
      long, transparent drapery. She wears a necklace of small beads and a garland in her disheveled
      hair. With her head thrown back she sings and dances ecstatically to the accompaniment of the
      tambourine which she plays with both hands. She glides to the right while below and to the
      right, a nude silen moves to the right in a violent pose, his right leg straight, his left
      sharply bent. His hair, beard, and tail are rendered in added white. In his right hand he
      holds an unidentifiable object and in his left, a white tambourine. Above him and to the right
      is another silen in repose, facing left. He is nude and holds a horn in his right hand; his
      left is on his hip. In the field between the two silens are bunches of
      grapes.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B:</hi> Three youths. In the center
      is a nude youth in right profile, with his body in three-quarters view. His right hand rests
      on his hip, and his left holds a strigil. On either side of him there is a youth in himation
      facing him. The youth on the left holds out a strigil in his left hand, the one at the right
      extends his right arm. In the field hang two round vessels and two triangular objects, perhaps
      leather cases. Under each handle there is an altar.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/46c419aaced826b5d1e1058928159e962ae693a65218a0b4d2975f7d536467f4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
