<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/4e3fbbfc40d56ec43609a3b924bb61217b859fcdf0ae78e988c45507bd1344ad> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Lattimore 1979, 71</bibl>; <bibl>Vierneisel-Schlrb 1979, 423-29</bibl>." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/4e4417b6851631abcb845db9139e71554fd35fec659f70ff5516b181629ff61e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Fighting hoplites. The standing warrior at left faces right and
      wears a cuirass, greaves, a short chiton with white rosettes, and a stilted helmet with a
      white crest. He carries a spear in his right hand; his chest strap is white as is the tip of
      the scabbbard. The warrior at right faces left and wears a short tunic with white dots at edge
      and white rosettes. The helmet crest, chest band, and scabbard tip are white. His shield
      device is a white vertical line with two horizontal crosses and there are red dots around the
      rim. The fallen warrior wears a helmet with white dots on the crest, greaves and a cuirass.
      His shield device is a white feline head (?) between white dots. His eyes are closed. White
      palmettes on the shield strap are visible on the fallen and left-hand warriors'
      shields.</P><P>A checkerboard pattern at the mouth, a band of five palmettes and a
      meander band below further decorate the vessel. At the sides of the scene are ivy leaf bands.
      There is a double red band below the scene.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/4e4bf45f2d282faa282d729c65016735780795dff3952bdc1c5d38ecaba586e1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Tondo: A satyr dances in front of a table that supports a kantharos<lb>Side A:
      Youths draped in himatia, holding staffs; a seated youth holds a lyre<lb>Side B: Youths,
      draped, sitting and standing"""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

