<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/5405582392656d573eb627d21e8e75368e771b1084413f621623629764eea439> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Panther, griffin-bird, bird, panther. The figures proceed in
      both directions from the handle and converge under the spout, the panthers tails overlapping
      just to the left of the handle. The panthers are shown in profile, with frontal heads.
      Incisions delineate important anatomical features. In front of each panther there is another
      creature, a griffin-bird on the left confronting a bird on the right. Both are in
      profile.</P><P>The spout, neck, handle, and shoulder are covered with black glaze.
      The shoulder is further decorated with vertical strokes of added white and pairs of incised
      lines radiating from the junction between neck and shoulder. The panel containing figured
      decoration runs continuously around the body. The figures are large and fill up the space
      easily, with the little remaining area in the field given over to dots and hastily incised
      rosettes.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

