<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/568347e6e7f53a335b1fee279a351c4087a7f53c09d922222c68937ab3237386> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Head of Persephone with flower diadem."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/568728656d46c9fbc57b4006d592936ffc9e3f70bb95e024f67a318af4c96a3e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Athena is depicted
      standing to the right, holding a writing tablet opened in her left hand and a stylos raised in
      her right. A red ribbon hangs from the opened lid of the tablet. The goddess is wearing a long
      chiton with a red belt, the aegis, helmet and earrings. Her large shield embellished with a
      club is leaning against her right thigh.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: An infibulated athlete is standing frontally, his head turned to the right. He
      holds a spear in his right hand, his left is resting against his hip.</P><P>Both
      figures are standing on a short band of meanders, interrupted by fields decorated with a
      cross. Poland-Reisinger-Wagner suggest that Athena is depicted contemplating what to write
      onto the tablet. Lullies interprets the gesture of the raised hand holding the stylus as an
      indication that Athena has already conceived of an idea and is now beginning to write it
      down.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

