    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/5a2728a7bf1e23f8c01948ad862a1d501ccfdba4ca82475bbe6689f3fc12e3a4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Nude, standing male figure, with left leg is slightly advanced"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/5a2a360d8021a551f311b644a6e049294d143a766db808a3558d9fc6ff0ba4d3> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: A nude young komast,
      his arms extended to left and right, prances to the right, a staff held horizontally in his
      right hand, like a spear. He seems to halt and draw back, as though spying the youth on Side
      B. <hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: A nude young komast, his arms extended to right
      and left, is walking to the right but looking back to the left. He holds a gnarled staff
      vertically in his left hand; a short cloak is draped over both arms. He may be looking back at
      the youth on Side A. Like the former, he has a line across his right ankle, possibly an
      anklet.</P><P>Beneath each handle is a single, upright palmette. From this,
      scrolling tendrils emerge on either side to enclose palmettes which frame the figures. The
      interior is all black. The inside of the handles and the space between the roots are reserved.
      There is a black band around the underside of the foot and a pair of concentric circles in the
      center. The side of the foot is reserved. A reserved stripe around the lower body serves as
      groundline.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/5a2bd98d543d735b5ade502189e5c46b8c9ac4abf0932c1818d7d15eae164b80> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Karouzou 1968, 150, pl. 47b</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/5a2efec3f76ad85c995086ce561fe810e9bc4e6954f963903beb7d6d346004db> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Votive stele to Apollo"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/5a3f537866f9ef79f0f99806b5f6a5a6eb865b90dbd1fdfdeeccedc089ff61c7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Athena attacks a
      fallen giant (Enkelados, according to Walters). Athena and the giant are shown between the
      painted "eyes"; she is on the left, and lunges toward the giant on the right. She wears a
      helmet and carries her shield in her left hand; she is dressed in an embroidered peplos and
      chiton. The giant is in a half sitting position, with his right leg flexed. The background is
      filled in with tree branches.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Same
      as Side A, but the giant has a Corinthian helmet and a white embroidered chlamys. Under each
      handle, a dolphin is depicted.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Int.</hi>: A
      potter sits at his potter's wheel. Above him are stacks of vases on a shelf, four kylikes and
      a jug. In the exergue is a dog. Drawing and incising on all the vase is extremely
      crude.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

