<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/5b82d6e98a58bfac51a6d3b3d55cb3a99ae4a127485916f0a2154accd075d662> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Shoulder:</hi> Horseman and
      charioteer with a quadriga race at a gallop to the right. The bearded charioteer leans forward
      over the horses, holding his reins with his left hand and his whip with his right. He wears a
      long white chiton. Behind comes the horseman with his long hair flowing, wearing a short white
      chiton, holding the reins with his left hand and plying his whip with his right. Behind the
      horseman is the meta (starting point). On the far right is a bearded brabeus (judge), facing
      left and watching the race as he leans on a staff with his right hand gesturing at the
      participants. He wears a striped himation. Above this panel is a frieze of circumscribed
      tongues. On the sides is a crenellated pattern. Chariot scenes occur frequently in the
      repertoire of the Euphiletos Painter.</P><P>On the main panel a Dionysiac thiasos
      is depicted with the god in the center, facing right, holding his kantharos in his right hand
      and a branching vine in his left. Behind him a bearded satyr plays the double flute as he
      walks to the right. At the far right another bearded satyr plays the kithara which is edged
      with added white to simulate ivory. Between this satyr and Dionysos, a maenad dances wildly to
      the right, while looking back toward the god. She plays krotala (clappers) with both hands and
      wears a wreath over her long hair, a long striped chiton, and a pardalis (leopard skin)
      knotted at her throat. At the far left is the other maenad who also dances, facing right. She
      wears her long hair with an ivy wreath, a peplos, and a short garment round her middle,
      embroidered and bordered with a meander, from which issues a snake. She carries a deer on her
      shoulders, holding the legs close with both arms. Across upper edge of the main panel runs the
      inscription, <foreign lang="Greek">*P*A*N*F*A*I*O*S *M*E*P*O*I*S*E*N</foreign>,
      "Pamphaios made me." Along the sides of the panels there are borders of embattled
      pattern.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Predella:</hi> A lion, moving to the
      right confronts a boar, facing left. Behind each of them is a
      palmette.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/5b8803bbb891a799a2764758929ae5926e1a17dc73bd197b89859fbd96ebc49b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
