<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/61f12c3603a9e6ddce028f084a86a55c602f72ed37862821bf017901b32bd14c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A black man stands with his back to the viewer and arms
      extended. His feet point to the right, while his head is in profile to the left. In his right
      hand he holds a bow, and in his left a mallet(?). He wears pants with wide legs, decorated
      with vertical stripes and rows of dots, and a long-sleeved top, belted at the waist. Over his
      arms and across his back is draped a mantle. To his right is a small stool and a palm
      tree.</P><P>Fraser (42) notes that this is the typical pose for figures in this
      group of alabastra.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/61f53bf1fd11c43b36a6b8178f87000a15917d3f6d39adc4d36689cc4a9d2b15> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Broken and repaired, with many missing fragments restored and repainted. The
      foot is modern. "Now augmented by fragments ex Philadelphia recognized by Payne."
      (ABV)</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

