<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6822e009de0b6469fdfaba4ddc072e872f086a074d64e0fdd3d96b84f2a78b68> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Interior: Dionysos and satyr. Side A and B: maenads dancing at the image of
      Dionysos."""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6823987b4c0ef9f012cfc55af5bfaa7657102bab2febbb953b9263f44bc790eb> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Shoulder</hi>: combat of Herakles
      and Kyknos (?). Herakles, followed by Iolaos, advances on Kyknos and Ares. Athena separates
      the two groups. Herakles wears a short chiton and lionskin, his sword on his left side. Iolaos
      is fully armed, with Boeotian shield and spear. Kyknos and Ares are fully armed, and wear
      visored helmets, short chitons, spears and Boeotian shields. Kyknos' shield has a palmette and
      lotus flower device, Ares' has the forepart of a winged lion.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Body</hi>: women drawing water at fountain house. The fountainhouse is a
      Doric portico with five waterspouts (lions and equestrian figures). The spouts pour water into
      five hydriae (of differing shapes) standing on blocks. Four women draw water, labelled
      <foreign lang="Greek">*I*O*P*E, *R*O*D*O*P*I*S, *K*L*E*O</foreign> ("Iope,
      Rhodopis, Kleo"). Iope holds a wreath or strap for lifting the hydria; the unlabelled woman is
      about to place a wreath or strap on one of the spouts. All wear long chitons. In the field,
      branches. Below main scene, animal frieze of lions and boars. Under foot, graffito or
      ligature.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/68331fdfc8a060a1ae19dc74f7a6edf87e2c217bb1f92f90b10be3f6222d87c8> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
