<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/69357834beb7cc6b5deb8e96ff9b2e0b5e1dfde53d3c1ff75398cf9c4dbc0573> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A cock stands on an exergue to right. In background are two
      lotus blossoms. In the exergue a fox runs to the right. There are chevrons on the ground line.
      There is a band of dicing between lines and a band of tongues around the outer rim. On the
      bottom are concentric circles.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/693e27fcb6f828ee7b9d545da7ecf4c6bb55e3e64be93e03c5bfb9b0cd45117d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Boardman 1995, fig. 10.4</bibl>; <bibl>Stewart 1990, fig. 459</bibl>; <bibl>Karouzou 1968, 103</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/694452aac24d903379786b99403be0250c2da5af1c3dc5fbd7429b448effd5ff> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: A woman stands with
      her head in profile to the right, holding an oinochoe in her right hand and a mirror in her
      raised left. She wears her hair in a bun, with a wreath on her head, a necklace, bracelets,
      and a long sleeveless chiton, girt at the waist. To the right is a laver set on a base, with
      several laurel branches growing around it, and a propped-up phiale. Eros hovers over it,
      facing right, with his right foot touching it and his left one raised (apparently resting on a
      rock behind the laver). He holds out a wreath over the bull rider's head, and a fruit and
      necklace in his other hand. He is nude, but wears a wreath, bracelets, and strings of beads
      over his left shoulder and around his right thigh. Next, a man-faced bull walks to the left.
      It has the body and horns of a bull, with a bearded man's face. On it is seated a woman,
      wearing a sleeveless chiton, necklace, and wreath in her hair, which is also in a bun. She
      daintily holds one of the bull's horns with her right hand, and balances a hydria on her knee
      with the other. Above her head to the right is a veiled head in a window, looking at the
      scene. A fillet hangs from the window. The oinochoe, mirror, laver, bull's horns, veiled face,
      and hydria are painted white. It has been suggested that this is Dionysos in the form of a
      bull, bringing Semele (his mother) back from Hades (Walters, 99). The veiled face is similar
      to those from Greek sepulchral reliefs, and is suggestive of the Underworld. On the neck of
      the vessel is a Siren in profile to the left, with hair in a bun, wearing a wreath and a
      necklace. Above and below it are phialae.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: Two youths stand facing each other. They wear wreaths and himatia. The one on
      the left has a branch in his right hand and a fruit and necklace in his left. The other youth
      holds fruit. Between the two figures is a tendril, and above that, a window. Behind each youth
      is a fillet and a phiale. On the neck of the vessel is a female head to the left, with hair in
      a bun, wearing an embroidered cap, beaded fillet, and necklace.</P><P>On the neck
      of the vessel is a wave pattern. On the shoulder is a flower with leaves on either side (Side
      A) and a tongue pattern (Side B). Below the handles are palmettes, and running below the
      figural design on both sides is a wave pattern.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6946ad59a1db5253652327490f3c3f78595a0ce805d867e7b1a54e53173a00f3> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Tondo: reveler<lb>Sides A and B: youths and horses"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6959e95d2bdb1a377d3c321634fb8aff9694ba5f1d34aaa7b2a1d6cb7d48d148> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Richter 1970c, fig. 72</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/697efe0ca54c64430aef089e214c6f89634fe113e66293c877df9e0dce993d24> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> a trainer in himation
      and white fillet stands to right holding a forked staff. Facing him is a youth with white
      fillet taking off his himation.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B:</hi> a
      youth in a himation leans to left on a staff.</P><P>There is an ovulo base line on
      Side A, a reserved line on Side B.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

