<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6a2dfa99f7d10cd35b3702919dfa2a1d94d86364e99e54a6c4ab7ec06f1dcef1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Clairmont 1993, 3.376 no. 3.446</bibl>; <bibl>Vermeule & Comstock 1988, no. 8</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6a35f4866a94f77a0f47becb44608fa5c63eed109c7e577e61de6de998725cdb> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A</hi>: departure of young
      horseman. In the center, a stallion stands in profile to the right, a youth behind him. The
      youth, wearing a chlamys and with a petasos hanging behind his back, is leaning on his staff
      and looking toward a second youth and an older, bearded man standing to the left. Another
      youth and bearded man stand talking on the right. The youth on the left stands facing forward,
      but looks toward the horseman on the right, leaning on the staff in his right hand. The older
      man on the far left is leaning on a staff tucked under his left arm and gestures with that
      hand, his right hand on his hip. Both men wear short mantles. The bearded man to the right of
      the horse stands in profile to the right, his right arm held straight out at shoulder height.
      His staff is held off the ground in his left hand. The youth he addresses faces forward but
      turns his head to listen, his staff tucked behind one bent knee and his right hand on his hip.
      His left hand rests limp-wristed on his staff. A shield hangs on the far right in its shield
      case, a scabbard below it. A writing case hangs on the far left, a stylus tied underneath
      around its middle.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B</hi>: departure of
      young horseman. The horse and youth in the center are almost identical in pose and dress to
      those on side A, except that the youth leans on a spear rather than a staff. Again, another
      youth and an older, bearded man stand to the left. Two more youths are involved in a
      discussion on the right. These figures echo the poses of those on side A, with small
      differences. On side B, the youth to the left of the horseman has his staff tucked under his
      left arm and is gesturing toward the horseman with his right hand. He is draped in a
      calf-length mantle. The older man on the far left is virtually identical to the older man on
      side A. The youth standing to the right of the horse stands facing left talking to the third
      youth. He is leaning forward as he gestures with his left hand, his right arm held at his
      waist, and his staff resting at his side. His companion stands facing him leaning on his
      staff, his weight on one leg and one arm held out limp-wristed at waist level. Both youths
      wear knee-length mantles. Again, a shield in its shield case hangs on the far right with a
      scabbard below. A money purse hangs on the far left.</P><P><hi
      rend="head">Interior</hi>: youth pursuing a girl to the right. A youth has surprised
      a young woman at an altar. He is running after the girl and has just grabbed her around the
      neck. He holds up his mantle with his left hand, baring his body. The girl, dressed in a
      chiton and himation, runs away, but has turned her head to look at the youth. She is holding
      her himation at her waist with one hand, while holding up the hem with her other hand. There
      is a white fillet tied around her head. On the far left, behind the youth, the edge of an
      altar is visible.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6a4ee5149caf2c9993437df7719d9b600021145f505db2cc7514dd371c34d735> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
