    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6a7c6c13521d24a4e9e017caec8d331feebb4b807c59cb9118902c77c3d59d96> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> Presumably during the
      Calydonian boar hunt, the boar on the left is being speared by three hunters: a man wearing a
      fillet and carrying a wrap on his arm, and two youths, both naked except for the fillet one of
      them wears. The boar is also attacked by a black dog which digs his hind claws into the boar's
      flank. The scene is reconstructed with this dog also biting the boar's neck, though his head
      is not part of these fragments. There is another dog, this one white, biting and clawing at
      the boar's hindquarters. The boar is clearly fatally wounded, as there is blood pouring from
      all his wounds, and he collapses to the right.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B:</hi> A wounded stag with a spear embedded in his back is in the center between two
      hunters on horseback. Due to the fragmentary nature, little is left of the stag or rider
      confronting him.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Interior:</hi> Swan to the
      right.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

