<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6c7f20210288095f4f253785623fda25057da32de70c0909066b36be5e7b1335> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Added purple appears on the bird's beak as well as the lions' eyes,
      shoulder, and belly; added white appears on the bird's beak and the lions' manes. At the back
      the tails of the lions intertwine and another rosette appears above the back of the left
      lion.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6c7fd067db7541a59a97f3b3b2620a97e0fb80946876e076ef02a118fea7c4c5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Two-storied Doric stoa; on the north side of the agora."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6c888c4157c005034a21eb9f1f76c57670aaede20862d3d024ce75dd6d150540> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A</hi>: Dionysos and Ariadne
      in a chariot. The four-horse chariot is depicted frontally, so that Dionysos and Ariadne are
      hidden behind the two central horses. Only the tops of their heads can be seen. They turn away
      from each other, Dionysos on the right and Ariadne on the left. Both wear vine wreaths, and
      vines laden with bunches of grapes spring from their shoulders and trail down the sides of the
      chariot. The two central horses turn their heads toward one another, their muzzles crossed.
      The two outside horses look to the outside.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side
      B</hi>: Dionysos with satyrs and maenad. Dionysos stands in the center facing right, his
      head turned toward the satyr and maenad on the left. He wears a long white chiton and a black
      mantle draped over his left shoulder. He has a long beard and, like the maenad and satyrs,
      wears a wreath of vines on his head. A long-horned goat stands behind his legs facing right. A
      satyr and maenad approach from the left, the maenad nearest to Dionysos. She is holding
      fan-like objects in her raised hands. She wears a chiton and himation. The satyr approaches
      with head slightly bowed, his left hand raised in a gesture of greeting or respect. The satyr
      on the right plays the double flute, head tilted back. His flute pouch(?) hangs from his left
      arm.</P><P>There is a palmette lotus chain on the neck of the amphora, and
      palmettes and a pendant lotus under the handles.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6c8c5269d51364d9644d8a9f69481c81b767e22154a060596e04eab723d9f074> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Hind legs of two horses, advancing to the left"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

