<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6e0cc474eb417c1b05efa0300d9e3245d54d70d9727b5e26d1822b5a9593b311> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Achilles and a wounded Penthesilea"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6e1b9f49502d0418d3c1eb596c65fd7a3a7e747f8a8f90ce7d1e0fa537719a5a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The neck and shoulder are decorated with bands of lotus and
      palmette. Above the shoulder decoration is another band of alternating red and black tongues.
      The main panel is bordered below the groundline by buds and tendrils interspersed with dots.
      Beneath this pattern are flamelike tongues that extend down to the body-base join. The base,
      handles and rim are black. Below the handle joins are large palmette, bud, and spiral
      patterns.</P><P>On side A, Theseus is fighting the Minotaur in the center, while a
      youth and a girl look on from either side. Theseus is naked, with a headband and a strap over
      his right shoulder, presumably to hold his scabbard. With his left hand he grasps the sinking
      Minotaur, and with his right hand he brandishes his sword. The Minotaur has fallen to his left
      knee. He holds stones in both hands, the right raised to throw. Blood flows from his upper
      right arm where the sword has wounded him. The two maidens, whose skin is white, each wear
      ankle-length, shortsleeved chitons. The lefthand one's garment is mostly black on top, with
      red sleeves and underarms, with a skirt that is red to the knees, where it is decorated by
      white lines and dots, and then continues to the ankles in black. The righthand figure's chiton
      has vertical red and black stripes above and below. The shirt hem is decorated with white
      dots, as is the hem of the long skirt. Both maidens have red headbands. The youths who stand
      to the far left and far right, are both naked. The youth on the left has a red headband, while
      the righthand youth has red hair.</P><P>On side B, two armed warriors duel with
      spears in the center, while a woman and man look on. The lefthand warrior is wearing a short
      red chiton with white dots on the hem, a cuirass, a greave on his left leg, a white strap over
      his right shoulder from which his sword scabbard is suspended, a masked, low-crested helmet.
      In his right hand he wields his spear; in his left is a round shield visible from its
      interior. The righthand warrior is dressed similarly to his opponent, without a cuirass, and
      with a high crest on his helmet instead of a low crest. With his opposite pose, this warrior's
      shield device is fully visible, four white and three red balls. The male onlooker on the far
      left has an ankle-length garment striped diagonally in broad red and black stripes. Its hem is
      dotted in white. The woman on the far right wears a shortsleeved, ankle-length chiton, the
      skirt red with a wavy white line decorating the hem. The blouse is covered with vertical black
      and red stripes, and dotted in white at its hem. The woman also has a red headband. In her
      right she holds a wreath. There is an ambiguous inscription in the field behind the warriors'
      legs.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6e24b1fdd68dfa0e3af8134d3ce59a25c8cc0f11a3400795fa92aeb0c0d0f549> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The decorated areas are coated with a pale, creamy slip, over
      which the designs are painted in dark brown slip, fired red or black in places. Covering the
      body are three decorative friezes separated by broad stripes. The first, which fills most of
      the shoulder, has four geese, nestled low on the groundline so that their feet are not
      represented. They are in two pairs, back to back, so that the middle two face each other on
      the front, separated by a large filling ornament in the form of a swastika with coiled tips.
      Throughout the background are other filling ornaments, including concentric circles surrounded
      by dots, dotted quatrefoils, and crosses with T-shaped crossbars on the arms. Pendant from the
      upper border and rising from the groundline are hatched semi-circles and cross-hatched
      triangles. In typical East Greek style, the birds are drawn in outline, with no use of
      incision as on Attic black-figure. In the middle frieze is a row of grazing goats, with black
      bodies and outlined heads, shoulders, and bellies. They are clearly billy goats (i.e. male),
      and have beards, long ears, short tails, and long arching horns. The background is cluttered
      with assorted filling ornaments like those in the upper frieze. The lower body of the vessel
      is filled with large lotus flowers alternating with lotus buds, all with dark centers and
      reserved edges. Around the neck is a broad cable pattern with dotted centers. Band of crude
      tongues around the upper shoulder. Mouth, foot, and handle are
      black.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

