<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6fec03b3a381a0d30c3577ee1800ef9ae497da4309498bcde8160f04f4a426e1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Peitho (labelled) standing profile to the left, wearing a himation
      draped over her left shoulder, over a sleeved chiton, and a sakkos, holds a phiale and above
      it a large alabastron (hung from cord by small square fastening) in her hand (her left hand is
      obscured by the himation). She faces a nude, winged Himeros (labelled) seated on a rock
      profile to the left, with his right foot slightly advanced, wearing a narrow, white taenia,
      who holds a torch (?) in his right hand, and rests his left hand on his
      lap.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6ff1a958813ca6dfb94f344eeb12c9778300e912c728e79683f7e0b35bfb759d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Svoronos 1903-12, 460, pl. 76 (with previous bibliography)</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6ff8f972b6343df3da1b73cb7ac792496b5f8f503cdc9d7cd7b3ddac80257bb0> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Late Archaic peripteral temple dedicated to Athena, located on high ground in the northern sector of the city. Also known as the \"Temple of Ceres.\""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/6ff92e1e9446cc18824453bb810dfafc37d43d3a4c1338798169cd9adf27ca5e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Stele depicting a standing, nude youth"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/7001c42ce0c5fe2e0f364d2ab5063747615d195e09cf867302ff88dc47beeb05> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Plain band and bands of geometric ornament decorate the vase.
      The widest band is situated just under the widest part of the vase and is decorated with a
      triple zig-zag pattern. Plain black bands and narrow bands decorated with rows of dots
      complete the decoration. The lid is decorated with black lines and bands, and one narrow band
      decorated with a row of black dots. The knob is striped with fine black
      lines.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/700250524788e4777727748bf995b55ea66d71fabc0241c04b842e662671548a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Demosthenes with his characteristic short, curly hair, bushy eyebrows and mustache, short, trimmed beard, and furrowed brow"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/7003220bb987504761c018ce5c2f30fbbd56bca982b466375e99acfa936c27bb> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>On the inside of the vessel, the tondo is decorated with a
      glaze dot and two concentric circles, one broad and one narrow. On the outside, the decoration
      runs in a band at the handle zone.<hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Five pairs of
      kneeling men and youths are depicted. Their hair, and the beards of the men, are painted red.
      All of them except the last figure on the left (head missing) hold fighting cocks under their
      arms or on their laps. The combs, wattles, wing coverts, necks, tail feathers, and bodies of
      the cocks are painted red. On the ground between the first couple on the left is a hare.
      Between the third and also the fourth pair is a hen. In the field around the figures are dots,
      suggesting pseudo inscriptions.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>:
      There are five pairs of kneeling males; all except the first on the left are holding cocks.
      The third pair from the left is two youths, and the fourth pair is a youth and bearded man.
      The head of one member of each of the other pairs is missing, but there remain two youths from
      the first and last couples and a bearded man from the second. The mock inscriptions in the
      field around the figures contain some actual letters.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/70032c996dc5dc13c39f670145c3e7d6c5b13e0318df70c85dee7c155382c62d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>At front center, Dionysos (but with pointed ears) rides an
      ithyphallic donkey to right. He wears a white chitoniskos and a red-striped cloak. Grape vines
      emanate from Dionysos. The reins on the donkey are rendered as grape vines. Before him at
      right, a satyr dances to right with upraised arms. At left, another satyr approaches the
      donkey from behind and lays his left hand on his rump, an amorous gesture. On either side of
      cup are white eyes with black outlines and pronounced tear ducts. Iris and pupils are rendered
      by three concentric circles, middle ring is red. Behind the eyes flanking the handle are two
      nude komasts wearing boots and each holding a kantharos. The one to the left of the handle is
      missing his head and left arm. The one to the right has lost a forearm. The one to the right
      has satyr ears but no tail. All beards are red.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/7005beda4eb79efc36ea83dccdeafd5bea438828d244ae9d6f7e3e6a27c79128> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<P>Foot chipped, surface worn. Some misfiring.</P>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/7009672f1f9f5cb2f67f253de60195c4e0dc6030972ab14fd735af9e48d5c648> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
