<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/746e80059a2969afc0b6914dd39aa28b8eb33310ff664e53900dfadaf3aca4ce> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """An owl, wearing a crest, and carrying a spear and shield, advances to the right, toward
      an olive frond that springs from the ground"""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/747105ccbc1d3720476c803a92eaf3ace8618dd6c07986be7d7b38c0baa9afcf> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> Two nude men,
      confronted. The beardless youth on the left wears his hair long with a long forelock and holds
      two cocks in his hands. The bearded man on the right approaches, offerings a leashed dog. What
      is being shown is the presentation of love gifts by the <hi
      rend="ital">erastes</hi> or older lover to the <hi
      rend="ital">eromenos</hi> or youthful beloved. This is called by Beazley, Beta, the
      second stage of courtship as shown in Attic vase-painting.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Side B:</hi> Similar scene. The bearded man on the left strides forward
      and offers the youth a stag while he reaches up to caress the youth's forehead. The beardless
      youth wears his hair long with two long forelocks in front of his ears and stands on the right
      holding two cocks.</P><P>On the neck is an intertwining palmette lotus. Under the
      handles is a bold design of spirals with accessory palmettes and lotus buds. Below the designs
      is a band of lotus buds and rays at the junction of the foot. Accessories are in red; and
      incised lines are used sparingly for anatomical details.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/747d6c8dedd305b18aa37acb72019af19a7ac79fbd1716cc8f2f5c692f77d96f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
