<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/75c6980d0060c7b2d328d514dd0d80e65ca302eac289ec8312c25d03662ec428> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Main panel:</hi> animal frieze.
      Four pairs of confronted animals and monsters share this space, with floral ornament between.
      Sphinxes, goats, cocks, and lions cover the space, with a small standing bird between the
      cocks and the lions. The floral ornaments vary in complexity from the relatively simple design
      between the lions, to one much more complicated between the sphinxes. Above the animals' backs
      and below their tails are incised rosettes and two lotus buds. Above the main panel, from the
      neck down, the vessel is covered with bands of upright buds, pendent lotus buds and blossoms,
      pomegranates. Below the main panel are seen a stopped meander, upright lotus buds and
      blossoms, rays, and widely separated stroke pairs as well as tongues on the
      foot.</P><P>Added red is seen on the birds and animals and floral ornaments, as
      well as the lotus buds and blossoms in the main panel. Most details of the figures here are
      incised.</P><P>The vessel's interior is fully glazed. The outer face of the rim is
      reserved, while the upper rounded surface is glazed. The strap handles are flanged. A double
      fillet separates mouth from neck, the upper glazed, the lower reserved. Another fillet is
      found at the base of the neck, and a third between the foot and the body. The underside of the
      vessel is reserved and unslipped.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/75c703ea36e0eadf894b43754d26e4d94d682633793b58f57cac6d55c4972c4b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
