<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/7bba891376d4fcdde0c20739578670d3e1a4a2f53128fc0cfbba8d2147bb6073> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """A: Philia (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the right, wearing a belted
      peplos, an ivy wreath, a long pony-tail, holds a barbiton in her left hand and a thyrsos
      diagonally in her lowered right hand; Satyra (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the right, her
      head turned profile to the left, wearing a sleeveless chiton, a himation draped and clasped
      over her right shoulder, hair in a bun, a red taenia, an ivy wreath tied with white string,
      holds an oinochoe in her lowered right hand, and a kantharos in her upraised left hand;
      Eupolis (labelled), a nude, balding, boy satyr, walking profile to the right, wearing an ivy
      crown, tilts his head back and holds a torch at waist level with both hands; before him is an
      attenuated Doric column.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

