    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<P><bibl>Comstock & Vermeule 1976, no. 154</bibl> (with previous bibliography)</P>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/81a677d3d0d0072ae737def376819726ca52a18cb0b51104e5dd7e39de1d50f5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Three nude Theban youths with red hair run to the right, the
      leader looking back to the left. They are fleeing the sphinx who attacks from the left, her
      forepaws raised. She has a white face and breast, and red and white stripes on her wings. She
      wears a red fillet. Lotus buds appear on the shoulder.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/81b1261cbeb2ce0b4fdec160c60ce5f499e20db0aecff085d90262fcf92eb3f1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Scene of women playing
      music. In the middle of the scene a woman sits on a chair, holding a lyre and flanked by women
      standing on either side. Eros comes flying from the right. Behind her a woman is standing at
      left, resting her left hand on the back of the chair. The woman at right holds in her right
      hand the double pipes (<hi rend="ital">aulos</hi>) and in her left a
      cradle-kithara. She is dressed in belted peplos. Between her and the seated woman, Eros, naked
      and with wings, like a little child, is flying to the left into the scene. There are diverse
      objects around the room: a chair, an open box between the seated woman and the woman at right,
      and, on the wall, are hanging several objects like a taenia and a crosslike instrument of
      unknown meaning and use.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Three
      youths in the palaestra. Three young men draped in himatia talk in the palaestra. The one at
      left carries a strigil and the one at right opens his hand showing a astragalos (knucklebone
      used in games). All of them hold knotted sticks. Hanging on the wall between them is a bag for
      the astragaloi.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/81b38d99f4941480a8cde8e2f890d28bf4599c0afb84f2d51ca267acb4ed38a4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Tondo: Dionysos before altar<lb>Sides A and B: dancing satyrs and
      maenads"""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

