<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8459072bed8917cd650c0b1f33f526da44ad34fb67a47e84135bf61739ad6424> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> Athena stands to the
      right, facing left. Her head, waist, and feet are shown in profile, while her shoulders are
      frontal. She holds her shield with her left hand and raises a spear high above her head with
      her right. She wears a helmet, the high crest of which overlaps the upper border of the panel,
      the shield bears the device of a dolphin, facing left. She wears a peplos in added red with
      incised meanders, girt at the waist with a broad girdle, over which hangs an overfold with
      meander borders, and an aegis with a fringe of snakes. Her face and arms are in added white
      for female flesh. In front of her is inscribed in retrograde, <foreign
      lang="Greek">*T*O*N *A*Q*E*N*E*Q[*E]*N *A*Q*L*O*N *E*M*I</foreign>, "I am one of the
      prizes from Athens." On the neck of Side A is a siren which faces right with its left wing
      advanced and its right wing stretched out behind.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B:</hi> The <hi rend="ital">synoris</hi>, a cart race with a team of two
      horses or mules, indicates the event for which the winner won the prize. A beardless driver in
      a light cart on the left drives on a pair of horses on the right in a race to the right. The
      driver sits with his feet resting on a foot board in the front of the car. He wears a
      sleeveless chiton in added red. He holds a goad in his right hand and a kalaurops (a long rod
      from which hang two pointed metal objects to incite the horses with their jingling). The
      horses are yoked to a transverse bar fastened to the pole; their yokes are those customarily
      used for mules. The wheels are those of cart not a chariot with no spokes, but a diametrical
      bar crossed by two at right angles. On the neck of side B is an owl with frontal face, facing
      right, its right wing stretched out, its left wing down. on the lower body is a band of
      rays.</P><P>Inside it were found cremated bones and six small vases: a
      black-figure lekythos, a plain hand-made jug, and four black glaze vessels, funerary offerings
      for the man who had presumably won one of the most prestigious games at the Panathenaic
      festival. This is the earliest known Panathenaic amphora.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/84679c07ba11c4d2f9276571d96f7314a8ec172d803a96a5bb27dffa9dc4aee5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Ext. Side A: Zeus, Poseidon, and Hades between Pegasi. Side B: Demeter, Hermes,
      Persephone, Pluto (or Dionysos?), vine branch. Int.: Nike."""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8483605e2676ab09aa76f44f3badd1878f8e1e73c12b64860b621de3b1ae1a20> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
