<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/895e2be2a9e62dd9583a63b4dabad763181af464e43681c851986540f5c394ef> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Burke & Pollitt 1975, 1 no. 1 (ill.)</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8960dc4af6eb8bba9003ae7cffb6be2874b2fd6b8442984bd6f2c7dcddbec128> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Boardman 1995, fig. 18.1</bibl>; <bibl>Waywell 1978, 16ff., 85f.</bibl>; <bibl>Cook 1976, 135-36, fig. 106</bibl>." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/896566fa9191aa0c12230df320811b21727348fd07211c40a361e01c168d25f5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Goose or swan, standing profile to the right (only head
      preserved); Chryse (labelled), standing near frontal, slightly to the left, with her weight on
      her right leg, and her left knee bent, wearing a belted peplos, a sphendone, black necklace,
      dotted-hoop earrings, and a black band on each wrist, looks down at the bird, and holds her
      right hand just above the bird, and holds her left arm down and back; Eunomia (labelled),
      standing 3/4-view to the left, wearing a belted, sleeved chiton with a kolpos, a white taenia,
      a short pony tail, black hoop earrings, a black necklace, and black bands on each wrist, holds
      a flower (?) in her left hand, at waist level, and a beaded necklace (?) in her upraised right
      hand; Eukleia (labelled), standing profile to the right, wearing a belted peplos, a sphendone
      with a wreath, a black necklace, black leaf-shaped earrings, and a black band on each wrist,
      raises her left foot on a rock, and holding a necklace between her upraised right hand and her
      lowered left hand, to a female figure, perhaps Nikopolis (labelled); a small deer (?) moving
      profile to the right; "Nikopolis" seated near profile to the right, head profile to the left,
      wearing a belted peplos, a black necklace, a sphendone with a wreath, and a black (?) band on
      her right wrist, rests her right hand on a rock, and her left hand on her lap; a laurel (?)
      branch.</P><P>The name of the fourth female figure has been alternatively read as
      Nike, Aike, Dike, or Nikopolis.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8974c0cfe503b8cab682e80c0a2d46aeda8b03523044686e472c20697ae35fc0> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Exterior:</hi> unpainted, except
      for a thin black line at the lower edge. On the exterior is a roughly engraved inscription in
      large characters <foreign lang="Greek">*A*I*T*I</foreign>, perhaps part of a
      dedication <foreign lang="Greek">*O *D*E*I*N*A *M*E *A*N*E*Q*H*K*E *K]*A*I *T[*H*N
      *P*R*O*X*O*U*N</foreign>, cf. <bibl>Naukratis, i, pl. 32,
      1</bibl>.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Interior:</hi> Symposium. A male
      figure reclines to the right on a cushion. He looks right and extends his left arm in the same
      direction as if engaged in conversation with a missing symposiast on the right. Sporting a
      wreath in added red he holds a dotted phiale in his right hand. With frontal chest and profile
      face and hips, he wears a himation decorated with crosses, tied about his
      waist.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8975f2ad59479014ee58a200c21b04431bca4ae55fb3df2347b042d3b4803c17> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Kyrieleis 1996, 6 no. 1, pl. 6.1</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/897bd4a7d574f06f3c4e73c064be6e9f10187519ce1b22ff8b727bcb8b908b0c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Sirius; head and shoulders of a dog"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/898f3f7fdd3851e5f82bfa6f662e8c38d6da4449fd5426f49155071395315591> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: A winged Eros is
      seated on a rock (?). He is in profile to the right, sitting in a slumped-over position. He
      has a necklace or chain of some type looped over his left shoulder, then down across his chest
      and under his right arm. He wears bracelets and anklets painted white, and a white wreath in
      his hair. His wings are also highlighted with white paint. He holds a phiale containing white
      fruit or eggs in his left hand.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: A
      woman sits on a chair which has crossed legs. Her legs are in profile to the right, but she
      twists her upper body around to look toward the left; her right arm is stretched out behind
      her in this turn, and a necklace dangles from her hand. In her left hand, she holds a platter.
      She wears a mantle which is only draped around the lower part of her body, and her hair is
      held up in a bun.</P><P>The shoulder of the vessel is decorated with ivy leaves
      outlined in white, with incised stems and clusters of berries (a favorite decorative pattern
      of this painter, <bibl>Trendall 1967, 597</bibl>). The upper border of the figural
      panel is two rows of alternate checks, and the lower border is a wave pattern. There are
      palmettes under the handles.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

