    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8b6921a3f1b608578fa6e582b75058e0f9f04339331b83af88e37d79309f0443> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> youth (Theseus?)
      running to right, pursuing maiden on side B. He runs right with both arms extended, in hot
      pursuit of the woman on Side B. The youth wears a himation around his neck and shoulders and
      high boots, but is otherwise nude. He has short curly locks in front and a mass of hair in
      back. Behind him are two spears, points down. <hi rend="ital">Side B:</hi> maiden
      fleeing youth on side A. She runs to right, looking back over her shoulder. She wears a long
      Ionic style chiton with loose elbow sleeves and a himation, the end of which is folded over
      her right shoulder and has a striped border. She has draped the himation over her left forearm
      to enable her to run faster. On her head she wears a sakkos or snood and earrings. Her right
      arm is outstretched, palm up; in her left hand she holds a branch with two spiral tendrils
      ending in a lotus bud. Both figures seem to walk on a reserved ground
      line.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8b6e7b21d9283cd619609f6fac8b2b92715ee8252ddcd828877f25048f8d8a5d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>At the left, a youth wearing a wreath and draped in a himation
      leans on his staff while viewing the sacrifice made by a similarly clad youth in the center.
      He pours a libation from a cup onto an altar with added white flames and an object. At the
      right, a nude youth seen from the back wearing a wreath holds a spit with meat on the end to
      be cooked over the flames. The ornament around the neck is an egg and dart band, the picture
      frames have a vertical flame pattern, and the ground line is a band of checkerboards
      alternating with three stopt maeanders.</P><P>In this period, several painters
      specialized in such small oinochoe. The youthful figures attending the sacrifice are typical
      of the late fifth century, unlike older figures seen previously.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

