<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8fc8e346fc90deec30943f380467461a6d3960a26ff7b8dd63853e1b0297b630> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The preserved portions of the vase are in good condition, with some
      discoloration occurring.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8fc9a6a0e854eeda91b339110f9c7a59a9ce3a5394cbec6115e4f5faf734ddc7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Ionic column; Peitho (labelled to the right of her head),
      standing 3/4-view to the right, her weight on her left leg, her right leg relaxed, wearing a
      peplos belted over a long overfold, holds her right arm at her side, and holds a footed chest,
      with three balls atop, and a sash, in her left arm; Aphrodite (labelled), seated on a klismos
      3/4-view to the left, with her legs crossed, wearing a himation around her legs, over a
      belted, medium-sleeved chiton with shoulder straps, a rayed sphendone, two bands on each
      wrist, and a dotted disk earring, rests her left arm on the back of her chair, and holds her
      right hand in front of her chest, in a speaking gesture; a kalathos basket; Hygieia (labelled
      above her head), standing 3/4-view to the left, with her weight on her right leg, her left leg
      relaxed, wearing a peplos, belted over a long overfold, holds a plemmochoe to the left, in her
      right hand, and a footed chest in her left hand; Eudaimonia (labelled), standing near frontal,
      slightly to the right, with her head profile to the right, her weight on her left leg, her
      right leg relaxed, wearing a himation draped over her left shoulder, around her lower body,
      and back over her bent left arm, over a short-sleeved chiton with shoulder straps, and a high
      pony tail, holds an eight-bead necklace down to the left, in her right hand, and holds her
      left hand, palm up (in a speaking gesture?), to the right; Paidia (labelled above her head),
      running 3/4-view to the left, with her weight on her forward, bent, right leg, wearing a
      sleeveless, belted chiton with a kolpos and shoulder straps, and loose, windswept hair,
      balances a stick on her outstretched right hand, and holds her left hand up behind her head;
      Eukleia (labelled above her head), standing 3/4-view to the right, with her weight on her left
      leg, her right leg relaxed, wearing a belted peplos and a sphendone, holds her right arm at
      her side, and holds a round (?) wicker basket and a sash in her left arm; Eunomia (labelled
      vertically, down the right side of her body), standing 3/4-view to the left, with weight on
      her right leg, her left leg relaxed, wearing a himation draped around her lower body and over
      her left arm (obscuring it), over a belted, medium-sleeved chiton, a broad taenia, and disk
      earrings, points the index finger of her right hand down to the left.</P><P>The
      long-standing misreading of "Eunomia" as "Aponia" has recently been corrected, and confirmed
      by Richard Stone, Conservator at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, at the instigation of Gloria
      Ferrari (see bibliography below).""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/8fd1c06b839bc2e5ee4305b60069c23ed1f1d3de579d7bc48c453c07fe51d73b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
