<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/94315614fcc087e98db34196c06a0121a69920ec802d53fa0eedb72f0fbdcf95> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<hi rend=\"ital\"><bibl>BMCRR</bibl></hi> II, 130, no. 70; pl. 74.20; <hi rend=\"ital\"><bibl>RRC</bibl></hi> no. 26/3, pl. I" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/9431c7e28bf5f459d1df54f37db7fe79f1dd930df71ac372451a2d1772670b50> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> Combat of two
      warriors. On the left, the victorious one advances to the right, bearded, he wears a helmet
      with a long crest. On his left arm he carries a round shield (shown foreshortened) with a
      tripod device. He is nude except for greaves on his legs and a garment around his shoulders,
      the ends of which are folded, crossed in front and tucked under his sword belt. Blood streams
      from a wound in his right shoulder, at the base of the neck. He attacks and thrusts at his foe
      with a long-bladed sword. On the right his antagonist has fallen, twisted to the right, his
      back turned toward the spectator, his left leg doubled up in collapse. His helmet is thus seen
      from the rear, a rare example of this in Greek vase-painting. Nude, except for a loin-cloth,
      his hair falls in long ringlets down his back. He holds his sword in his right hand and a long
      spear in his left, his scabbard hanging by a red baldric from his right shoulder. He is dying
      from two wounds, one in the left breast, the other in the right thigh, from which blood
      streams in added red. Ribs, backbone, and calf muscles are shown in dilute
      glaze.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B:</hi> warrior advancing. Moving to
      the left, the warrior wears a tight-fitting helmet without crest and a short stiff chiton (of
      leather or linen?) decorated with dots and crosses. On his left arm he carries a round shield
      (shown foreshortened) with a tripod device, in his right hand a long
      spear.</P><P>Below the design there is an elaborate and beautiful horizontal band
      of palmettes, addorsed and enclosed with tendrils.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

