<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/94889c166f6c2156b33248f4de2d4981ab4946b96fb91aa0ac5f1802d2ed9794> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Athena, armed, stands
      to the left between two Doric columns surmounted by cocks. Her chiton is simple and
      undecorated. The shield device is a Nike holding a long sash in both hands. The inscription
      runs along the inside of the left-hand column.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: javelin-throwing on horseback. Two epheboi ride to the right, a target centered
      between them. The rider in front has already thrown his javelin and is past the target, his
      javelin left sticking in the bull's-eye. His right hand is still raised behind his head after
      the throw. The rider on the left raises his javelin in his right hand as he prepares to throw.
      The target is a shield supported by a post. The shield device, a crown, forms the bull's-eye.
      Both epheboi are dressed in chlamys and petasos, although the petasos of the foremost rider
      has fallen behind his back. The horses are depicted in almost identical stances, their back
      legs together and firmly planted on the ground, while both front legs are staggered and raised
      off the ground.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/948d82216a5bf833332c1538d145a04f125faa1db35550c074e7b0f4b069bd49> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
