<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/99ab85200259d7aa6525cbefbde591e895eb97afad47dc7a2fb99e192355af6c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: the farewell of a
      warrior. The rather crowded panel shows the warrior in full armor to the far left, surrounded
      by his two children. The boy on the right is wearing a mantle, the little girl a chiton with
      white floral decoration. Nearby stands a charioteer in a quadriga. Behind the chariot wait
      several figures, all looking toward the warrior: a woman in a peplos with incised decoration,
      a hoplite, a second woman, another hoplite, a bearded man, and a third hoplite. The shields of
      the warrior and the last hoplite both show a tripod as shield device. The shield of the second
      hoplite is decorated with white and red dots.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: two hoplites fighting over a corpse. The one on the left wears a chiton with
      white floral decoration and a chlamys with ornamental flowers and red dots, the one on the
      left a chlamys with red dots along the seam. His shield shows a white bird as a shield device.
      Between them lies a dead hoplite on the ground.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

