<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/9ad14c075c225127940eacd9805fcffc8615ea73ae9e44039a82866732b562cd> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>On the front of the body, a woman stands to right between two
      bearded sirens. The woman wears a belted peplos decorated with bands of zigzags, wavy lines,
      and dots of added white, the latter also appearing on her fillet. The rest of the peplos is
      tinted with added red, as is her face. With her left hand, she touches the face of the siren
      before her. Like the woman, both sirens have red faces, long black hair, and fillets with
      white dots. Added red colors their breasts and two broad stripes on their wings, which are
      also decorated with bands of dots and dot-rosettes in added white. Their wings are raised and
      extend behind them, overlapping at the back of the vase. Between the figures, in every
      available space, are blobby rosettes with asterisk-incision. Five concentric circles on mouth;
      dots on side of the rim; band of simple, unframed tongues on shoulder; stripe around
      foot.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/9ae12ba7e9e36fc4a742f479d711d11649edae0c0f82d2befae71b324a4728c3> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
