<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/9d227e6f760ea68a435fa0721afec4330d800c563f195cdcad9d00a2377e6956> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Main Panel</hi>: three women with
      hydriae at a fountain. The fountain is on the far right. One of the women is at the fountain.
      Her foot is on the first step and she is about to fill her hydria or has just finished filling
      it. Water is gushing from the fountain's lion head spout. The central woman is leaving the
      fountain, walking away to the left, her hydria balanced on her head. She has raised one hand
      to steady it. A third woman approaches the fountain from the far left. Her hydria is empty,
      for she carries it horizontally on her head. Her arms hang at her sides. There is a low-flying
      bird between the central woman and the woman on the left. A second bird is perched on the top
      of the fountain. A tree at the far side of the fountain has spread its branches in the
      background of the scene.</P><P><hi rend="head">Shoulder scene</hi>:
      Herakles and the Nemean Lion. Herakles and the lion wrestle on the ground while Athena and
      Iolaos watch. Herakles has forced the lion's head to the ground and the lion tries to push his
      head away with his left rear paw. Herakles' quiver hangs above him and his mantle hangs to his
      left. Athena is seated on a stool on the far left holding a spear, her shield resting on her
      left knee. She wears a chiton, aegis and a crested helmet. Iolaos is seated on a stool on the
      right. He is holding something in his right hand, possibly a club. He wears a short chiton and
      there is a sash draped over his right arm. His other arm is held
      akimbo.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/9d2398d7cc69bb5f7dde21d6b2f0423cef50ee94958dba43a15b466b400bfc05> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
