<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/9e02254f98f73f6dd93a88f85035b455af71cc8cb4853ab9706f8e4a5abf78d5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> III, 538, no. 1883, pl. 99.4; <bibl>Cohen 1880-1892, 2.253, 74</bibl> " ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/9e17540d9ce5cd372745a10c910392533c8e6f9e4d38f30bef12a8fb18711684> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The central panel (only on obverse) is framed by a simple,
      vertical guilloche on either side, with filled centers, and the panel contains: a leaping dog,
      an ibex, a leaping dog and ibex (all r.). The filling ornament: triglyph motive in two
      different heights at the base line; in the very center, below, a somewhat abstract palmette;
      on top, a hanging half rosette (with a triangular interior subdivision and an outer border of
      small squares in between a double line); at the left, a large, now rather faded, quatrefoil
      rosette. Spoked-wheel rosettes, dot-rosettes and cross-designs are scattered, spaciously.
      Three registers of "crescents," the middle one in reverse direction, each register separated
      by a row of dots bounded by thin lines. A row of simple strokes (tongue patterns) at the base
      of the neck, and a meander band on the neck. There is a square, in brown glaze, drawn at the
      base of the handle and the reverse is otherwise decorated with rays. There are now only traces
      of added red on the decoration.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/9e1b10c696685e10b38f1c7402228b04ccda079b66350dfd99e2874e3412e59e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A (body, upper level): Eudaimonia (labelled), standing 3/4-view
      to the right, with her left foot raised on a rock, wearing a belted peplos, and a sphendone,
      rests her left arm on her knee, and holds a branch (?) in her upraised right arm; above, a
      bearded satyr (only upper half of body shown emerging from behind a hill), 3/4-view to the
      right, wearing an ivy wreath, holds both bent arms in front of his body, the left arm raised
      higher; a bearded satyr, Simos (labelled), seated 3/4-view to the right, wearing an ivy
      wreath, looks down to an amphora in his lap, held in his left hand, from which he pours wine
      into a kantharos, held in his right hand; a nude, winged, laureate Eros (labelled), hovering
      above, 3/4-view to the right, with his left leg raised, resting his right hand on his hip, and
      curving his right arm in a speaking gesture; Eudia (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the left,
      wearing a sleeved chiton, a himation draped around her lower body and over her left shoulder,
      and a sphendone, holds her right arm at her side, and an upright thyrsos in her upraised left
      hand; Dionysos, reclining 3/4-view to the left on an ornate couch, wearing a himation around
      his legs, and a wreath, holds a thyrsos in his upraised right hand; he is attended by a nude,
      winged, laureate Himeros (labelled), at his feet, standing profile to the right, with his
      weight on his right leg, and his left foot advanced; and Opora (labelled), emerging from
      behind the hill (visible above her knees), standing near frontal, with her head turned profile
      to the left, wearing a sleeved chiton, a nebris over her left shoulder, a long pony tail, and
      an ivy wreath, holding a trefoil-lipped oinochoe in her lowered left hand, and a plate of
      fruit in her bent left arm; a vine; Thyone (labelled), seated 3/4-view to the right, with her
      head turned profile to the left, wearing a sleeved chiton and a himation draped over her legs,
      and a crown, resting her left arm on her knee, and cradling a thyrsos in her right arm; a
      nude, winged, laureate Pothos (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the left, with his right leg
      raised on a rock, resting his left arm on his hip, and holding in his right hand a grape
      bunch; a kantharos below him; a female figure, perhaps Oreias (labelled), standing 3/4-view to
      the left, wearing a himation draped over her left shoulder, over a chiton, and a kekryphylon
      (?), holds a thyrsos upright in her upraised left hand, and reaches her right arm to the left;
      a tripod on Doric column; a bearded satyr, Oinopion (labelled), seated 3/4-view to the right
      on a rock, with his head profile to the left, wearing a nebris over his left shoulder, and an
      ivy wreath, rests his left hand on his knee, and his right hand on the
      rock.</P><P>A (body, lower level): A deer standing profile to the right, left
      front leg advanced; Hebe (labelled), standing near frontal, with her head profile to the left,
      wearing a long-sleeved, patterned, oriental tunic over a chiton, and a sphendone (?), reaches
      her right hand to the deer, and bears plate of food on her bent left arm; a nude satyr
      reclining 3/4-view to the left, leaning on an amphora, with his head turned profile to the
      right, hidden partially by his bent right arm, wearing an ivy wreath, rests his left hand on
      the ground; a palm tree behind him; a tripod on doric column; a young satyr, Sikinnos
      (labelled), standing profile to the right, with his weight on his right leg, and his left leg
      bent, wearing an ivy wreath, stretches both arms to the head of an ass, standing profile to
      the left; a lekanis between them; above, a nude, bearded satyr, Silenos (labelled), seated
      profile to the left, leaning back on a wine skin, legs crossed, wearing an ivy wreath, playing
      a double flute held in both hands; a tripod on doric column; a female figure seated 3/4-view
      to the left, enveloped in a himation, which is veiled over her head, a chiton, and a taenia,
      holds both arms (obscured by the himation) at her sides, and looks
      up.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

