<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a2b958a802f987b3a0c32329008e4e2ff02138ceacf441f836c8c5f06cbe49ef> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A youth, perhaps Eubouleus, standing near frontal, with his
      head profile to the right, wearing a long-sleeved, short, oriental tunic, a red taenia, and
      tall boots, raises his right hand at his side; his left hand is obscured by Dionysos, standing
      near frontal, with his weight on his left leg, his head turned profile to the right, wearing a
      long-sleeved, long, oriental tunic, a himation around his waist and over his left shoulder,
      obscuring his left hand, a nebris tied over his left shoulder, and a red ivy wreath, rests the
      back of his left hand on his hip, and holds a gold thyrsos in his lowered right hand; white
      Demeter, seated 3/4-view to the left on a blue cista, with her head turned 3/4-view to the
      right, wearing a colored peplos, a gold relief polos crown, a gold beaded necklace, two-part
      pendant earrings (in relief), a gold band on each wrist, rests his right hand on his knee, and
      holds a gold scepter in his upraised left; a young, white boy, Ploutos, standing near frontal,
      with his weight on his left leg, and his head turned profile to the left, wearing a blue
      chlamys on his back tied with red cross-straps, a short pony tail, and a gold taenia, rests
      his right elbow on a cista, and cradles in his left arm a keras; white Kore, standing near
      frontal, slightly to the right, with her head turned 3/4-view to the left, wearing a
      button-sleeved chiton, a himation, a laurel wreath, a gold band on her right wrist, a gold
      beaded necklace, and two-part pendant earrings, holds two torches, one in each hand, to the
      left; a female figure, Eleusis (or Rhea ?), seated profile to the left on an omphalos
      (otherwise interpreted as "the Mirthless rock"), wearing a himation veiled over her head and
      around her body, obscuring her left arm and her hand, draped over a sleeveless chiton (?), a
      stephane, a gold beaded necklace, pendant earrings, and one band on her right wrist, rests her
      feet on a footstool; Eros seated 3/4-view to the right, with his head profile to the left, and
      his (blue?) wings frontal, wearing a himation around his lower legs and waist and a red
      taenia.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

