<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a41c59a29ea20ddb10f101d6d286e75a03e1e5e63c95ac333792b4343336d8dd> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A: Nude Theseus (labelled), advancing 3/4-view to the right,
      with his weight on his bent, forward left leg (partially obscured by a rock), wearing a white
      taenia, and a black/red scabbard strap over his right shoulder, holds a bronze podanipter, or
      large shallow dish (brown wash to indicate bronze), in his right hand, behind his head, and
      reaches forward his left hand to pull the head of Skiron; nude, bearded Skiron (labelled)
      seated on rock 3/4-view to the left, rests his left hand on a rock, while he reaches his right
      arm straight to Theseus, turning up his right hand to beseech the hero; a tortoise behind the
      rock; Theseus (labelled), advancing 3/4-view to the right, with his weight on his bent,
      forward left leg, wearing a chlamys over his left arm, a white wreath, and a red/black
      scabbard band over his right shoulder, holds a sword in his extended right hand arm, and a
      rock in his left hand, which is obscured by his chlamys; a barren olive tree; a sow, advancing
      profile to the left, raises her front legs on the rocks; in front of the sow, Krommyo
      (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the left, with her weight on her left leg, pulled back (her
      age is revealed in her bent posture, as well as her wrinkles and white hair), wearing a
      button-sleeved, belted chiton, holds a staff in her left hand, and beseeches Theseus with her
      outstretched right hand; nude Theseus (labelled), standing near frontal, with his right leg
      bent profile to the left, his left leg straight to the right, and his head profile to the
      right, wearing a black/red scabbard strap over his left shoulder, holds a branch of the
      pine-tree with his right hand above his head, and reaches his left arm to the curly hair at
      the top of the head of Sinis; nude, bearded Sinis (labelled), kneeling frontal on the ground,
      with his head profile to left, and his right leg and arm (beseeching) straight to the left,
      raises his left hand to the trunk of the tree.</P><P>Tondo: Athena (labelled) in
      front of a palace with an Ionic facade; Theseus (labelled) and the Minotaur
      (labelled).""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

