<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a80bc2be242db624876423e319b0c18bc3019638a00bf8fb502dcbd9feaa6c2a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Satyr pursuing a nude maenad, profile to the right"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a80bf4aba9d0ce3bdc78b4d198297e745d5f0a7939af6c98f8afc959a513b4cc> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A:</hi> A group consisting of
      an equestrian with two bearded companions moves to the right. The bearded man on horseback
      wears a headband and a red chiton. He has tied an animal skin over this garment. The band and
      the seams of the chiton are decorated with white dots. His right hand is holding a spear. The
      horse has white teeth and its mane is tied up. Red lines mark the mane, the chest, and the
      muscles on its hind legs. Above the horse is a bird in flight, its wing and tail feathers
      indicated in white. The bearded men on foot are both nude except for a short mantle. They are
      both carrying wreaths in their right hands, their left arms are slightly raised. They wear
      necklaces and headbands with dotted decoration and their mantles show dotted rosettes and red
      dots. A nude man walks in front of them carrying a small mantle, similarly patterned as the
      others, over his left arm. Two smaller figures occupy the space below the handle: first
      another nude, bearded man, who has his hair tied up in a knot and wears the same attire as the
      previous man, raises both hands in pursuit of a girl. Her arms are raised and she wears a
      black and red peplos, its seams decorated with white dots. Red paint marks the straps of her
      sandals, the necklace and armbands, and the headband.</P><P><hi
      rend="head">Side B:</hi>This scene shows only a few variations on the opposite group.
      The equestrian is lacking the animal skin tied over the chiton. Behind his two companions
      another bird in flight is painted below the handle. The bearded man walking in front of the
      group with the horseman wears also a red chiton with white-dotted seams, an animal skin tied
      over it, and a red Phrygian cap. In front of him two men are facing each other; their hands
      are raised. Both have red hair, which is tied up, and they wear the dotted headband and
      mantle.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a819d5849beb90612d9aced5ebdb9a326c623c50e5cf813a82a9ded738d41db2> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
