<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a84f4a23272e854ff019618e9cda74b507e735085f905693583cd5d15c7cbd9c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>At the rim, there is a band of dotted net pattern. A fancy
      pinwheel rosette is located in this band at either side of the handle. Below the net band are
      two rows of alternate checks. In the animal frieze is a stag between lions, then a stag to the
      left, and a panther to the left. The filling ornament is incised "plus" rosettes (which is
      characteristic of the Perachora Painter's work). Below the animal frieze is a row of single
      dots, then a band of rays on two levels.</P><P>The Perachora Painter is known from
      fragments of his work found at Perachora and Corinth. This is the only complete vase by him
      (Amyx, 373).</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

