<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a9af1961af7f4d9f48cd6a64244754765cc8b8320a96d900f1a53935fa98d998> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Two bearded nude
      revelers lie on their backs with their feet toward the center and their heads toward the
      handles. They are masturbating. The man on the left wears a red fillet around his head and a
      flowered red and white garland around his neck. The hair around his nipple and his penis are
      painted red. The man on the right, wearing a flowery wreath on his head and a red garland on
      his right shoulder, leans on a folded red and white painted pillow, and has just ejaculated.
      His beard, testes, and the glans of his penis are painted red. He "extends his free hand in
      greeting"! (von Bothmer, 221)</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: A
      male (von Bothmer identifies it as male, 221) siren stands to the right with wings outspread
      and left hand extended, palm up. He wears a peplos on his shoulders and a fillet in his hair.
      Bordering his tail bar are ornate bands of dots and incised wavy lines. His body is one large
      apotropaic eye. His face, fillet, and peplos are painted red, as are parts of his wings and
      the pupil of the apotropaic eye. The second ring of the iris in the eye is painted white, as
      is part of the wings.</P><P>Beneath each handle, a dog defecates facing Side B.
      The dogs' necks and excrement are painted red.</P><P>The inside of the vessel is
      glazed except for the reserved line just below the glazed rim and the tondo, which is
      decorated with a dot and two concentric circles, one broad and one narrow (dilute). On the
      exterior, the narrative zone encircles the upper part of the bowl; a painted line runs around
      the lower part.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a9af9deff9109db76fd1b6827b54e1d0e8d81fb0ed5479d1dbaed394e4ec0825> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>On Side A, Dionysos is seated in a cart, drawn to the right, by
      two donkeys. The god wears a long chiton and himation, and an ivy wreath in his hair. He holds
      a grape vine, bearing clusters of grapes and blossoms in added white, in his left hand. The
      cart has two wheels and is of the type often seen hauling cargo, definitely different from the
      normal chariots used by the gods. The harnesses of the donkeys are rendered in added red and
      have leaf decoration in added white. A man moving to the left, looking back over his shoulder
      precedes the cart. He too wears an ivy wreath. He also wears a short chiton in added white,
      and a himation with added red dots. A goat precedes this man in turn. Side B is the same, only
      the added white is better preserved and there is some decoration on Dionysos' cart. An ivy
      tendril within lines of glaze decorates the lip of the cup. The handles are glazed. The lower
      body receives alternating red and black strokes above a black foot. The underside of the foot
      has concentric circles.</P><P>The theme of Dionysos in a donkey-cart is fairly
      unusual. The god is connected with donkeys early in Attic art with depictions of Dionysos
      sending Hephaistos back to Olympus mounted on one. In late black figure vase-painting,
      particularly in the early fifth century, scenes of Dionysos mounted on a mule become more
      common. The scene of Dionysos in a cart, like this one and <rs type="vase">Athens, Agora
      P26648</rs> are related to the scenes of Dionysos mounted, with the emphasis being on
      Dionysos' pastoral/agricultural connections.</P><P>The Theseus Painter decorated a
      great many skyphoi and was the principal artist of the "White Heron group". The skyphoi by the
      Theseus Painter tend to be earlier than his lekythoi, probably dating to before
      500.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a9bcd30a6a2a2c82c850b74917be203b35db212c62f880ca0ef9ff837013c250> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMC</hi></bibl>, Thrace, no. 58; M. Comstock, <hi rend=\"ital\">Bulletin of the Museum of Fine Arts</hi> 61 (1963) 110-11, 2 figs. = AMS, <hi rend=\"ital\">Numismatic Literature</hi> 71, 501; C. Vermeule, <hi rend=\"ital\">Proceedings of the American Philosophical Society</hi> 109 (1965) 381, note 61; <bibl>Vermeule 1968, 146-47, fig. 74</bibl>; <bibl>Romans and Barbarians</bibl>, no. C60 (ill.); E. Ghisellini, <bibl>LIMC</bibl> VII, 1.884, under no. 59, <bibl>Sear 1982, 311, no. 3274</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a9cbfb69d8e85ba75f36c5fc641c51935e86143b1d3c26cdcd22969a3dd10215> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """A: Dithyrambic victory: a bull, standing profile to the right, before a
      tripod on a one-stepped base, is being adorned with stemmata by a female figure, leaning
      profile to the left, with her right foot advanced, wearing a peplos belted over a long
      overfold, a long pony tail, and a plain stephane; a female figure standing profile to the
      right, wearing a peplos and a sakkos, as well as an olive wreath, places stemmata over the
      horns of another bull, standing profile to the left, in front of similar
      tripod.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a9d53e4552337b8b01c8d51294c423fee5e88c6473c226d877eebd49f6646e17> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<P><bibl>Buitron 1972, 144-5</bibl></P>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/a9e7e4c25941ff717295a11c1d9e0d402e1f3bf94632f80f96d6d9bb3089c6f0> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
