<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/aa1f39d4ac8b4f6434bdf63c471669e7e8cd4bcecd3896f1016736247dc8d813> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Vierneisel-Schlrb 1988, 9-11, no. 2, pls. 2-3</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/aa1ffb7145e2fd6bd24b2b2c41e531eaf7e64faee9e69bfd22e3ef7f50af75a5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> Aeneas is in the
      center, facing right as he carries his aged father Anchises out of Troy. The hero's body is
      bent over with the weight of the old man whose leg the son holds up with his right arm while
      he protects them with the Boeotian shield on his left. Aeneas wears a helmet, cuirass, and
      short chiton, with spears strapped to his back. The father Anchises has long hair and a beard,
      wears a long embroidered chiton and carries a scepter. He is framed by women running away on
      both sides, but looking back at the central scene. They wear long chitons bordered with
      stripes of added red and embroidered himatia. The one on the right has drawn hers up as a veil
      over her head. Could this be Kreusa, Aeneas' wife whom he forgets and leaves behind to perish
      at Troy? The other woman might possibly be Aphrodite, Aeneas' mother. Their gender is
      indicated also by their white flesh. On the left a beardless archer runs in clad in a
      high-peaked cap, cuirass, short chiton in added red and quiver. On the far right a balding,
      bearded elderly man stands absolutely still witnessing the pious act and holding onto his
      staff. He wears a long chiton and himation. The hair of both elderly males is depicted in
      added white.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B:</hi> On the left is a
      bearded warrior, fully armed, with short white chiton and embroidered chlamys, thrusting a
      spear with his raised left hand at an opponent who retreats before him. The first soldier
      protects himself with a shield on his right arm. The retreating soldier who runs to the right
      glances back at his assailant. He defends himself with a shield on his right arm and his spear
      with his left. He has two white plumes on his helmet and wears a short chiton in added red.
      His Boeotian shield has a thunderbolt device. Behind him is a third fully armed warrior in a
      short chiton in added red. He defends the man in front of him, by preparing to hurl his spear
      with his raised right hand while defending himself with a shield on his left. His shield has a
      dolphin in added white as device.</P><P>On the neck there is a double honeysuckle
      chain. Above the main figured design is a tongue pattern. Below the design are circumscribed
      lotus buds. Below that are rays on the lower body. Beneath the handles are
      palmettes.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

