<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ab16abe30403fdaea699ac77763e6502f325699c41c78c09d6eb07f988d2387d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: At left, Athena stands
      in profile to the right. She holds a spear in her right hand, and a helmet in her left. Her
      hair is wrapped in a scarf, and she wears a chiton fastened at the shoulders. On the right is
      a pile of rocks (?), on which sits a basket. The wicker lid, decorated with olive wreaths, has
      been thrown off and is lying on the rocks. Two snakes emerge from the rocks, near the base of
      the basket. A small child, dressed in a cloak thrown over his shoulder, is seen from the waist
      up in the box. He looks towards Athena and waves with his right hand.</P><P>The
      child is Erichthonios, son of Athena and Hephaistos. The myth was that the virgin Athena went
      to visit Hephaistos at his forge. He made advances to her and she ran away, disgusted.
      However, some of his semen spilled on the ground, and Erichthonios was born from that. Athena
      then took the baby and gave him to the daughters of Kekrops, Herse and Aglauros, for
      safekeeping, as is told in <bibl n="Eur. Ion 20ff.">Eur. Ion 20ff.</bibl> Athena
      had entrusted the baby Erichthonios to them, on the condition that they not open the basket in
      which he was kept with the two snakes. They did, and as punishment Athena drove them both mad,
      and they threw themselves off the heights of the Acropolis.</P><P>Keuls (123)
      suggests that the box in which Erichthonios sits is a substitute for Athena's non-functioning
      womb.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Two youths are depicted
      running. They should have been Herse and Aglauros, daughters of Kekrops, but they are
      male.</P><P>The upper border of the figural panel is a band of olive branches, the
      lower border is a band of maeanders and crosses.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ab1d502f150a907e2dc8fcbb65ef637281d90f0b5da9a9a4130e7fca433b44cb> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
