<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/af199819d83f4d76d065dd329e4c0213dc115cc949bcc6207b90b0c4c2ad6a7f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Departure of a warrior. A charioteer in a long white chiton
      holds reins taut as he stands in the box of a quadriga facing right. His Theban shield,
      decorated with dotted circles in white, hangs on his back. Behind the horses stands a hoplite,
      his body pointing right, his head turned to the left. He wears a Corinthian helmet with a
      stilted crest over which is a red fillet. His shield decorated with white dots is on his left
      arm. A white sword baldric passes over his shoulder. At right, a nude boy stands facing left.
      The near trace horse has a red mane and red chest band. The near horses nod their heads, the
      far horses raise their heads. The near pole horse has a red tail. A pair of fillets hangs in
      the background.</P><P>Shoulder: a pair of lions attack a deer at center. On either
      side galloping away are young horsemen in Thracian cloaks.</P><P>Below the neck
      are black and red tongues. Framing the main scene are ivy vines. Double red stripes circle the
      body below the panel and above the zone of rays on the lower
      body.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

