<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b08d8af16d1f712d9389f0fa34d2165ed5663c679b9c3446c44d3d4d72eb2db8> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The inside of the handles, as well as a space between the
      handle attachments are clay-colored. On the shoulder just below the body-neck join is a band
      of tongues. All the figures are standing on a clay-colored groundline.</P><P>On
      side A, Athena presides in the center over a battle between two hoplites. The warrior on the
      left is unbearded and appears to be the aggressor. He is wearing a short chiton, breast plate,
      and low-crested helmet, and a sword in its scabbard suspended from two dark red straps over
      the shoulder. In his left hand he holds his shield with the skull of a steer as its device. In
      his right hand he wields his spear in a threatening manner at the second warrior. The second,
      bearded warrior has fallen back to a squatting position as blood flows from two wounds, one in
      the torso, one in the thigh. He is naked except for his high-crested helmet and a mantle which
      has slipped from his shoulders and hangs over his arms. His helmet is high-crested and his
      sword scabbard hangs from a dark red double strap over his shoulder. In his right hand he
      holds his sword, attempting to defend himself. His shield is in his left hand, which is flung
      rather uselessly behind him. In the center Athena strides right, wearing a long sleeved chiton
      with broad horizontal patterned stripes on its lower part, a mantle, aegis, and dark red
      bracelets. Her hair is tied with a dark red band. In her left hand she holds her helmet, in
      her right her spear. She turns her head to the left to look at the warrior whom she has deemed
      the victor. Added reddish brown emphasizes the warriors' muscles, as well as the breast plate
      and the lefthand warrior's beard shadow.</P><P>On side B, three warriors are
      preparing for combat. In the center, a young warrior, naked except for his helmet and a mantle
      tied around his thighs, pulls on his greaves. The warrior to the left is also unbearded,
      wearing a short chiton, a mantle slung over his arms, and a helmet and holding in his left
      hand a spear and shield with a rooster as its device, as he watches his companion arming. The
      bearded warrior on the right is dressed similarly to the one on the left. He holds his spear
      in his right hand and his shield, with a triskelis for its device, in his left. The round
      shields have been drawn with a compass. Added red is used for musculature, the folds of the
      chiton, the beard shadow of the middle warrior, and the end of the righthand warrior's beard.
      On both sides the figures are outlined in light relief.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b0a57e9b0b5b6e7108037c39e074bafc556edc0de7305a1c9efb1dfac4926145> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
