<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b175e3b33f2224834738ffb5b95dfe031ecb1403f90b9ee7489ce31830b77243> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Broken and repaired, with missing pieces restored in plaster but not repainted.
      Very worn in many places, with loss of painted design, which may still be traced by means of
      the incision.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b1790d806f52ea006af605a40ffbc01b5c3e93e31ceba4f4d29198f32efbb333> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Walled, open air sanctuary; on the Acropolis, joining the Erechtheion at the west end."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b1850ab19da723cd36f7e8a546801d32e6ba09b25e6800517fea6c2abccb2d0d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Interior:</hi> The tondo is
      indicated by a thin red circle within which a carpenter kneels to the right with his left knee
      raised and his right nearly touching the ground. In his left hand he grasps the upper part of
      a wooden beam which rests obliquely before him and bears what seems to be a lock. In his right
      hand he holds an adze (skeparnon). The head of the adze is lashed to the heft with a cord. He
      wears a wreath executed in added red and a bordered himation knotted around his loins.
      Anatomical details are indicated with dilute glaze and the outline of his short curly hair is
      incised. The figure fills the tondo.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b18874af98f8a81e4fc7c6106ea5e1058082166e8b92a61bc71249bb602342d4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "First Battle of Greeks and Trojans"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b188d2ddff257e8ede1d552492a27e26af6e3c6055188ec36d56a45e97867bee> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Shoulder:</hi> Soldiers arming: At
      center a beardless warrior faces right, fastening a greave onto his left leg which rests on
      his helmet. He wears his hair long and filleted with a short chiton and sword, and his right
      greave already on. Confronting him is a female figure (his wife or mother?). She stands facing
      left and holding his spear with her right hand. She wears her filleted hair long and is
      dressed in a peplos. Behind her a warrior fully armed with helmet, shield (with a bent white
      leg as device) chlamys, short chiton, and greaves, faces left and holds the young man's shield
      (with a white tripod as device). Behind him, an archer walks to the right, turning back with
      his left hand raised and carrying an unidentified object in his right. He wears a peaked
      Phrygian cap, short chiton, and quiver. At the far right a fully armed warrior looks on. His
      shield bears the device of three pellets. With his back to the young warrior another fully
      armed warrior faces left, away from center. He, too, has the shield device of three white
      pellets. Confronting him further left is another beardless archer who holds a in his raised
      left hand and a in his right. He is dressed like the first. At the far left a beardless man
      looks right, standing quietly and watching the preparations. He wears a long chiton and
      himation and holds a staff in his left hand.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Body:</hi> At center a bearded warrior walks right, carrying on his left
      shoulder the dead body of an Amazon off the battlefield. He wears his filleted hair long with
      front locks and is dressed in a cuirass short chiton, and greaves, holding his two throwing
      spears in his right hand. A shield with an ivy wreath device rests against his leg. She, limp
      and lifeless, her eyes closed in death, wears a wreath in her long hair, a short chiton,
      cuirass, an arm bracelet, anklet, and sword. Is it Troy, Achilles, and Penthesilea? These
      names are not inscribed. To the right a warrior and archer depart to the right. The warrior
      looks back at the central scene. He is fully armed and his shield bears a triskeles device in
      white. The archer, wearing a peaked Phrygian cap, short chiton, quiver, and greaves, carries
      an axe in his left hand. On the left, behind the central group, an Amazon has fallen to the
      ground with her left leg drawn up under her. She protects herself with her shield on the left
      arm and holds her spear in her right hand. She wears a high-crested helmet, cuirass, short
      chiton, and greaves. Over her a fully armed warrior strides to the left with a shield device
      of a bull's head and with his right hand transfixes her with a spear. Above the last warrior
      is inscribed <foreign lang="Greek">*K*A*L*O*S</foreign>, "(he is) beautiful." In
      front of Achilles, <foreign
      lang="Greek">*K*R*I*T*I[*A*S]</foreign>.</P><P>A circumscribed tongue
      pattern runs above the shoulder panel, around the base of the neck. Borders of ivy run down
      the sides of the panels. A palmette frieze runs across the bottom. On the lower body there is
      a band of rays.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b18d237121c216813adec56f96418ae79c01a3d1254ec197f0b672c438962a5e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Female figure, wearing a belted chiton and himation, seated 3/4-view to the left on a rock"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

