<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b211889c93f836a1dba60a42c324c8cc364f5293e68be08b970839742391c6f3> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: A nude, bearded komast
      is dancing with a white-skinned woman wearing a short, tunic-like garment. Added red is used
      for the garment and the man's breast. Both gesture emphatically, and the komast turns his face
      frontally. <hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: The same subject and composition,
      differing only in the position of the figures' arms. The use of added red is also the same,
      but either the woman's flesh was not coated with added white or it has completely worn
      away.</P><P>Pomegranate-net pattern on rim. Below each handle is an upright
      palmette growing from the base of a lotus blossom, each with cores of added red; from these,
      coiling, interlaced tendrils emerge on either side. Figures on a baseline of triple stripes.
      Rays on lower body. Handles, interior, and outside of foot black. Black stripe around
      underside of foot.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b216b1eb4476a800165880f6b0f50f99ec8a1f5c24c0a3952f3ee8c5337a3351> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
