<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b2d6ca4c23ab82b4e9b659e1ace6f7f7e878b466dfb542cadace896598cef31b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A</hi>: head of a bearded man.
      The man is in profile to the left, and is shown from the shoulders up. His long hair is bound
      at the nape of his neck with a white band, and white fillets are tied around the crown of his
      head, crossing over his ear. His skin is painted with added red, although his stylized ear is
      black. His round eye is also done in black glaze, and he wears a simple black
      chiton.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B</hi>: horse protome. The horse is
      shown in profile to the left with one of his forelegs raised. He is predominantly black but
      his neck has been painted in added red and his mane is drawn with alternating black and red
      locks. He has a round, black eye.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b2d968a5df2dd8a7e85424b8584b5a0597165f4854b4b3e151e53b75b854899e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "A cowherd and six Muses"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b2dd76859b5ea9a2d73ccc435e7442c644b199e95740dd765d90abce671370ad> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Athena and Hera"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b2ecfd5dc7a7c2f67f5f6d9076ad1e4dbe7676988b3e7ea2538703540ff57052> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A so-called "double-decker" Siana, with distinct decoration on
      the rim and the body. <hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: On the rim is an ivy wreath
      framed by drinking horns. The ivy leaves are alternately red and black; the wavy vine is drawn
      with dilute glaze. On the body, framed above and below by stripes of dilute glaze, a ram
      stands to the left, grazing between two panthers with frontal faces. The necks of the animals
      and parts of their bodies are colored with added red. On either side is a single palmette with
      a core of added red and a tendril linking it to the handle.<hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: The same, but without drinking horns and with only one palmette (at left).
      <hi rend="ital">Tondo</hi>: Framed by a simple black circle, a youth rides to the
      left on a hippalektryon, a cock-horse, with the head and forelegs of a horse and the body,
      legs, tail, and wings of a rooster. There are touches of added red on the rider's breast and
      the body of his mount. The incision is crudely executed.</P><P>Black stripe around
      outer rim; reserved stripe around inner rim. Lower body black except for a single reserved
      stripe. Black circle on underside of foot. Outside of foot black except for outer edge.
      Handles and all interior except tondo black.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b2eed8318bf0dacde8d918c7f62db2df5323d58ca3d3f398b15201e928af577f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
