<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b54ed9d31fdc3825d93a952c92861737f6191d714916e8b2f6fddfbbfd51417f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Achilles stands,
      facing right. He holds a spear in his right hand and his shield is slung over his left arm so
      that the inside is turned toward the viewer. He is dressed for battle; he wears scale
      patterned armor on his torso, a leather skirt under which is a short chiton, greaves and a
      crested helmet (it is impossible to tell if it is a Corinthian helmet, because the front part
      is lost).</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Briseis stands facing
      right. She holds a flower to her nose with her left hand, and her right rests on her waist.
      She is dressed in an ornate chiton of crinkly fabric and an overmantle. This last is decorated
      with swastikas and dots, and has a meander border. She wears earrings and a
      diadem.</P><P>Briseis was the prize of Achilles, and was taken from him by
      Agamemnon. Because of this slight to his honor, Achilles refused to continue fighting in the
      Trojan War. Homer describes the parting of Achilles and Briseis in the <hi
      rend="ital">Iliad</hi>:</P><P>". . . and Patroclus gave ear to his dear
      comrade, and led forth from the hut the fair-cheeked Brises, and gave her to them to lead
      away. So the twain went back beside the ships of the Achaeans, and with them, all unwilling,
      went the woman. But Achilles forthwith burst into tears, and withdrew apart from his comrades,
      and sate him down on the shore of the grey sea, looking forth over the wine-dark deep ...
      (<bibl n="Hom. Il. 1.345-350">Hom. Il.
      1.345-350</bibl>)</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b55ab3dea71ce02bbec302a8edcfe6e84c5f243656ceb085094bf9f9659cc190> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Side A: Alcaeus and Sappho<lb>Side B: Dionysos and maenad"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b55b59294eeea093da715d6d4296e2246ff2a05eb2284ad289da7b4549e665a3> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """A female figure, perhaps Hygieia, standing near profile to the right,
      wearing a peplos, a short pony tail, a black band necklace, and disk earrings, holds a box in
      her left hand, and holds her right hand at waist level; a female figure, perhaps Peitho,
      standing 3/4-view to the right, with her weight on her left leg, wearing a sleeveless,
      high-belted chiton, holds a sprig of vegetation in her left hand, and points her right hand to
      Tyche (?); a winged Eros, crouching 3/4-view to the right, crowns the female figure to his
      right, possibly Tyche, seated on a stool 3/4-view to the left, wearing a sleeved chiton, a
      himation around her legs, a short pony tail, a black band necklace, and black hoop earrings;
      she tilts her head back, holds her left arm at her side, and raises her right hand in front of
      her face; a female figure, perhaps Harmonia, standing 3/4-view to the left, wearing a sleeved
      chiton, a himation draped over her left shoulder, a kekryphylon, a beaded necklace, and
      dotted-disk earrings, holds her left hand at waist level, and raises her right hand in front
      of her face.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

