<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b70c0cef984b851109712e707c37023218b99fd4f763c2114e40a7eda11de5c2> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A: A nude bearded satyr, labelled Aietos, standing profile to
      the right, leaning back on his bent right leg, holds the stem of a kantharos in both hands,
      and tilts his head up; Euboia (labelled), dancing 3/4-view to the right, with her head profile
      to the left, wearing a belted, sleeved chiton with a long kolpos, a kekryphylon, tilts her
      head down, and bends both arms, the right one down, and the left one up, and holds in her left
      hand and thyrsos which she rests diagonally across her left shoulder; a nude, bearded satyr,
      Kissos (labelled), dancing near frontal, with his head profile to the left, tilted down, bends
      both legs; a maenad, Kinyra (labelled), dancing 3/4-view to the left, with her left leg bent
      back, wearing a sleeved chiton with a long kolpos, an ivy wreath, and a long pony tail, holds
      her right hand at her side, palm down, and holds a thyrsos at diagonal in her left
      hand.</P><P>B: A nude bearded satyr, Lemnos (labelled), moving profile to the
      right, with both legs bent, holds a wineskin in both hands, in his lowered left hand and
      raised right hand, and faces a maenad, Delos (labelled), dancing profile to the left, with her
      weight on her forward right leg, wearing a sleeved, belted chiton with a long kolpos, and a
      red taenia, tilts her head back, and plucks with her right hand at a lyre which she holds in
      her left hand; a nude bearded balding satyr, dancing near frontal, with his head profile to
      the right, and his legs crossed, tilts his head, holds his right arm straight at his side, and
      raises his left arm; a maenad, Tethys (labelled), dancing 3/4-view to the right, wearing a
      high-belted, long-sleeved chiton with a long kolpos, and a kekryphylon, advances her left leg
      and spreads her arms.</P><P>Tondo: A nude bearded satyr, Demon (labelled), dancing
      profile to the right, with his weight on his left leg, bends both legs, holds his left arm
      down, and holds a kantharos in his right hand; a maenad, Choro (labelled), moving 3/4-view to
      the left, wearing a long-sleeved chiton with a long kolpos, a kekryphylon, and a red band
      necklace, holds her right hand at her side, and holds a lyre at waist level in her left
      hand.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

