<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b9f3c80341a80b3ef766a1a8be6c2ed77d75c40bbef402d003f96ba7a52c712f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Side A: horseman arriving home. Side B: youth leaving home."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b9f7ddbc4554d989f475382b331c9ff2df1ea38e739e3188c8f67e1d56921146> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: olive harvesting.
      Three olive trees. A youth climbs the center tree and shakes its branches to harvest the
      olives. Two other men beat the branches with sticks from below. The olives fall to the ground,
      where they are collected by a youth with a basket.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Herakles and centaur Pholos. Pholos, on the left, holds a
      large bough from which hang a hare, a fox and a bird, and lays his hand on Herakles' hand.
      Herakles wears a short embroidered chiton, a sword and a quiver, and holds his club over his
      left shoulder, from which his lionskin hangs. Hermes is seated behind Herakles, wearing a
      chlamys, a petasos, winged boots and holding his caduceus. A deer stands next to
      Pholos.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/b9fef6e8e107cbf46d887df1761508a98559c16fe8ddd076ca3976647d60069f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Side A: horse and rider. Side B: woman."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ba016fd4760ef4c6a5eb6e7048e970617a3fe5f5008dcd8b58d352981651b5f4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Square roofed colonnade; in the Agora, beneath the Stoa of Attalos."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ba0249bb9a14a98f1ed68ed99c23fe0d3900b928df5e16563d72c4d36e280eeb> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Two-aisled stoa; the north boundary of the Sanctuary of Apollo."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ba06a5b1159c7bee0ee4c334902e4d1485bbb5fde006025528e04a50899869c4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Dionysos stands to the right dressed in a red wreath, chiton,
      and himation; his left foot is advanced but he does not seem to be walking. The folds of the
      chiton on his upper body are drawn with dilute glaze, but those above his feet are drawn with
      relief lines. The himation draped over his left arm hangs in long straight folds. In his right
      hand he carries a large black kantharos, the drinking cup that is his particular attribute. In
      his left hand he holds a long, knotty staff and a branch of ivy with red leaves. His long hair
      hangs down his back and in long, corkscrew tresses on his shoulders.</P><P>The
      groundline is a short band of ivy leaves framed by paired stripes; there are dots in the gaps
      between the leaves. A band of dotted egg-pattern nearly circles the base of the neck. Except
      for the side and base of the foot, the rest of the vase is
      black.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

