<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/be560cc72481822aec7f9fcedf9b45f865ef9f192f4cf30f5bfa7b0c6a1d058e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Revelers dancing to the music of flute and castanets. The
      procession of revelers moves to the right. It starts at the handle of the kyathos, where the
      procession is led by a woman playing a double flute. She is dressed in chiton and himation.
      She is followed by a naked man with a piece of cloth draped over his shoulders. He walks or
      dances with arms spread wide, looking back at a man carrying an amphora. The man with the
      amphora is naked, and is bent under the weight of the large amphora which he carries on his
      back. His stomach bulges slightly in this awkward position. He holds an unidentifiable object
      in his right hand. This man is followed by another man in a short chiton and mantle who holds
      a staff in his left hand. He is looking back over his shoulder at the woman behind him, who
      has one arm raised and is playing castanets. She is dressed in chiton and himation. Behind her
      is a naked youth in a short mantle walking or dancing with bent legs, holding a long
      projectile-like object. A man brings up the rear of the procession. He is wrapped in a mantle
      and is looking back over his shoulder to the left and holding his left arm akimbo. All the
      male figures are beardless. All the figures wear red
      wreaths.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/be57b8e64b664be76c4c2bd53b87937982ae34ffec2d4148b2c0800fc18ccbe8> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
