<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c262894bb33385553ee49021a537b0354935354295eb273f49bd2f8918df5a33> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Perseus is here
      depicted running to the right, wearing a short chiton with decorative borders, a skin, and
      winged boots. His cap of invisibility is tied underneath his cheek with a red ribbon; he also
      is equipped with a kibisis and harpe.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: this side shows a running Gorgon, apparently in pursuit of Perseus. She is
      wearing a long dress with sleeves and dotted decoration, a short mantle slung over her right
      shoulder, winged boots, earrings, and a red bracelet.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

