<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c588c3d9aca0c9bebe163fb8358c5cb7d647f21b8524861f1e61d3cc43f72d26> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Side A: four youths. Side B: three boys."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c58a68978e94854398adb9cf03e827d96770d337683c25d947065fc478e2e5d6> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Athena receives the
      baby Erichthonius from the hands of the earthmother Ge and proceeds to wrap him in her mantle.
      Hephaistos is watching from the left, his right arm resting on his hip, his left holding a
      staff. A mantle with many folds is draped around his shoulders. Two Erotes are flanking the
      scene on either side, balancing on delicate scrolls. The one on the left is holding on to a
      floral scroll for support and looks at the newborn child, the other is holding both a lyre and
      a scroll.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Zeus is seated on a
      folding chair, his right hand extended offering a libation bowl to the infant Erichthonius.
      The father of the gods is dressed in a long chiton with sleeves, a mantle, a taenia, and he is
      holding his scepter. A gorgoneion decorates the two joints where the seat is connected to the
      chair. In front of him stands Iris, who has just filled the bowl. She is also wearing a long
      chiton with sleeves and a mantle, her hair held up with a ribbon. Similar to the previous
      image, the scene is flanked by two Erotes. The one on the left is playing a lyre with seven
      strings, the one on the right extends his hand toward the seated Zeus.</P><P>All
      figures show delicate rendering lines and incised contours.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c58b0dd34308c74cf10b8bc0dc9c383f0fcbd58c0aa75da91d994e75a78ac169> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>GuideDelphMu 1991</bibl>; <bibl>Stewart 1990, 128f.</bibl>; <bibl>Brinkmann 1985, 77ff.</bibl>; <bibl>Hurwit 1985, 295ff.</bibl>; <bibl>Simon 1984a</bibl>; <bibl>Watrous 1982</bibl>; <bibl>Boardman 1978a, 158</bibl>; <bibl>Ridgway 1977, 269ff. and elsewhere</bibl>; <bibl>Robertson 1975, 152 ff.</bibl>; <bibl>FdDelph 4.2, 57-171</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c593d2ed02d4b492d843c04e496ea960614fb36a9b781ef6da4bd65a94fc36c7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><bibl>Walters 1928-29, pl.
      55.</bibl></P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c59f4e1518f3476762b459fa3793dc425de08e637f4341222e52eb7e813aac53> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The interior, handle, and lower portion of the bowl exterior
      are black. The outside of the rim has an unusual embattlement pattern with five small dots in
      the intervals, done in black on white ground between fine lines.</P><P>Large eyes
      separate the central figure from those at the handles. The eyes, though incompletely
      preserved, are relatively small and elongated, with the outer corners pointing upward and
      long, curving tear ducts. The strongly curved outlines of the eyes are executed in white
      paint, added over the white ground. The outer ring of the eye is red, while the next, equal in
      size is painted white. Probably there was a central black area with a small red
      pupil.</P><P>The cocks, while not completely preserved, are rendered in great
      detail. The eye and beak are incised, while comb and wattle are in added red, with carefully
      depicted points and blade of the comb. The throat has a strong convex curve, while the hackle
      bears white dots, its lower feathers indicated in incised points. Each wing feather has an
      incised outline and a dot of red paint. The long flight feathers probably appeared in two
      layers, set apart by a scalloped line of incision with added white paint. Four or five long
      saddle feathers were incised in outline, while two long sickle feathers were painted black.
      The tail feathers are rendered similarly to the flight feathers, with the same scalloped
      incision. The color of the two cocks' tail feathers differs; every other feather on the
      lefthand cock is red, those of the righthand cock white. Each cock faces the
      handle.</P><P>The komast in the center of the scene has an unusual costume that
      covers much of his body. The remaining parts are rendered in little anatomical detail. His
      head appears too large for his body, partly because of the mitra wrapped around it, and partly
      because of his extensive projecting hair and beard growth. The hair and beard are painted red.
      The komast's eye is large, low, and carefully incised, and his nose is straight. His
      short-sleeved chitoniskos has buttonholes drawn, but no buttons. Its collar is white, and its
      hem is dotted white. The skirt folds are broadly spaced, curvy incised lines. His boots are
      red, laced around the ankles and given prominent tongues. His upper and lower limbs have few
      details except the open incised loop of the kneecap. He is holding in both hands a lyre with
      swan-head terminals.</P><P>The face and neck of the molded female on the kyathos
      handle are painted white. A red band with white dots holds her long, red brown, wavy hair away
      from her face. Three tresses hang behind each ear, and her curly bangs are shown by a single
      row of raised dots. Her eyes and eyebrows have the same color as her hair. Her lips are
      undefined.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c5a5d79f0d4802184839a3fb5dec8270ce5b78abc54ef7fcfdc4ce0b282421b7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Broken and repaired, with missing fragments restored with plaster. Discolored
      and inaccurate repainting of contours, particularly noticeable Side A: horses, head of the
      warrior, chest and arms of the charioteer. Considerable erosion of the added colors,
      particularly the white.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

