<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c666ca3b401eb050ca70e4ba795e3897c3f0c601535c48be6882cb9057b96a4a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> II, 410, no. 493; <bibl>Cohen 1880-1892, 1.537, 15</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c66b5ecd58e271d767bb9f16f3eb5a27147fc5c8455e6bc930f6c46d28c28d93> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Body</hi>: To the left is Herakles,
      wearing the lion skin and carrying a bow and quiver. He has grasped the boar by its left rear
      leg and lifted its hindquarters off the ground. This has caused its front legs to buckle under
      it, and it appears to be in a very helpless position. To the right stands Athena. She is
      wearing her snake aegis and a high crested helmet. She holds her spear in her left hand and
      gestures toward Herakles with her right.</P><P>The panel is bordered vertically by
      bands of ivy leaves, and there is a horizontal band at the top of upright bars. Athena's skin,
      the boar's tusks and belly, the teeth of Herakles' lion skin and details of his chiton are
      picked out in white paint. The boar's neck, the rosettes on Athena's robe, and the pattern on
      Herakles' chiton is decorated with red paint.</P><P>Cohen notes that Herakles wide
      and bushy mustache is typical of the Lysippides Painter's early period, as seen also on the
      figures of <rs type="vase">Louvre F 294</rs>.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c67c942064e132886b4e79e711ec6ffa35a99462e97a84dc287e4981b57d1765> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
