<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ca216abfe12ba7a0c7c0d664997d3071c8453d992d7277788d9c5f6f55c87cce> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: A scene of sport. A
      jumper in the middle of the scene is training with weights. He is naked and his muscles are
      well rendered through thin lines. Around his left ankle he wears a band, perhaps an amulet. In
      front of him, at his left stands his coach dressed in himation. Over his shoulder he holds a
      stick used to maintain discipline (rhabdos). Both of them wear a red wreath, now mostly lost.
      Between them there are hanging on the wall a sponge, an aryballos and a strigil, the gear of
      the athlete for cleaning up after exercise. Behind the jumper on the floor at right there is a
      pick for loosening the earth for the long jump.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: Scene of music contest. In a building there is taking place the performance of a
      kitharode. Between two Aeolic columns, signifying a building, stands a bearded kitharode,
      dressed in a special kind of tunic or mantle. In his right hand he holds a plektron. In front
      of him at right, a bearded man sits on a stool. He holds a knotted stick and he may be a
      referee. Both of them wear a red wreath, almost gone.</P><P>The fact that all the
      figures wear a wreath and the nature of the scenes itself recalls the Panathenaic festival in
      Attica, which included contests in both sports and music.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ca249506752e865eaa4508d0c239d158da25769bb0f90cc9dd69de04478269e5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Broken and repaired; foot re-attached. Some flaking of glaze on the exterior,
      including the foot and some of the lions. The interior is much more eroded, with most of the
      glaze on the cock lost.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

