<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cb7a69d94f697bf26da57914c2f3b7bb66fe7ef6414ab46d5c71c449de58ff3d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Tondo: Discus-thrower and acontist<lb>Sides A-B: Athletes"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cb9198e7a4e2d32e0222119eeabccc96ce7dbb6ed68a38e5d7f8f33ddce052b8> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Heavily eroded, with considerable loss of the painted design. The loss of added
      color has left the maid an ethereal ghost of her former self, with only the barest outline of
      her body remaining and little trace of her garments. The other woman's himation has fared
      better, but the former crimson color is now very pale. The added colors were not of clay slip,
      but rather mineral pigments added after firing, which are particularly prone to
      erosion.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cba1cf0e516389d2f54c4ae5f8e3008a00c3d9300940c811d3f3e011ae7579f5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Karouzou 1968, 142</bibl>; <bibl>Svoronos 1903-12, 258-59, pl. 38.1</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbad85cb753d1cfa81137b49833e72fd2177b365edab965ba186927c1613fb07> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Five joining fragments." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbb5d15a24acb935f98720a63e1acff16f08bc3dd46f5e8a6adfcd099f2bfef2> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Herakles' arrival at
      Olympos. On the left, Herakles, wearing his lion skin and armed with a bow, strides to the
      right. Athena walks in front of him. She grasps his left wrist with her right hand, and with
      her left hand reaches out before her to the seated Zeus, apparently about to touch his beard
      in an imploring gesture. Athena wears a belted peplos and aegis with snakes. Zeus is seated on
      a small throne. He holds a staff in his right hand, and reaches out to Athena with his left.
      Under the figural band runs the horizontal inscription <foreign
      lang="Greek">*F*R*U*N*O*S *E*P*O*I*H*S*E*N *X*A*I*R*E *M*E*N</foreign> ("Phrynos made
      me. Hail!").</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: The birth of Athena.
      Zeus sits on a throne, facing right. Both of his hands are raised in a gesture of surprise or
      pain; in his right hand he clutches the thunderbolt, and his left hand is raised towards
      Hephaistos. From his head sprouts the head and upper torso of a (slightly under life-size)
      Athena. She carries her shield in her right hand and spear in the left. In front of these two
      stands Hephaistos; his legs are turned in profile to the right, and he seems to be walking in
      that direction, but twists his upper body back to look at Athena and Zeus. He gestures toward
      them with his right hand, and holds his axe in his left.</P><P>This scene depicts
      the moment after Hephaistos has hit Zeus on the head with his axe to assist in the birth of
      the goddess, and is now fleeing the scene. This event is also depicted on an amphora of Group
      E which is roughly contemporaneous (ca. 550 B.C.), <rs type="vase">Basel
      103.4</rs>.</P><P>Below the figural band on this side is the horizontal
      inscription <foreign lang="Greek">*X*A*I*R*E *K*A*I *P*I*E*I *M*E
      *N*A*I*X*I</foreign> ("Hail and drink me, verily!").</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbbdb13d55dc91b3dd4246bbc5d5c3a452362e6ca5f07362160c9cc962051c68> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Leopards, hare, swan."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbd60cd2b6caa5667647f56e3b6ae30d626227aad0259df4e290c4d947ddcf10> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: To the far left stands
      Athena, in a scale breastplate, helmet and chiton. She holds a lance and gestures with her
      right hand to Achilles. In front of her stands a Nereid holding a helmet and lance. She wears
      a chiton with an overblouse extending to her waist, and a scarf in her hair. In the center of
      the composition sits Achilles, mourning the death of his friend Patroklos. He is seated on a
      chair to the left, his head bowed. his upper body is wrapped in a cloak which partially covers
      his head, and he is wearing a diadem. Underneath the cloak a short embroidered chiton is
      visible. He holds a staff in his left hand. Thetis stands to his left, her arms wrapped around
      his shoulders. Her hair is bound up in a diadem, and she wears a long chiton and over it a
      cloak decorated with circles. To the right of this scene, another Nereid stands, her right
      hand covering her mouth as though she were moved by Achilles' suffering. She wears a chiton
      and an overcloak pinned at the left shoulder. With her left hand, she balances a shield
      upright on the ground. The shield design is of a woman (Athena?). The nereid's hair is pulled
      up in a scarf. Behind her stands an old man, possibly Phoinix, wearing a
      himation.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: To the left stands a
      Nereid, holding a sword and helmet. In front of her is a youth (Achilles?) in profile to the
      right. He is wearing a long himation and a cloak which partially covers his head. His right
      arm is hidden under his clothing, and in his left hand he holds a spear. He is facing another
      Nereid, who holds greaves (?) in her left hand. Behind her stands a third woman, holding a
      quiver (?). All of the women wear long chitons; the center woman also wears a cloak over her
      right arm, and a scarf in her hair.</P><P>Palmettes decorated the lower handles,
      and the bottom border of the figural pattern has a band of
      maeanders.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbd86081cb90b54a22e07e70bf0f59684423e60489a32bdc495342e00e613a66> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Sides A and B</hi>: siren between
      two draped youths. On each side a siren stands to the right, wings spread. She is flanked by
      beardless youths draped in ankle-length mantles. Each youth has raised his left hand to waist
      level, still hidden under the mantle. There are palmettes on either side of the
      handles.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbdcb2c9b4de37282c593f2f6e0e89103be075f4aafaa0e90ead650300cc9465> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Boardman 1995, 72, fig. 56</bibl>; <bibl>Comstock & Vermeule 1976, no. 55</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbe08d13e4c3f304b3bee9f8e08e62aca279622544b07e7b058895977975ef30> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Smith 1997,</bibl> cat. DR 13; <bibl>Lawton 1995</bibl>, 131 no. 109, pl. 57; <bibl>Meyer 1989</bibl>, 311 A 166; <bibl>Svoronos 1903-12</bibl>, 671 no. 458.3, pl. 228.3; <bibl>Sybel 1881</bibl>, 207 no. 4250." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbea41451dd8438a1df9eafca13110dfd4dd464d4af5411352dd413246181697> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Side A: two couples consisting of a man and a woman between
      sphinxes at either end. The two women have long black hair, wear black chitons with red
      mantles, and hold a black wreath in their right hands. The women have white skin. Both men
      have red hair with a fillet, and wear black mantles over short white chitons. The chiton of
      the man in the left pair has incised folds, and a himation with incised stars. Below, two
      cocks between two sirens.</P><P>Side B: at center, an Amazon runs to right looking
      back to left. She carries a spear and a red shield with white dots at edge. Her red helmet has
      a black crest, and she wears a short black chiton decorated with stars. On the lower part of
      the chiton are three rows of white sirens or birds. To either side of her, a sphinx and a
      cock. Below, a warrior runs to left looking back to right with red shield and helmet with red
      crest. To the right is a ram and to the left, a panther.</P><P>On the neck are
      lotus and palmette festoons. On the shoulders are red and black tongues, on the central zone
      of the body, lotus and palmette festoons. At the base are rays.</P><P>The style of
      the scene is "Tyrrhenian".</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbea9ade43b900b1046027dadfa8b345ba1ce9af5ff0e69e5535d4d5fd5f8501> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Apollo standing with a laurel staff and a phiale"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbee26509cbaa351dbad15a29a8ffe1541a101a69181eff72e22a0e3d83a34b1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Sydenham 1952, no. 926</bibl>; <hi rend=\"ital\"><bibl>RRC</bibl></hi> no. 415/1, pl. LI; <hi rend=\"ital\"><bibl>BMCRR</bibl></hi> 418, no. 3373" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbf2f0809908a1db07eb2a57e358c4bfe398f6d1a71ce0391737d03f53252450> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Sides A and B: Dionysos between satyrs and maenads."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbf77c89b06b97cd17366f647856467a8c75241f6df97993d1f73e348df9759a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>All black except for a reserved band at the level of the
      handles, the insides of the handles, the side and bottom of the foot, stripes around the lower
      body and the inner lip, and a small disk in the center of the interior, the latter with a
      dotted circle in the center. Figure decoration is limited to the handle zones. Sides A and B
      are nearly identical: in the center is a sphinx seated to right, with white face and neck, and
      added red on the breasts and covert feathers; the tail is curled into an S-shape. On either
      side are two gesturing, nude men, both standing to right, but with the right one looking back
      at the sphinx. Both have red hair, and on one side the man at right has a red beard. Flanking
      this central trio are two beardless, red-haired men in himations, the latter with touches of
      added red.</P><P>On either side of the handles, tethered by undulating tendrils,
      are single, upright palmettes with fronds alternately red and black. Added red colors the
      fillet between foot and body.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cbf7edd20642d9f54c826faf933c7d5ab4d569c56154becb61aa61f1eede9fb5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Intact and in excellent condition. Fire a lighter black on the outside from a
      line mid-way down the body, probably because it was et within the mouth of another vessel in
      the kiln.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

