<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cd1d27800f7480503d73bc4c52e898c6277a97d3bd9379fe0a68189e4cce4310> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "A: warriors about to leave home. B: three youths."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cd269c2148a2023c66e3778eedf7ff9f4e056b6dba413f0edbc8b14593f64d9b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Under rim, diagonal symmetric palmettes,
      egg-and-dart.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side A:</hi> Sappho and Alcaeus
      each hold a barbiton and plectrum (attached to their arms by bands). Alcaeus, standing to the
      left in a pensive attitude, inclines his head downwards, but is singing, as the small "O"s
      issuing from his mouth show. He is barefoot, and wears a long, transparent chiton, a small
      mantle and a fillet around his head, and is barefoot. Sappho turns to listen to him, showing
      her face in a somewhat awkward three-quarter view, and prepares to answer his song with hers.
      She too wears a long transparent chiton but has a long, heavy mantle. The scene might refer to
      a competition between the two poets at a festival of Dionysos (who is depicted on the reverse
      of the vase).</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B:</hi> Dionysos and maenad.
      Dionysos standing at left offers maenad a kantharos.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cd27188181d98a18214763c923f67137580bf712cc6fb621db6ee56d6a034b0a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Champion warrior fighting with lance, possibly Ajax"@en ;
