<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cde290ca38972fac0806fa21b23f61d6a72b19365f95771d9cb39b55ba0350a4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Standing female figure wearing a peplos"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cdfe2bda74bb45d814194b74eec9f6cbacf2d1675a044a11f1f7b01b8f5a1474> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Above the scene on side A is a lotus-palmette band, while over
      side B's scene is a chain of opposing lotuses and palmettes. A band of rays appears on the
      lower body. Three red lines circle the foot of the vessel, and two each above the band of rays
      and beneath the scenes, as well as one each on the neck above the handles and on the upper
      edge of the rim. Two red lines are visible above the scenes, extending from handle attachment
      to handle attachment.</P><P>On side A, a charioteer stands on a quadriga, wearing
      a long chiton and holding a kentron as well as the reins. Next to him in the chariot is a
      bearded man wearing chiton and mantle. Behind the team of horses stand a woman and a hoplite
      facing each other. The woman is dressed in a peplos decorated with white lines and dots and
      two broad red areas, one one her chest and one at the garment's lower border, as well as a
      necklace and headband. The bearded hoplite wears a high-crested helmet that covers his face
      and holds a spear and shield, both partially visible behind the horses. On the far right, in
      front of the horses, stands a second woman in chiton, peplos, necklace, and headband. She is
      facing the others, and her garments are red striped, with white lines as decoration. Red is
      used on side A for the mane, forelock, tail, and breastband of the horse farthest forward, two
      horizontal stripes on the quadriga, the charioteer's beard and the hair, beard, and part of
      the mantle of the man next to him, the pupils, headbands, and stripes on the peploi of the
      women, and the helmet of the hoplite. White is used for the women's skin, the hindmost horse,
      dots on the edge of the peplos overfall of the righthand woman, and the lower edge of
      hoplite's helmet crest.</P><P>On side B a quadriga is shown frontally. The
      charioteer wears a white himation and holds a kentron. Red is used for a broad horizontal
      stripe on the chariot, the charioteer's hair, and the manes, forelocks, and breastbands of the
      horses.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ce00d841cd3cf5f41e661ba31ab7afa9875223effd8f0766618a665af959c9c6> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Side A: cocks between hens. Side B: goat between sirens."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

