<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ce285d25c71d169518b88bf8dfd0cf99eb5774d00451b627f56ce142ef7cd12a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>This tiny ovoid aryballos has four main zones of decoration.
      The uppermost, the neck, is modelled in the shape of a female head. The carefully defined
      features of the broad face are enframed by dark hair that hangs in straight locks to the
      shoulder of the vessel. The tapering body is divided into three distinct bands of decoration.
      Centered in the upper zone is a pendant lotus bud bisected by a delicate floral scroll that
      spreads around the shoulder. Below is a frieze of goats rendered in the black-figure
      technique. On the front of the vessel, two goats confront on e another and on the back a
      larger goat grazes. The empty areas above, below and between the animals are filled with pairs
      of chevrons and dot rosettes. At the base is a row of thin, pointed rays. The flat strap
      handle is decorated on its outer surface with a net pattern. Around the mouth are two
      overlapping rows of incised rays.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/ce3b67d2946bd65f4babe097b743358c047a5bbf0f6404dc14694a3f9157e759> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
