<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cf9c882ad3aac49f41626cc9275c1c03ca890e841a2ce58fb002c1370fec18af> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Two hunters on
      horseback pursue a deer to the left. The hunters are bearded and wear tunics of added red.
      They hold the reins with their right hands and hold a spear aloft in the left. The horses have
      red manes. Below the horse in the center is a hound, which like the deer and the horses on
      both sides, has both its forelegs in the air. The horse at the right has its weight back on
      its rear legs, as though rearing up, while the horse at center is stretched out in full
      gallop. The deer, possibly a stag, has already been hit by a spear, the point of which has
      pierced its back and emerged by its left shoulder. Added red is used to color the deer's
      breast and belly the spots on its rump.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: The composition is nearly the same as on Side A, but the chase is to the right,
      and whatever added color may have been used has disappeared. The deer's head is damaged, but
      traces of added red remain on the body.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cfb72b3c6c71991dd697fb55a3591837207f298d2b661ddd039816c81eb57b8f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
