    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cff2a7485a8b3b3e9d6387fe517d4980483f6440d65d4db0dfa2c68b920691f1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Two Theban youths,
      dressed in full cloaks with black borders, sit on folding stools, facing into the center of
      the composition. The youth on the left holds his hand (covered by his cloak) up near his face.
      The one on the right holds a staff in front of him. In between them is an Ionic fluted column,
      which supports a base decorated with egg-and-dart molding. On top of this sits a sphinx,
      facing right. Its wings are spread, and it sits in a half crouching position, with its
      hindquarters partly off the ground, and its tail in an S-curve behind it. The sphinx is
      apparently a statue, and can be compared to other sphinxes from monuments such as the brother
      and sister stele at the Metropolitan Museum, New York (Richter, figs. 96-109). The Nolan
      amphora in Boston (<rs type="vase">Boston 06.2447</rs>), by the Achilles Painter,
      depicts Oedipus and the Sphinx. It is more free and three-dimensional in its
      representation.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Two dancing
      ithyphallic satyrs are depicted. The satyr on the left is in profile to the right. He holds a
      drinking horn with his right hand, and a large pointed amphora with his left. His left leg is
      raised so that his thigh is parallel to the ground, and his right knee is slightly bent. The
      other satyr walks to the right, but turns his upper body back to wave at the first satyr with
      his right arm. The second satyr is bald, and holds a drinking horn in his left
      hand.</P><P>The borders are: Side A, above the figural band is a complex meander
      pattern, below the band is a meander and checker pattern; Side B, above the figural band a
      simple meander, below a wiggly line with florals (?). Under each handle is a
      palmette.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/cff957d24cde4a70cb0d9b6dccb3bc3a64ea530f252e43de1d344932b942148d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
