    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<P>Broken and repaired, with minor repainting.</P>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d1cd910b16715397e31ad83819b800091012432150f2ad291ec58ff52cb54e00> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Broken and repaired, with cracks and minor gaps restored. No large pieces are
      missing, and the surface is in generally good condition, with good preservation of the added
      colors. The glaze has flaked in some places, and there are gouges and
      nicks.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d1ce24ef0eea1c9bc5c4fdddf06ba2dc40f9bc8327be2b59576d0116e0769da0> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Sides A and B: young warriors in battle. Tondo: athlete."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d1e53150e731f7eb2ffe7ed3e6c5161996672a682836134ab4e15d39ba24df8f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Interior</hi>: Herakles
      sacrificing, assisted by a satyr. A fire burns on the altar which stands on the right.
      Herakles, unusually dressed in a long tunic worn over his lion skin, holds a kantharos in the
      fire, his other arm raised in a salutory gesture. A satyr stoops beside him, mostly hidden by
      Herakles. He holds over the fire the end of a long stick. Herakles' club leans against the
      tondo 'wall' behind him.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: satyr
      attacking a sleeping maenad. A naked maenad lies asleep, her head resting on one hand. She
      leans against a box or other square object covered by a cloth. Her hair is covered by a
      sakkos. The ithyphallic satyr crawls in from the left with his arms outstretched; one hand
      already grasps the sleeping girl's right arm.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: Herakles and Cerberus. Herakles, guided by Hermes, leads Cerberus out of hell.
      Hermes, walking to the left, looks back and gestures to Herakles with his left hand, his
      traveler's staff held in his right hand. Herakles, following at a run, in turn looks back at
      Cerberus who is here depicted with only two heads, both snarling. Hermes wears a chlamys,
      petasos and winged boots, Herakles a short chiton and his lion
      skin.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d1e610960abcf93042fc49b14387b8e23c5a553932943c6030a0ec842e289d8e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><bibl>CVA, USA 15, Cleveland 1, p. 11, pls.
      15-6</bibl>.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d1e759505c1d2a8b54ef7d87c31368e04d82a6d9264db82b3d1dd8109a3ed61b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> II, 352, no. 253; <bibl>Cohen 1880-1892, 1.479, no. 94</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d1f3e6b48f87c8c3a56aa08f4085e48145048419fa5cb10a5564b2fdee46f71c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A</hi>: Herakles and the
      Nemean Lion. Herakles struggles with the lion while Athena looks on. Herakles, on the left,
      has wrapped his left arm around the lion's neck, pushing downward with all his strength,
      forcing the lion's head to the ground. Herakles' fingers are locked together and his head
      rests in the lion's mane. The lion mouth is open, his tongue hanging out, as he struggles with
      Herakles, trying to push his head away with his left rear foot. Athena stands behind the two
      facing right. She is holding her spear in her right hand and gestures with her left, and is
      shown dressed in a chiton and her aegis. Herakles is bearded and naked, his mantle hanging on
      the right and his quiver on the left</P><P><hi rend="head">Side
      B</hi>: Hermes, Herakles and a female(?) figure. This side is badly damaged, but Hermes
      can be identified on the left by his winged boots, short mantle and staff. The lion skin
      identifies the figure on the right as Herakles. A third figure in the center is dressed in a
      long chiton with a meander pattern on the bottom border. This figure can probably be
      identified as female.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

