<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d3035923efd92a8acda819b7d2af071b512e0617288d1ed9e44555fdeaefee5d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The vessel has an echinus mouth with a flat and unglazed top.
      There are rays on the mouth, interrupted above the handles. The neck is glazed entirely on the
      inside. There is a fillet between the mouth and neck and between the neck and the body. The
      vase has a spreading foot, which is glazed on the top only, and there is a nipple on the
      underside of the foot. On the neck is an alternating palmette and bud chain, with dots in the
      links. There are two lines above this design, and one below. There is a ring between the body
      and the foot; there are rays above the foot, and a chain of upright lotus buds with dotted
      interstices, framed by triple lines above. An enclosed tongue pattern and lotus-palmette chain
      decorates the shoulder and continues under the handles. The handles are tripartite, and
      unglazed on the inside. At the root of the handles is a row of pendant filled triangles. The
      handle sides are decorated with a large hanging rose with four layers of petals. The the right
      and left of the rose's stem develop four large running volute scrolls arranged in a square.
      Two pairs of fan palmettes occupy the top and bottom spandrel, and there is a black lozenge
      between each lateral spandrel. A black triangle framed laterally by a glaze line occupies the
      central spandrel underneath the handles.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      A</hi>: A duel is depicted. The left warrior is sinking to his knees, while the one on
      the right advances on him. They both have swords and shields: the warrior on the left carries
      a Boeotian shield while the warrior on the right carries a round shield. The shield of the
      right hand warrior, seen from the outside, has the device of an incised whorl. There is a
      nonsense inscription in the field.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>:
      Both warriors have their swords sheathed and fight with spears and round shields. The warrior
      on the right is turning to flee; his shield device is a panther protome. Each warrior wears a
      low-crested Corinthian helmet with a bell corselet over a short-sleeved chiton, and greaves.
      Their scabbards are hung at their sides by baldrics. There is a nonsense inscription in the
      field.</P><P>Some of the decorative borders of the vase are highlighted with red
      paint, as are the helmets, greaves, chiton folds, and parts of the warriors' shields. The
      irises and whites of the warriors' eyes, the hilts of their swords, and details of the panther
      protome are painted white.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d30b9889c6678a94b0f208bfec60bd511bdd8bd1fa442114343d5a0ff6ccd390> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Decoration in white paint, much of which has flaked off making the scene
      difficult to interpret.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d311d172f39c8be3e4a5c16e6a308b8bc52a3910ee4af01ccdc1bc846056ddbf> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
