<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d36cf9bf93751aec716e92d70f2172d78e851893c4d4528ddfc0034d280d4ac4> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> II, 247, no. 140, var. (AVG written without cross bar)." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d36d9067c821b7cc44499433b12941aabdc21ec63759723aeba837fee3ba6aa1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: An older man, nude
      except for a cloak draped over his shoulders, walks to the right and looks over his shoulder.
      He carries a barbiton (stringed instrument) in his left hand. He seems to be distracted by
      something behind him, and so is not playing the instrument; however, his fingers are poised on
      the strings and he holds the plectrum with his right hand. He holds a walking stick under his
      left arm. "His lithe body is strangely both tense and languid; his muscles and sinews are
      taut, but his down-turned head and slightly flexed knees impart a sense of languorous grace."
      (Williams, 41). The lower border is a band of stopped meanders alternating with patterned
      squares (crosses and dotted saltires).</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: A young reveler walks to the right. He holds a staff in his right hand and a
      kylix in his left. He wears a wreath in his hair and a cloak draped about his shoulders. The
      border below his feet is a meander pattern.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d37afcf37026b8e2329562268468a717b2dbd779afa6078e47e830c3ed37cf15> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Theseus and a boar. Theseus is on one side of the handle and
      the boar is on the other. Theseus is running to the left with outstretched arms, and looks
      back to the right. He is holding a club or sling in his right hand. A garment is draped over
      his left arm. Theseus is naked but wears a hat with a hemi-spherical crown and a short brim.
      The boar is running to the left, toward Theseus, his teeth
      bared.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d387be59572446786ef935b51d039cdd81c821bbe4c76615e66ead25db80056a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
