<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d4530eb9af608e2a4e333f7e4566ba2f12dbe8e3f6b39b019a01588d983c5b1f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>This vase is thought to have commemorated a choral victory,
      perhaps at the Thargelia festival, as suggested by the presence of Apollo. It would then have
      been commissioned by the choregos.</P><P>A: Centauromachy?</P><P>B
      (upper level): Nike flying profile to the right, wearing a sleeveless, belted chiton,
      decorated a short pony tail, and a white-peaked crown, bends her right arm at waist level, and
      reaches her left arm (missing beyond the shoulder) to the right; Dionysos (head, neck, upper
      torso, and feet missing) seated 3/4-view to the left, wearing a himation around his legs,
      holds a thyrsos (?) diagonally in his lowered right hand, and holds his left arm in front of
      his body; a winged female figure (Hygieia?), standing profile to the right, bends her right
      arm at her side, and reaches her left arm up to decorate a trophy; a winged Nike (labelled
      above her head) (only top of head, wings, lower legs preserved), standing profile to the left,
      with her weight on her advanced left leg, presumably also decorating the trophy; Apollo
      (labelled above his lyre) (left leg, lower torso, left elbow, and right hand missing, upper
      torso details indistinct), seated 3/4-view to the right, with his head profile to the left,
      wearing a himation around his legs, and an olive wreath, holds a lyre in his left arm, and
      rests his right hand on his seat (rock?); a female figure (only the back of neck and hair, the
      right shoulder, and the legs below the thighs are preserved), standing profile to the right,
      wearing a sleeveless chiton, and a long pony tail, holds a thyrsos (?); a satyr (?), dancing
      to the left (only lower legs are preserved); Komoidia (?), standing (or seated?) 3/4-view to
      the left (only head, shoulders, and mask held up in right hand are preserved, details lost),
      wearing a sleeved chiton (?), and a sphendone with an ivy wreath above, rests a thyrsos on his
      left shoulder; below, a small animal (griffin?), profile to the right; an acanthus column,
      aligned almost directly below the tripod; more (missing) figures, including Galene (labelled),
      a satyr seated 3/4-back-view to the right (the left of his head, his left arm, and his feet
      are missing), wearing an ivy wreath, raises an oinochoe in his right hand; below, a maenad; a
      satyr dancing (?, only feet preserved, one profile to the left, and one nearly frontal); a
      maenad seated 3/4-view to the right (only her head and the bottom of her drapery are
      preserved), with her head profile to the left, tilted up, wearing a sphendone (with a
      wreath?); a maenad standing profile (?) to the left (only the back of her head and her right
      forearm are preserved), wearing a pony tail, holds a mask with straight hair in her upraised
      right hand; Paidia (labelled above her head), standing 3/4-view to the left, wearing a
      sleeveless chiton, a long pony tail, and an ivy wreath, holds a thyrsos to the left in her
      right hand, and holds her left arm back, at her side.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

