<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d6d784d433c09a924b69c433e0f58923134e9e8f47063907a0556446441cac2d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A (upper level): A female figure, perhaps Erato (labelled)
      standing 3/4-view to the left, with her right foot raised on a rock, bent at the waist,
      wearing a sleeveless, belted chiton with a kolpos and shoulder straps, and a rayed ovolo
      taenia, black hoop earrings, and a black band necklace, rests a tympanon (decorated with a
      wreath on its rim, and maeanders on its edge) on her right knee, the top of which she holds
      with her right hand, while she plays it with her left hand; Mousaios (labelled), seated
      3/4-view to the right, wearing a patterned, long-sleeved, oriental tunic, a chlamys draped
      down his back, calf-length leather boots, a laurel wreath, rests a kithara on his left knee,
      which he plays with both hands; above him and to the right, nude, red, winged Pothos
      (labelled), leaning 3/4-view to the right on the shoulder of Kalliope, with his left arm,
      weight on his right leg, left leg pulled back, wearing a red taenia, points his right hand
      down and to the right; Kalliope (labelled), seated 3/4-view to the right, with her legs
      crossed, and her head turned 3/4-view to the left, wearing a spangled himation draped over her
      legs, under her hips and back, over a medium-, button-sleeved, belted chiton, a rayed
      cross-hatched sphendone, black hoop earrings, and a black band necklace; Harmonia (labelled),
      emerging from behind a hill (only shown above her hips), wearing a belted, short-sleeved
      chiton, with shoulder straps, a black band necklace, two white bands on each wrist, and a
      short pony tail, holds her right hand below her chest, and her left hand above her left
      shoulder.</P><P>A (lower level): Melpomene (labelled), seated near profile to the
      right, with her legs crossed, wearing a bordered himation draped over her legs, over a belted,
      medium-sleeved chiton, a black band necklace, black hoop earrings, a rayed ovolo taenia, holds
      a harp on her lap, which she plays with both hands; Deiope (labelled), seated 3/4-view to the
      right, with her legs crossed, wearing a bordered himation draped around her legs, over a
      belted, medium-sleeved chiton, a black band necklace, black hoop earrings, a rayed,
      cross-hatched sphendone, holds her left hand on her knee, and raises her right hand slightly
      to the right, on the back of which is perched a small bird); she looks down to the nude baby,
      Eumolpos (labelled above his head), kneeling profile to the left, wearing a black band on his
      right wrist, and a black strap with trinket attached, draped over his right shoulder; he
      reaches his right hand up to Deiope, and lowers his left hand slightly; a short tree; nude,
      red Eros, with frontal wings, standing 3/4-view to the right, perched behind Aphrodite's right
      shoulder, with weight on his right leg, and his left leg relaxed, wearing a rayed taenia,
      points his right hand down to the left, and holds his left hand above his shoulder (in a
      speaking gesture?); Aphrodite (labelled above her right shoulder), seated 3/4-view to the
      left, with her legs crossed, wearing a spangled bordered himation over her legs, over a
      belted, medium-sleeved chiton with an overfold, sandals, a black band necklace, black hoop
      earrings, and a cross-hatched sphendone, with a rayed maeander ampyx, rests her left hand on
      her seat, and her right hand on her knee; Terpsichora (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the
      left, with her head 3/4-view to the right, weight on her right leg, left leg relaxed, wearing
      a belted peplos, a rayed ovolo taenia, a black band necklace, black hoop earrings, holds a
      plectron in her lowered right hand, and a lyre in her slightly raised left hand; Peitho
      (labelled), seated 3/4-view to the left, with her right foot raised on a rock (?), wearing a
      himation draped over her legs and up her back, over a medium-sleeved, belted chiton, sandals,
      a black band necklace, two white bands on her right wrist, black hoop earring (fugitive), over
      a rayed patterned sphendone, looks up at Terpsichora.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d6d7fe1ef8b53e39578e1d73a7ea7285583777f204ad853bbb6bb1e9d7de2a10> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Black glaze on the interior has flaked off in places and worn away in others,
      so that the red wash beneath is visible. There is incrustation under the handles and on the
      underside of the foot.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

