<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d7ae9972aca3f0c9701e31e719024969e914ae94e56e67524af36075330d64ad> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """B. Caprez-Csornay, "The Andrs Alfldi Collection," <hi rend="ital">Museum of
      Fine Arts, Budapest. Newsletter</hi> (undated); <bibl>Shapiro 1993</bibl>,
      74-75, 235 no. 23, figs. 26-27; <bibl>Add2</bibl>, 364; <bibl>Boardman
      1989a</bibl>, fig. 301; <bibl>LIMC</bibl>, 4.49 s.v. Eukleia no. 2, pl. 22
      (A. Kossatz-Deissmann), 64 s.v. Eunomia no. 10 (A. Kossatz-Deissmann); I. Wehgartner, "Das
      Ideal massvoller Liebe auf einem attischen Vasenbild. Neues zur Lekythos F 2705 im Berliner
      Antikenmuseum," <hi rend="ital">JdI</hi> 102 (1987) 195 fig. 8;
      <bibl>LIMC</bibl>, 2.274 s.v. Apollon no. 733 (B. Lambrinudakis et al.); D.
      Cramers and E. Simon, "Ein neues Werk des Meidiasmalers," <hi rend="ital">AA</hi>
      1978, 71 n. 8; J.G. Szilgyi and M. Szbo, Antik Killts (Budapest 1974) 51-52 fig. 31;
      <bibl>Hamdorf 1964</bibl> 111 no. 440f; <bibl>Hampe 1955</bibl>, 120g,
      121; <bibl>Mtzger 1951</bibl>, 19; <bibl>Schefold 1937</bibl>, 63,
      71-72, figs. 20-23""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d7bc75c3fac94a6f4ba28c2bec02f7a9ea4701171a046d4e3de2b5269cd2c849> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Symposium. Side A: Dionysos and satyr reclining. Side B: Satyr drawing wine."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d7c97e82795d51a478100c7f51a6a11c6326de492195ddd492e1c92cbe44c171> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Tondo</hi>: The figure decoration
      is confined to the tondo in the interior. A woman stands to right on a reserved exergue.
      Before her at right is an altar on a one-step base, with a cymatium molding topped by volutes.
      The blood on the side of the altar is drawn with dilute glaze. The woman wears a sakkos and a
      spotted peplos with a border of running S's. With her right hand she holds out a phiale of
      wine, which she will pour on the altar as a sacrifice. Behind her, at left, is the corner of a
      building, with a plain anta at the corner and a door decorated with bands of dotted circles
      separated by brown zigzags. The escutcheon on the upper panel may be a knocker; the
      star-shaped ornament on the lower panel may be a keyhole.</P><P>The tondo frame is
      a simple reserved stripe. The exterior is black and undecorated. The insides of the handles,
      the space between the handle roots, and the side of the foot are reserved. The fillet above
      the foot is framed with reserved stripes.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

