<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d940df5fb620fa80742d81e84d826a6ef8f21a54a96cc811f90c4e5cdb53c5d7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>On sides A and B, over a maeander band, a continuous scene of
      five men and a flute player at a symposion. <hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: three men
      in a drinking party (symposion). Three men draped in himations are lying on decorated cushions
      and talk gesticulating with their arms. All three have beards and curly black hair and hold
      drinking vessels in their left hands. The first from left, looking to the right, holds a cup.
      The second, looking to the left, holds also a cup, and the one at right, faces to left and
      holds a skyphos. On the wall behind them is hanging a basket.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Two men and a flute player. Two more men belonging to the
      same scene as in A, are lying on cushions, draped in himations. Both men, first and second
      figures from left, turn their heads to look at a youth playing the double flute (aulos) behind
      them. The men are bearded and have curly black hair. The one at left holds a skyphos in his
      left hand and the one in the middle, a cup. The flute player, rightmost figure, wears a tunic
      or mantle around his lower body and leans on a decorated cushion.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Tondo</hi>: A seated youth with a lyre. A black haired youth is sitting
      on a stool, holding a lyre in his left hand, while his right hand goes back as he were ready
      to start playing. He is draped in a himation and wears shoes open in the
      front.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d9474b9fe3015468658f84bbab212808da7d600f762870706430382e0d34a883> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Most of the red of the woman's chiton and tainiai worn away, as is the upper
      layer of the man's chlamys; small losses from the white ground along the breaks and
      elsewhere.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

