<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/db2b70c579702f33af8d60d608a314585ff5294f48405139a9ab631747da6466> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Richter 1984, 131-33, figs. 94-95 (with previous bibliography)</bibl>; <bibl>Richter 1954, 66-67 no. 103</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/db2b7d27dfce97da7064f91334ac0982a6523dd703467ec6bb15d674a6afea09> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The body is divided into three registers. Animals fill the top
      two, with lotus buds and flowers in the lowest. Top register (shoulder): a kneeling stag is
      flanked by a griffin and sphinx. Middle register: four wild goats are grazing to the right.
      Guilloche appears around the neck. Varied filling ornaments are
      used.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/db35d3dfb5424224abbda3535fb2a698b3b7faa1fc297013a4504ddbc69b4ff6> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Tondo: A nude satyr, wearing a red fillet tied around his head,
      is shown in a frontal pose, with his head turned profile to the left; he dances, with his
      weight temporarily on his right leg, holds both hands on his waist, and looks down at a table
      to the left, on which a kantharos rests.</P><P>Side A: A youth, wearing a
      himation, leans 3/4-view to the right, on his staff, and holds his hand on his hip. A second
      youth, wearing a himation and a narrow red taenia, sits profile to the right on a box, and
      plays a lyre; behind him is a cross ornament. A third youth, wearing a himation, leans profile
      to the left, on his staff, and holds a sprig forward, in his right hand, as a gesture to the
      musician.</P><P>Side B: A youth, wearing a himation, sits near profile to the
      right on a box; he holds a sprig in his right hand, and a staff upright in his left hand. A
      second youth, swathed in a himation, sits profile to the right on a box; behind him is a cross
      ornament. A third youth, wearing a himation, leans profile to the left, on his staff, and
      holds his right hand in front of his face, in a speaking gesture.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

