    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e2b2f5c9799268a5abc10a0c0e8001c50388b950e69a148ca88140433ef9b641> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> II, 119, no. 553; <bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">RIC</hi></bibl> II, 69, no. 439" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e2b42707dc0387854f6e5408176e2b43c21171c9896ed0efcadbcee014e016f9> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Some important parts of the figure of Pegasos have been restored--the upper
      section of the head, central areas of the wing and hind leg, and the tail.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e2b503ff5e65a754d083b8f84ec612e2c5341cd5aa0532b5f332be0cc13daf60> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: On the left, a man
      stands leaning with his right hand on the border, and with his left supports a shield balanced
      on the ground. His right leg is crossed casually in front of his left. He wears a short
      embroidered chiton, leggings, and lace-up boots, all of which are traditional Oscan costume.
      He looks towards a woman at the center of the composition, who is walking in profile to the
      right. She wears a long crinkly peplos with an overfold to her knees (the portrayal of this
      type of dress is characteristic of the painter); her hair is bound up in a scarf. She pours an
      offering from the vessel she is holding (which is a nestoris, an Italian vessel shape) into
      the phiale held by the youth at right. He is dressed in Oscan costume, like the first man, and
      is leading a horse off to the right.</P><P>Trendall (1989, p. 24) notes that this
      is one of the first Apulian vases to show people wearing native costume. The representation of
      the nestoris is also unusual.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Four
      draped youths. On the left, a youth is shown frontally, with his head in profile to the right.
      His right hand is on a staff, and his left on his hip. He wears a himation draped to leave his
      chest and right shoulder free. An animal leg (?) is suspended on the wall in the background.
      It is also present in the composition of <rs type="vase">Matera 9978 (no.
      63)</rs>, but there is no explanation for it. To the right a youth wearing a diadem
      stands in profile to the left, as if in conversation with the first character. He is wrapped
      in a himation with a black border, so that only his feet and head show. On the wall to the
      right is a set of hand weights. The third youth to the right wears a himation like the first.
      He stands frontally, with head in profile to the right. His right arm is extended, and he
      holds a staff. His left hand is on his hip. A cross-shaped object is suspended from the wall
      to his right. The last youth stands in profile to the left. He is completely wrapped in a
      himation like the first one.</P><P>The rim of the vessel is decorated with a olive
      wreath border, while the neck has an ivy and berry pattern. The upper border of the figural
      scene is a tongue pattern, while the lower is a maeander and crosses. In the center of the
      composition on Side A, hanging from the upper border, is a semicircular pattern decorated with
      rays and a spiral pattern. The vertical borders are a pattern of checks.</P><P>The
      Sisyphus Painter is "A highly competent draughtsman, but his larger compositions lack unity,
      being often arranged in studied groups, which seem to be inspired by sculptural originals,
      like the Parthenon and Phigaleia friezes." (<bibl>Trendall 1966, p.
      19</bibl>).</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e2c3a29670a239135a60cf79984f95f201afa9523a55770ddbc9c03a1f87973c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Lewes 1920</bibl>, no. 38" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e2ee25d5cfa6b9b79a4f967406e7ec4c1a8b68d56110c0796c6e9bd1fad01a97> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
