<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e50455e22e09b2cf2a0d8270019aff17eca40e94129afcb5746b458958e25a2b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Side A: Dionysos reclining on his left elbow, looking right, on
      a kline with its legs below the ground line. His himation has fallen to his waist and covers
      his legs. He wears a wreath. Eyes appear to either side with two concentric white circles at
      the centers. Behind are grapevines.</P><P>Side B: Dionysos, wearing himation, sits
      to right on a folding stool. He holds a keros, or drinking horn, in his left hand. His right
      arm is hidden. Behind are grapevines. There are eyes, as on Side A.</P><P>Below
      the neck on the shoulder are black tongues. On the neck are three linked black palmettes on
      each side. A zone of rays is seen on the lower body.</P><P>Lid: a black knob with
      reserved bands; at the edge is an ivy vine with red stem and black
      leaves.</P><P>On the class of neck amphorae with pictures on the shoulder, see
      <bibl>ABV, 276</bibl>.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

