<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e6f3f541d1d69e3d69e914ad99922c8fbb74aa8095730c6ee291ff1a724b98cd> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "A worshiper approaches Aphrodite (?) and an attendant"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e6fd596eace23977e13c31a2aaa0ced1a8d91f63c56d1f69d05c8ee89d488415> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> At the left, a satyr
      carries what looks to be a stamnos with ivy garland decoration in his arms. He wears a wreath
      with added purple berries (korymboi). Dionysos reclines backwards on a goat holding a
      kantharos out in his extended arm. He grasps the goat around the neck holding onto its horns.
      His garments are an Ionic chiton with dilute glaze folds and a himation. The goat has dilute
      glaze on its forehead and upper beard. Black glaze relief lines are used for both animals'
      (sides A and B) horns, ears and eyes. A satyr at the right carries a wineskin on his
      shoulder.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side B:</hi> Hermes reclines backwards
      on a ram, holding a kantharos in one hand and a staff in his arm. He wears chitoniskos,
      chlamys, petasos at the back with added red ties, and winged boots. His beard is done in
      dilute glaze. The latter is also use for the ram's fur between the horns and overall curls;
      the horns have added red ribs and its tongue is in added purple. Hermes extends one arm to the
      satyr at the left (wearing an ivy wreath in added purple) who plays the double pipes (aulos);
      the animal skin case hangs from his arm. The satyr at the right carries a vat (or bell krater)
      with an ivy garland on his shoulders and a wine skin slung over his arm.</P><P>A
      narrow band of tongues decorates the top of the shoulder where the neck would have
      joined.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e6ff8a0a054f2fcf3cdbf56ba01b24ca29659ae81d3d139d2386f0cab2efa0f0> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Side A: Dionysos and satyr. Side B: satyr. Tondo: armed dancer and
      Hippalektryon"""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e71808c75f656d811ee73a7ac4336c0389f67ddeb747ee0e8cb24bd2e05a2862> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
