      2</bibl></P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e83a631e28a5159bf60b08b065aef76ddda285f89861f1d102703c4fbe6b4a0f> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Some lime accretions remain on the surface; otherwise it is in very good
      condition.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e84476a8f16a1a549e825b89d663a0e23becdb7032e64a208833dc9fce6f3467> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> I, see note on 304 and pl. 51, 16" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e845f1180c84a0407a2693ab969e13f01f4dd5f7770131bc604cb607b62dcff7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Eutychia (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the right, with weight on her
      left leg, wearing a sleeveless, belted chiton, a rayed stephane with a spangled design (which
      also looks like four unintelligible characters of a word) and a bun, two bands on her right
      wrist, a beaded relief necklace, dotted disk earring, holds a white chain with five beads, in
      her lowered right hand, and a footed box with three dots (fruit?) above it, in her left hand,
      with her left arm bent; Eunomia (labelled), standing near profile to the right, with weight on
      her left leg, wearing a sleeveless chiton belted over a long kolpos, cross-bands on her chest,
      a rayed, maeander-patterned taenia over a bun, two relief bands on each wrist, a black band
      necklace, a relief bead earring, tilts her head down, looking at a white chain with three
      beads, held between her raised right hand and her lowered left hand, both arms bent; Paidia
      (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the left, with weight on her right leg, wearing a belted,
      sleeveless chiton, a single black band necklace, dotted disk earrings, a high pony tail tied
      with a string with white baubles, a ringlet hanging in front of her left ear, an two relief
      bands on her left wrist, holds to the left a footed box (identical to that held by Eutychia)
      with two dots atop (fruit), in both arms, bent at waist level; she slightly obscures a
      cushioned stool.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e847718396357e61b7a61f2c46e2a4655a4d859def53c3b5ffcdde67279936db> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The vase has been reduced to a large fragment, consisting mainly of one figure
      panel and a small portion of the neck. The fragment is itself repaired from many smaller
      fragments. Lost in the large gap in the center, now restored in plaster, are the bodies of the
      horses at right and the head and upper body of the groom. The man holding the reins has lost
      his head and torso. The added white of the charioteer's chiton has worn off at the top but not
      the bottom. At both left and right, drill holes connected by shallow channels once held metal
      rivets and staples from an ancient repair; the repair at right had a triangular
      shape.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e84bf9cf19c64cb98f994a5c358d477a6371e5dc421395681320dec160e3c6c3> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Bearded Prometheus (labelled), standing 3/4-view to the right (only
      head, shoulders, and upper arms preserved), wearing an olive wreath, white hair, upper body
      nude, bending slightly to the right, both arms held slightly forward; Leda (labelled) and
      Athena (labelled ); head and left shoulder of a figure with curly hair and animal horns,
      pointed ears (Pan?), head tilting down; outstretched arm of Peitho (labelled retrograde), and
      part of her right shoulder, wearing a button-sleeved chiton; head and left shoulder of an
      unbearded youth (?), standing 3/4-view to the left, short curly hair, wearing a chlamys
      fastened on her left shoulder, and a chiton (?) billowing behind the neck (?); head of
      Timandra (labelled), daughter of Tyndareus and Leda, standing 3/4-view to the right, her head
      tilted slightly down, wearing a button-sleeved chiton, short curly hair tied with a taenia;
      head and part of the right shoulder of female figure standing 3/4-view to the left, tilting
      her head down, dark curly hair bound by taenia with maeander pattern (labelled, to the left of
      the head.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e85e5f55ab8744ed58def9abd0b5ba18732bbfb325c0728a5da6b7b87b41c2f3> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Karouzou 1968, 131-32, pl. 41</bibl>; <bibl>Svoronos 1903-12, pl. 105</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8601d89efced9af9de24aa56a79473317b13794601732087b2c3fb6bd2d6612> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Stadium with seating and colonnade along north; located directly inside the south wall of the city, adjacent to the lower gymnasium."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e868ef35431844f3519e96eaf0dc7ba93cbea41a51dea70f6a91a586be77bf2d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Tondo</hi>: bearded satyr runs to
      right and looks back holding animal wineskin with both hands. Tail and ivy wreath on head in
      added red.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e86c978b925fb74a9cc763da941d916138726a380f85767ed1b42a15ead7fdf6> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Smith 1991, 64, fig. 68</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e86cf72694e68f760c3ad15a097755d630052b4953ce1b11fefbd7d90a572501> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> III, 338, no. 785, with reverse legend; <bibl>Comstock 1975, 22-23, illus.</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e86db9fe510260e925c29d9b049ef56a3a9cd64a4cabe0346a88b49822d012b6> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><bibl>CVA, USA fasc. 17, p. 27, pl. 40, 3 and
      4</bibl></P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e870b61278bd7a3b1f35022c0f860135e71feff8cbed44476870cebdfbcf8688> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The mouth (except the top), and the outer surfaces of the feet
      and lugs are black. On each circular side there is a black stripe around the edge, then a
      broad black band circling a reserved tondo, the latter decorated with a four-spoked wheel with
      a double rim. There are three black stripes on top of each handle and on the bottom of each
      foot.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e87bd07dd4da7c4d5943c4870cea1e415a81d566dc7f10824887a10e3a5b8d5e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A</hi>: Nike between two
      youths. A Nike hovers in the air between two youths, her wings spread, her knees bent and her
      toes almost touching the ground. She is holding a piece of cloth stretched between her
      outstretched arms, and looks to the right toward one of the youths. She is wearing a chiton
      and himation. The youth on the right faces the Nike, his right hand resting on a staff. He is
      wearing a mantle. The youth on the left stands facing forward, his head turned toward the
      Nike. He also wears a mantle.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B</hi>: Nike
      between two youths. A Nike, her wings spread, has landed and is walking toward the youth on
      the right with outstretched arms. She is dressed in a chiton, a short himation, and a sakkos.
      The youth on the right stands with his right arm resting on his staff, looking toward the
      Nike. The youth on the left stands facing forward, his head turned toward the two on the
      right. The fingers of his left hand, held at his side, are spread wide. Both youths wear
      mantles. A wide, open vessel on two tall legs sits on the ground between the Nike and the
      youth on the right.</P><P><hi rend="head">Interior</hi>: two standing
      boys. Two boys wrapped in mantles stand facing one another, the boy on the left stepping
      forward as he speaks to the one on the right. The hands of both boys are hidden by their
      mantles. The boy on the left wears his pulled partially over his head, while the mantle of the
      boy on the right is knotted at the back of the neck.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e87f52eaab16730d11c3bf3a87f736a723a4907d2c55d12fb4eeaf175976d19e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """A chariot proceeds to the closed door of the house of Admetos: Alkestis,
      Admetos, Apollo, behind the horses, with laurel crown, kithara, and plektron; Artemis, wearing
      a peplos and a sphendone, holds torches; Hermes; Peitho, standing frontal, with her head
      turned to the right, wearing a chiton, a himation, and a taenia, holding a dinos (?) on her
      head.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e891917e4036883b67d84633d19a89272685b9d6ab75d97d92a5081dc5fd9b08> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Brouskari 1974, 139, fig. 267 (with previous bibliography)</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8a2027544ca0466fd5cd894665bf5e850d2d3d6c10e84ccefbe4effb059194d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>To the right of the handle, there is a youth on horseback,
      facing right, with a small regardant bird in front of him. The youth's short pants (or
      chiton?) are painted red, as are alternate strands of the horse's mane, breast, and rear
      flank. The neck of the bird has red dots, and its wing cap and alternate feathers are also
      red. To the right, there is a serpent with four coils, tail near the bottom of the panel and
      head near the top. Incised circles and ovals decorate its body, with a scale pattern on the
      belly. Its mouth is open and tongue darting. It is flanked by two cocks, facing inward. They
      have incised rows of parallel lines on their necks and double rows of tail feathers. There is
      a smooth reddish-brown enhancement (over jet black, lustrous paint) on their combs, part of
      the pouch under their beaks, wing caps, and alternate tail feathers. To the right of the cock
      is a sphinx facing left. It has a raised sickle-shaped wing, and there is red paint on its
      face, wing cap, and alternate feathers. For filling ornament, there are three small rosettes
      with double center rings below the serpent, one above each cock, one between the cock and
      sphinx, and one over the hindquarters of the horse.</P><P>On the lowest band are
      rays, above which is a thick band of black. The neck, mouth, and handle are black, with a
      relief ring at the neck painted red.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8a4ea3bd01db9685ce3cd9ee971cf7ac632313885d6723bce2e4d70976d8574> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Lewes 1920</bibl>, no. 24" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8aaff48ebd3863ab1d2ea71c3ccedafc0b4d63918a60f8ee4877849ee337d28> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Side A: Helios (Sun) riding a quadriga of four winged horses, among diving and swimming
      youths<lb>Side B: Eos pursuing Kephalos, accompanied by a dog, and preceded by the
      veiled figure of Selene (goddess of the Moon), riding on horseback"""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8b4d68c3fda85547f981f4368c7091901d6355d56edbd3c4b9ce580c5f16156> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Danae and Perseus in chest. Danae, drawn in outline, rises from
      the chest, clad in a chiton and himation; the latter worn over the back of her head. She faces
      right. In front of her is her son Perseus (whose head and neck alone appear) with long black
      hair. The chest is decorated with dots and rays and has claw feet. Against the white of the
      raised chest lid fly four sea birds.</P><P>On the shoulder where the shoulder
      meets the neck are rays/tongues. On the body above the design is a running meander band broken
      up with squares with reserved crosses.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8bc70afc5ea92c2bfc9c7b08f6a836f3e5d7e893f6222e0963802f141709e45> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Smith 1997</bibl>, cat. DR 34; <bibl>Lawton 1995</bibl>, 153 no. 167, pl. 87 (with previous bibliography); <bibl>Svoronos 1903-12, 669 no. 448.2, pl. 221.2</bibl>." ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8c35b00523937b5dfd759ea056e660a74c0aa065e4dd40d7c3c8dfc4cd2561a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
