      (1987), Acquisitions 1986, pp. 162-163, no. 12</bibl>.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8c8d4b0fe81d8cd9f80b5f7519d55988a95114992bcee0380376c74cb2739c1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Aphrodite wearing an unbelted chiton"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8c8e6cec105645d05770da2413bdb5fd2a7736b832b9d2f5f304051bd24f242> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Hamiaux 1992, no. 126</bibl>; <bibl>Boardman 1988, 11ff.</bibl>; <bibl>Parthenon-Kongress, (Marcad and Pinatel)</bibl>; <bibl>Brommer 1977, 121-3</bibl>; <bibl>Picard/Manuel, 2.468</bibl>; <bibl>Froehner 1876, 152ff.</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8caba2f216a8fbe2ee00fa2de3134b7408cfde13ecd62d68b875722eef673c3> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<P>Much black glaze fired red.</P>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8cdd044a23393718b41516e0b3c49834897778eff1dd9938f6212b216688017> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "House with many rooms; at the southeast corner of the Sanctuary of Zeus (Altis), among the ruins of the Southeast Building and the East Baths."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8d0a7f2d1cd6ef1293e7843b61411a9a914bafedc96b3d90aaed444834cc9b0> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Retaining wall; in the Sanctuary of Apollo, north of the Temple of Apollo and protecting the Sacred Way."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8d202880ac0c8699280710337e4db844baef6135c7ef751667e082095d17cb1> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Broken and repaired from numerous fragments, with some repainting of cracks and
      wide fissures. The edges of the fragments are worn and irregular. The painted surface is
      eroded in places, with loss of relief lines, particularly in the very center of the interior,
      where the right arms and hands of both figures are lost, and the satyr and maenad on the right
      of side B.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8d3c6d9bbdd23ea7ef56e59b67a8544975e10527a34b206299d33ceb0013f46> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Two seated women and a standing figure"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8de3e425955177298beaf976b775768208923c2b09ff2c417ab4a7b6d5a690e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Continuous animal frieze. A siren with wings spread forms the
      focus of the frieze on one side, since all the animals turn towards her. The siren faces right
      and is shown with body and wings in three-quarters profile, head and tail in profile. Added
      red decorates her wings, tail and breast. She is flanked by griffin birds with curled wings.
      Panthers stand behind each of the birds. Opposite the siren is a lotus-palmette with an
      attached upright bud on each side. It is flanked by griffin birds with raised wings. Filling
      motifs of dots, blobs and small and large incised rosettes cover the
      field.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8ec09fe1a61354ca6d1a4728baa37cb256d003c6888e28f5acdf0d039f86795> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Helen, seated on a chair, surrounded by Paris (in Oriental costume), women, youths, and
      Erotes"""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8edea5ccaae9ae2effd4e472591ad8d12f69f2c41494778846faa16611c3f99> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Tondo</hi>: a Silen seated astride
      a wine-skin with a rhyton. His bald head is wreathed with ivy, and long locks of hair fall to
      his shoulders. He holds a horn rhyton in his left hand, and looks down at his right hand which
      is held in front of him. In the field, <foreign lang="Greek">*I*P*P*A*R*X*O*S
      *K*A*L*O*S</foreign> ("Hipparchos is beautiful"); on the wine-skin, <foreign
      lang="Greek">*I*P*P*A*O*X*O</foreign>, probably the same
      name.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8f6b564ca0a2f0b6c9ae7853449a0422d3b6604e82c0db9f057bb66c06ba8a2> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "A small imperial Roman temple, distyle in antis, perhaps dedicated to the cult of the Gallic spring god, Bormus (Borvo)."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e8ff102eed4ded6d1d18dbd124677835795cff80421dc0a788ee6e474dc0d89d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Statues of Dionysos, Orpheus, Zeus, and others"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e903a058e3d4cc351c4b67802b2acfec77120d98058226c1ca7582b382ed43ff> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
