    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e9cc55f458c397e6e6a9f1e67364c5a926254b8eded5caf1d7ab771111bd0c9e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "On the flat, a helmeted king holding a lion by the mane and brandishing a mace, with a naked man crawling away up a hill, a flying bird of prey, and a cartouche with irregular markings; on the convex, a beetle"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e9cd45441614834381c56b882f09918abe92bfcbbaecee89d7a2c11333441d54> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Brouskari 1974, 47, fig. 85</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e9d4d8089eb8fb3e448faa85579e601721f77b2e933c565f4c7094deb828530e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Side A</hi>: Silenos strides
      forward in right profile, hands bound behind back. Following him is a bearded hunter who looks
      back, head in left profile. The hunter wears boots, short chiton that has a black border at
      neckline and hem, and petasos hanging behind neck. His right hand holds two spears; his left
      hand hold the ends of the thongs that wrap Silenos's wrists. To the hunter's left is hunting
      dog.</P><P>A relief contour line runs throughout. Relief line is also used for the
      drapery detail, the top of boots, thongs. Hair is outlined in reserve. Dilute glaze is used
      for the inner details of the body, neck and sleeve of the chiton. Added purple appears on the
      petasos cord and the thongs of Silenos.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side
      B</hi>: bearded Midas stands three-quarters left, face in left profile. He wears a
      pleated chiton beneath himation and carries a staff in his upraised right hand. Some relief
      contours are used. Midas's hair and beard are outlined in reserve. Dilute glaze is used for
      inner details of the chiton.</P><P>Tongues are seen above each picture,
      terminating beneath the handles. There is a graffito on the
      shoulder.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e9e19b057467ee57037c1c6210f2e5ec2b05a8192346f98fd23a1883d1c6ce3d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> I, 193, 213; pl. 36.9" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e9e211e75820535f2dc261afb79601c8796b0d7a840d189b086c7222da0a1008> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl><hi rend=\"ital\">BMCRE</hi></bibl> V, 208, no. 279; <bibl>Milkovich 1961, no. 55</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e9f1d1eafe678a0ff9f4d5387d786efbc458361ddc4310ca0bb9ab848848c566> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A</hi>: two youths and a Nike.
      A Nike alights between two youths to announce a victory. She lands facing left, her wings
      pressed together and her feet tucked up behind her. She wears a chiton and sakkos and is
      enveloped in a large mantle which hides her arms. The youth on the left, whom she faces, is
      stooped over, leaning on his staff. He appears to be raising his right arm, perhaps in a
      gesture of greeting; his forearm is not preserved. He is wearing a mantle which falls to
      mid-calf. Another youth moves away on the right as if frightened, but turns his head to look
      back. He holds his forearms outward, although his hands are hidden under his heavy mantle.
      Both youths wear wreaths.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B</hi>: two
      youths and a Nike. A Nike has landed between two youths, facing left. Her wings are extended
      behind her and she is dressed in a chiton and mantle. The youth on the left faces her wrapped
      in a mantle and leaning on a staff. The youth on the right is identical in pose and dress to
      the right-hand figure on Side A.</P><P><hi rend="head">Interior</hi>:
      a youth adoring a herm. The youth stands left, facing the herm. He is hunched over slightly,
      leaning on his staff, and has extended his right arm toward the herm, palm outward. He wears a
      himation with his right shoulder left free and a vine wreath around his hair. The short,
      ithyphallic herm stands on a low base and is represented with very long hair, a long beard,
      sideburns and a mustache. His phallos is nearly one-third his height. Ribbons, rendered in
      dilute glaze, hang over its arm strut along with a wreath, now faded. Below the wreath is a
      kerykeion. There is an inscription written above his head, along the
      rim.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e9f513e508e70e182f04b8c95c6c09543109112dd21c6f40e17b077dc6c9e2d9> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
