<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f08f1490bda9f6fae5b9443bbe5d59ce4fa8932a857aff3b6745e93599f988b5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Lewes 1920</bibl>, no. 77" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f096cd4620a8f5089a07ef7311ca1bda4ed9baca2d0e66bdd84ca845c0b1e8f5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A Maenad is seated on a bull. She faces right, and looks back
      over her shoulder. She has long hair, bound with a diadem, and wears a necklace and
      embroidered sleeved chiton. She is playing crotala (castanets). In the field is a vine
      branch.</P><P>On the rim of the vessel is a checker pattern. On the neck are
      alternating palmette and lotus flowers, and below that, pomegranate
      buds.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f0b2c6780cffb550f30bb321d537886932d06f4db5992f135218ca6fffa224d7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Hermes and a Nymph dancing"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f0b9fb593f174a013e47086cfd65762c4c952a9fe591de318dce5fc284ba7a6e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Exterior: a nude youth squats to right before a white basin
      (louterion) into which water pours from a white spout at the upper right. He holds a cloak in
      his right hand and a yellow and red mirror in his left hand at which he gazes. He has
      earrings, a white necklace, a beaded bandolier, a thigh chain, anklets and boots. His hair is
      tied with a broad cloth band. Behind at left is a single ivy leaf.</P><P>There is
      a red fillet around the rim, tall tongues on the neck, a laurel wreath with yellow berries on
      the shoulder with a yellow rosette at center. Above the scene is an ovulo, and a large fan
      palmette on back, flanked by coiling tendrils. Under the handle are Paestan palmette
      fronds.</P><P>On semi-circular lid: a phlyax actor walks to left and looks back to
      right. He carries a crooked cane in his left arm, wears sandals, long sleeves and trousers
      tinted with brown glaze and a light tunic; a false phallos extends below his
      cloak.</P><P>On quadrate lid: the head of a youth to left with a red
      wreath.</P><P>On quadrate lid: head of a woman to right, in kekryphalos with
      radiate stephane, white necklace and earrings. On the underside of the lid, the same thing
      appears, without the kekryphalos. Figures are outlined in black, with only the background
      reserved.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f0cfc764777bb8c4be44f87820fc92b22d86cd5bedaab080d4a09fec00341a0e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "On the flat, silen astride a sphinx, seizing her by the hair; on the convex, a beetle"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f0f1c5914fd1799fdb2c928cb433d3e097830b3d5cf557d704de2ebb67dd8946> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A: An inscription, <Foreign
      lang=Greek>*A*R*X*W*N*K*A*L*L*I*M*H*D*H*S</Foreign>, along a black Ionic (?) column
      on a one-stepped base, topped with a white plinth, with broader black plinth above; on the
      plinth a female figure, standing 3/4-view to the right, with her weight on her left leg, and
      her head in profile to the right, raises her right hand, and cradles in her left arm a white
      keras from which emerges a small, white boy, Ploutos, with black hair, wearing a black
      himation (?); he reaches his right hand up towards the head of the female figure; in the
      center, an archaistic Athena Promachos, standing profile to the right; an inscription,
      <Foreign lang=Greek>*T*O*N*A*Q[*E]*N*E*Q*E*N*A*Q*L*O*N</Foreign>, along another
      black column supporting a statue, identical except that the boy is shown holding a smaller
      white keras, rather than emerging from it.</P><P>B: A bearded male figure,
      probably the referee, standing 3/4-view to the right, with his weight on his left leg, and his
      head turned profile to the right, wearing a white olive wreath, and a black diagonal himation
      draped over his left shoulder, arm, and hand (the latter resting on his left hip), holds a
      white grain stalk diagonally in his right hand, which hangs by his side; a white Nike with
      black wings, flying 3/4-view to the right, wearing a black chiton with a long kolpos, awarding
      a white garland to a nude pankratiast, with himantes (leather hand thongs), leaning 3/4-view
      to the right over another nude pankratiast, also with himantes, on the ground, 3/4-view to the
      left; a white female figure, perhaps Olympias, standing 3/4-view to the left, legs crossed,
      with her weight on her left leg, wearing a black himation draped over her left shoulder and
      obscuring her left hand, which she rests on her left hip, and a long pony-tail, leans on a
      short thick white column (?) with a flat base.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

