<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f1c50f0d169a0a186c0b4198691034fa48665bb9fd582c24a9b1ea5145548ac6> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>"Chariot" krater depicting two charioteers in cloaks, driving a
      two-horse chariot, and a pair of naked belt-wrestlers. The scene is repeated on the krater's B
      side. The chariot is decorated with a scale-pattern; the wheel is ovoid, and descending into a
      triple-banded ground line which encircles the vase. The horses' bodies are extremely
      elongated, and reins stretch across the exaggerated distance from the chariot to the horses'
      bridles. Flowers spring from the horses' backs and from the chariot's front, on one side; on
      the other, a series of rippled triangles descends from the pole-stay. The wrestlers' hands are
      drawn with opposed thumbs visible. The faces of the charioteers and the wrestlers are
      strangely rendered, with a reserved area containing a dot for the eye, and with a bent line
      extending from nose to shoulder. This line apparently represents the front of the neck, but is
      confusing, as it encloses a reserved area which contrasts greatly with the solid-glazed faces.
      Vermeule and Karageorghis suggest the line could represent a face protector. Under each of the
      handles, a long bird with a curved beak and semicircles for feet looks back over its
      shoulder.<P>This vase marks the first appearance of a pair of wrestlers joined together
      by a belt. In belt-wrestling, an Oriental sport that sporadically appears in the Levantine
      Aegean, the opponents are strapped together around the middle and attempt to pull each other
      off balance. Vermeule and Karageorghis observe that the wrestlers' gestures on this krater are
      similar to those of boxers. The neck and foot are glazed, with an additional band just above
      the foot, and the handles are outlined as well.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f1cb020dfe767a4461a804638049f194529f432c2c183b7d601161b32f64f02a> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>The black glaze has mostly fired brown. Some of the floral ornament has been
      repainted.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435429> .

