<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f2ef2d734149f34a23e2b824246b203b3a5cd7c45731cfe2fbe6ca7ab1242688> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "<bibl>Vermeule & Comstock 1988, 71 no. 75</bibl>" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f2f806dcafe32f68941de2f84b6fa836aac1661d51c10e2c2e036c4c8daae80e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="ital">Interior</hi>: An ephebe wearing an
      ivy wreath in added purple draws wine with an oinochoe from a krater decorated with an ivy
      garland. He holds a cup in his left hand. Added red is used to delineate tendons and muscles.
      The border is a meander.</P><P><hi rend="ital">Side A:</hi> Three male
      figures wearing himatia recline on striped cushions. The left figure holds the ends of his
      fillet in both hands (his sideburn is in added red); the middle one holds a skyphos in his
      left hand while holding his head with his right hand (his staff rests against the wall in the
      background), and the third with added red sideburn and fillet, plays the aulos; its spotted
      animal skin case with added red tie hangs on the wall.</P><P><hi
      rend="ital">Side B</hi>: Three male figures like those on side A all hold cups. The
      left one, with bearded frontal face wearing a dotted wreath in added purple, holds a skyphos
      to his lips, the middle one with fillet and sideburn in added purple holds a kylix up in his
      right hand, and the third wearing an added red wreath holds a skyphos. A basket with added red
      fillet hangs on the wall between the middle and right figures. Added red is used for
      musculature.</P><P>The artist is a late Archaic painter of cups related to the
      Antiphon Painter group, whose style is derivative of the "Panaitian" style of
      Onesimos.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

