<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f46be908283fa44e6dd7ebe0223d54c84ecdaf3affc7633644236c8cd9020362> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A</hi>: Dionysos in his
      chariot. Dionysos, crowned with ivy and carrying a drinking cup, is shown stepping into his
      chariot. Dionysos stands on the left, facing the four-horse chariot on the right. Dionysos'
      right foot is already in the chariot, while the toes of his left foot are still on the ground.
      He holds the reins with both hands, a kyathos in his left hand as well. Dionysos has long hair
      and a long beard with a red stripe. He wears a white chiton and a black mantle draped over
      both shoulders. A large ivy wreath crowns his head. Vines sprout from the kyathos and extend
      over and behind the horses on the right. The four horses overlap; all have red stripes on
      their fetlocks and tails.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B</hi>: Dionysos
      with satyr, maenad and a male figure. Dionysos and a maenad stand facing one another at the
      center of the scene, while a satyr and a man look on. Dionysos is shown in profile to the
      right, handing a vine-sprouting drinking cup to a maenad. He is wrapped in a mantle which
      hides his right arm, and wears a large wreath on his head. He has long hair and a long beard.
      The maenad tips her head down to look into the drinking cup as she reaches for it with her
      left hand. She has white skin and wears a chiton and himation. There is a red headband around
      her long hair. On the far left, a nude satyr stands facing Dionysos and the maenad, his right
      arm bent at chest level and his left arm at his side. He has pointed ears, long hair, and a
      beard; both hair and beard have been painted with red stripes. On the far right, a man moves
      away from the other figures, but looks back at them over his shoulder. He has long hair and a
      beard, both red-striped, and wears a short chiton, a short mantle draped over both shoulders,
      and a pointed cap with a turned-up brim. The vines sprouting from Dionysos' drinking cup
      extend above and behind the figures on both sides.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

