    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Gate building; in north wall of the Sanctuary of Poseidon."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f613aebd589f4938d290a9b27fd85dc496116b17788e394a8efc65606098903b> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """A: Nike and Phyle on either side of a bull<lb>B: A bearded man between two
      women"""@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f624920ac3483f05173f27673758a56016e24d00b1c04be8c61e09727355689e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A:</hi> Standing woman.
      Adorned with a v-shaped necklace, she stands, facing front, dressed in a long transparent
      Ionic style chiton with loose elbow sleeves and overhang (kolpos), broken up into many folds.
      Her hair is bunched up on either side of her head and gathered in a fillet. With her right
      hand she holds up a long tasseled fillet and grasps the same in her left hand. Her feet are
      shown in profile, pointing to the right where there is a basket full of wool or fillets,
      indicated in red.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B:</hi> Youth. Draped in
      a himation which comes up over the back of his head, he faces left. He stretches out his right
      hand to the basket on Side A, and holds a branch. With his left, he leans on a staff, the top
      of which is concealed in the folds of his garment. Since the alabastron is a funerary
      offering, perhaps the woman is bringing the fillets to decorate a tomb as on <rs
      type="vase">RISD 69.142.1</rs>. Fillets were a token of remembrance and were
      frequently shown tied to the tomb stele.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f6260ede5012b1739dc9e53544f3e9da806048a0637804d3211748faaa15d481> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Two gods or heroes shaking hands"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f628502fbedfef7dbe89ec1560ce2cfa1d2d6296cc3c06cdf63fd1cb8d8c59d2> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Bull, hound, goat and lion."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f62ec5eb8ffc451a2db52feb569e7e6cdb81fb1ba1acb9b364b8c8da03ef0ca5> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Lid: seated woman (bride?) wearing a himation and chiton looks
      into a mirror held in her left hand. Behind her is a single Doric column. In front of her at
      right, a woman spins with a spindle whorl in right hand and distaff in left hand, with a
      kalathos to right. Walking to the right and looking back to left a woman holds an open chest
      in her left arm from which hangs a fillet. With her right hand she plucks up her chiton on her
      shoulder. A woman standing to the left holds a sakkos in her right hand, and an exaleiptron
      (plemochoe) in her left. Another kalathos sits on the ground to right. To right, is a woman
      like the one holding the chest, except this chest is closed and a sakkos dangles. The scene
      may be a bride and her attendants or a generalized toilet scene. All the women wear peploi. On
      body is an ivy band. On the flanges of the lid and body is an ovulo
      pattern.</P><P>According to Beazley (<bibl>ARV2, 1396</bibl>) this is
      more or less closely related to the Painter of London E
      106.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f633b0ae234fe68048738d595cb55845de349258427389e3975f49e5b35a97a9> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
