<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f8d85d071bca06bf7901bf5d2632b8093382a870e89d03024efdfe37bd9cecca> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Bibliographic references"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<bibl>Shapiro 1993</bibl>, 76-77, 236 no. 25, figs. 28-29; I.
      Wehgartner, CVA Berlin, Antikenmuseum 8 (1991) 66-67, pls. 46, 48.4, ill. 22.3 (with previous
      bibliography); G. Krte, "Eichelfrmige Lekythos mit Goldschmuck aus Attika," <hi
      rend="ital">AZ</hi> 37 (1879) 93-96 pl. 10.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026497> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f8da7be48b46d65d4a6526198f3b396367b2baf8588451fbf7fed45c1a5da66d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>A: Okeanos (labelled to the right of his head) (missing lower
      face and upper left arm), standing profile to the right, with his left foot advanced, wearing
      a himation draped over his left arm (missing) and around his lower body, over a medium-sleeved
      chiton with a patterned hem, and a taenia (his hair in a krobylos), holds a scepter with
      palmette finial upright in his slightly raised left hand, and holds his right hand at waist
      level; Ge Panteleia (labelled to the right of her head) seated 3/4-view to the right on a
      decorated stool, with her feet on a footstool, wearing a himation draped over her left arm and
      around her lower body, over a medium-, button-sleeved chiton with an overfold, and a rayed
      stephane, holds a scepter with a palmette finial upright in her slightly raised left hand, and
      a phiale at waist level, in her right hand; bearded Dionysos (labelled retrograde diagonally
      from his right elbow), standing profile to the left, with his left foot slightly advanced,
      wearing a himation draped over his left arm and around his lower body, over a medium-,
      button-sleeved, patterned chiton with an overfold (?), and an ivy wreath, holds an ivy branch
      in his slightly lowered left hand, and branch with fugitive white leaves/flowers in his
      extended right hand; a small panther (leopard?) behind him, standing profile to the
      left.</P><P>B: Bearded King Balos (labelled above his scepter), seated profile to
      the right on a stool, wearing a himation draped over his left shoulder, his hair in a short
      pony tail, holds both bent arms at waist level, spreads the fingers of his right hand (to
      receive the phiale from Themis?), and a scepter diagonally in his left hand; Themis (labelled
      to right), standing near frontal, with her head profile to the left, wearing a medium-,
      button-sleeved chiton, a himation draped around her lower body and over her left shoulder, and
      a red taenia, holds a phiale to Balos, in her outstretched right hand, and a trefoil-lipped
      oinochoe to Epaphos in her slightly upraised left hand (her left arm is bent); bearded Epaphos
      (labelled retrograde to the left of his head; missing body between hips and neck, and both
      arms, except right hand), standing profile to left, his right foot advanced, wearing a
      himation over a chiton, and a white wreath (fugitive), also holds a scepter upright in his
      slightly upraised right hand.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/f8ea297db032d7e17f50c4975356d4fa306652be3c43d743015a60a492b86b8e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
