    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "The upper half of Zeus Philios or Zeus Meilichios, shown profile to the right"@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/fc0118f382317462a3b3cd31d96a489c30676ca74808c9b339c0a5bbdddb85c7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P>Sides A and B are virtually identical. The horses and horsemen
      stand side-by-side facing forward, their heads turned toward one another. The horsemen on Side
      A are young and unbearded. The youth on the right is crowned with a laurel wreath. His
      companion wears a simple red band over his hair, and his brow is furrowed. The preserved
      horseman on Side B is bearded and he wears a red fillet. Both men and youths wear
      short-sleeved tunics. The manes and tails of the horses are done in added red paint. They wear
      simple bridles.</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

