<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/feb907f1663b9fd7bb9b50946c743415c77cf12e8288e1e7c369a277bc31fdde> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Summary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Herakles (Side A) going to the fountain (Side B)."@en ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300080102> .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/febaea76a702aef5e8618a7669c0df75b56ab5a45a838ff01117e3d38b7e0c89> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Iconographic description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """<P><hi rend="head">Side A, shoulder:</hi> Herakles
      battles Nessos. Herakles pursues the centaur brandishing his sword in his right, his left fist
      extended forward. Nessos attempts to flee to the right, holding a white stone in his left.
      Deianeira slips from his back and runs towards Herakles with her arms raised. The hero wears a
      short white chiton, the lion's skin loosely pulled over his head. Deianeira wears a belted
      peplos, decorated with white dots along the seam, on top of a long garment with figurative
      central panel showing white sphinxes with extended wings. Nessos wears a white wreath; his
      chest is rendered in red.</P><P>The central group is flanked on the left by two
      centaurs. The first brandishes a huge white stone; he also wears a white wreath. His chest is
      depicted with a red beard and red chest, his hind legs are outlined in white. The second
      centaur holds a smaller stone ready to be hurled; only his chest is painted in red. They are
      complemented on the right by a group of three figures facing the central battle scene. The
      first is a woman dressed in a chiton and a red mantle, its seam decorated with white,
      partially missing dots. She is followed by an older man holding a staff. Slightly balding, his
      beard and hair is rendered in white; he wears a red mantle over a chiton and a red headband.
      The last figure is another woman dressed in a long garment painted red below the waist. She
      holds a wreath in each hand. The skin was painted in white; the color is now lost. From the
      left handle a lotus blossom grows on a long, curved stem. The background cover readable, but
      meaningless inscriptions.</P><P><hi rend="head">Side B, shoulder:</hi>
      Centauromachy in three groups. The central group consists of a centaur brandishing a tree
      trunk above his head, flanked by two attacking warriors. The centaur is turned to the left,
      his head facing backwards. His mouth is open and the bent right front leg indicates a first
      stumbling. He is rendered with a red beard and red chest, wearing a wreath with formerly white
      wreaths. The two warriors are shown in Chalcidian helmets with white crests, belted swords and
      round shields. The right shield is painted in red, the left was possibly white. The left
      warrior wears a red armor over a short chiton decorated with a grid pattern. Between his legs
      are two straps visible which could indicate a poorly executed skin. The right warrior wears a
      tight red garment longer than the previous with small sleeves and a wide seam. Two spirals
      with white dots on the chest possibly recall an armor. To the left of the central group a
      bearded warrior pursues a fleeing centaur. The warrior is nude, except for a Corinthian
      helmet, sword belt and shield, his spear raised in attack. The fleeing centaur is turned
      backwards and clasps a white (?) rock in both hands. His hair, beard, and outlines of muscles
      are rendered in red. To their right another centaur is pleading with his opponent. In the
      typical gesture of begging for mercy he places his fingertips onto the forehead and chin of
      the warrior who is pressing on to him with raised spear, his shield protectively held in front
      of him. The centaur's hair, beard and detailing of the body are red; the wreath in his hair
      was possibly white. The Attic helmet and round shield of his opponent was once white. He also
      wears a red armor and a chiton with incised decoration. All centaurs appear to be defeated. In
      the background, meaningless inscriptions.</P><P><hi rend="head">Upper Animal
      Frieze A:</hi> The distribution of the animals does
      not....</P>""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435430> .

